{
  "raw": {
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005955": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Administrative Assistant (26005955) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administrative Assistant (26005955) Job Description Administrative Assistant Dent Med-Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005955 ) Since 1896 the School of Dental Medicine has been educating students to take their places among the best dental practitioners in our region and across the country.  Each day the school's faculty and staff contribute to its mission to advance the future of dental medicine through teaching, research and service. In addition to being a great place to work the University offers robust benefits including: * 11 Paid Holidays, Paid Vacation, Sick and Personal Days *  Additional Paid Time off (Winter Recess) during the period between Christmas and the New Year  * Paid Parental Leave *  Educational benefits for eligible employees, their dependents and spouse/domestic partner * Above-average Employer Contribution towards Medical, Prescription Drug, Vision, Life, STD, and LTD Insurance plans * A robust retirement savings plan option.  Including 100% match on employee contributions of 3-8%(150% after vesting) and enhanced match for those nearing retirement * Free PRT bus pass. Job Summary Performs administrative assistant support work of moderate complexity. Essential Functions Oversee daily operations of Oral Surgery clinic activities, coordinate patient scheduling, and optimize staff productivity.  Direct daily operations of dental clinic staff and assist with training of new clinical and administrative staff as directed.  Assist with clinic workflow implementation and manage department coverage. Ensure adherence to healthcare laws, including OSHA safety guidelines and HIPAA patient privacy rules. Manage medical billing and coding procedures. Monitor and maintain inventory on medical/clinical and office supplies while maintaining facility equipment.  Notify appropriate contacts for ordering and service issues. Oversee patient relations and address patient clinical issues.  Help explain office policy to patients. Help support staff as needed (i.e., scheduling, collect payments, insurance, etc.) Monitor patient satisfaction. Assist coordination of meetings when needed. Help arrange for staff CE. Manage ExamSoft for clinical course needs of Clinical Course Directors. Assist predoctoral students with patient matters and academic matters. Physical Effort This position involves moderate physical activity, including frequent standing, walking, and occasional lifting. You will be required to stand and walk for extended periods, move between workstations, and lift and carry small to medium‑sized items (up to 20 lbs) occasionally. Tasks may also include pushing or pulling equipment, reaching at or below shoulder level, and repetitive hand and arm movements. No heavy lifting or prolonged strenuous exertion is required, but candidates must be able to perform these activities safely and consistently throughout the workday. Reasonable accommodations will be considered for qualified applicants, in line with accessibility standards. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Administrative Assistant II Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005135": {
      "title": "HERL Communications Specialist IV",
      "description": "Job Description - HERL Communications Specialist IV (26005135) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - HERL Communications Specialist IV (26005135) Job Description HERL Communications Specialist IV Med-Human Engineering Research Laboratories - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005135 ) The University of Pittsburgh / U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) Human Engineering Research Laboratories (HERL) is a collaborative venture advancing rehabilitation technology. HERL merges academic and VA expertise to enhance independence and quality of life for individuals with disabilities. Our mission is to innovate, design, and implement cutting-edge technologies, promoting mobility, accessibility, and improved healthcare for those with disabilities. Through interdisciplinary research, HERL strives to empower individuals and shape the future of assistive technology. As a University Institute with a broad portfolio of projects, HERL communicates to and with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders through multiple mediums. These multi-modal efforts include conducting outreach on assistive technology advances, providing ongoing project updates, publicizing the work of our academics and engineers, promoting participation in human subject research trials, and advocating for inclusionary design for people with disabilities. HERL is seeking to hire a full-time staff Communications Specialist IV. A bachelor’s degree is required, with a degree in Communications, Journalism, Public Relations, Marketing, Digital Media, English, or a related field strongly preferred. The ideal candidate will have at least three years of experience in one or more of these fields. The following skills and experience are strongly desired: Media relations, to include responding to inquiries, arranging interviews and site visits, and providing informational background materials. Professional photography and videography. Digital and physical production of newsletters, flyers, posters and related materials. Management of organizational social media accounts, including LinkedIn, Instagram, Facebook and YouTube. Experience maintaining and updating an organizational website. Special event coordination. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications including Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud applications such as Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Bridge, Premiere Pro, Audition and Acrobat. Submission of writing and/or media samples is not required but encouraged. Incumbent must successfully complete a U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs background check. Job Summary Develops complex web and print content and marketing. Acts as strategic contributor for communications team and creates marketing materials for marketing team. Participates in meetings designed for content planning and development. Ensures consistent messaging and maintains University brand and style. Essential Functions Serves as HERL’s primary contact for and liaison with all media and public relations entities. Designs, produces and publishes multimedia products, to include videos, still photography, podcasts and related materials. Identifies, tracks and fulfills all sponsored project communications requirements. Maintains the HERL website. Manages HERL social media accounts. Designs, edits and publishes HERL’s quarterly newsletter and annual calendar. Assists with coordination of HERL special events. Promotes opportunities for human subject trial participation in HERL research. Catalogs and curates the online publication of HERL academic research. Adheres to legal, regulatory and policy requirements required of the VA and University of Pittsburgh. Physical Effort Light. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. Work is largely performed in an office environment and requires the ability to operate standard office equipment and keyboards. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Communications Specialist IV Job Family Communications & Marketing Job Sub-Family Communications Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $63,000 to $67,000 annual Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Writing Sample, Media Sample Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006119": {
      "title": "Financial Analysis Manager",
      "description": "Job Description - Financial Analysis Manager (26006119) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Financial Analysis Manager (26006119) Job Description Financial Analysis Manager Office of Administration-Health Sciences - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006119 ) Position Summary: The Financial Analyis Manager serves as a key technical leader within the Financial Planning & Analysis team, driving the transformation of financial reporting, data analytics, and business processes across the organization. This role is responsible for developing automated reporting solutions, improving data integrity, optimizing financial processes, and leveraging modern reporting tools to enhance decision-making. The position partners closely with finance leadership, IT, and operational stakeholders to create scalable solutions that reduce manual effort, improve reporting accuracy, and establish best practices for financial analytics. Key Responsibilities: Reporting Transformation & Business Intelligence •         Lead the modernization of financial reporting through the development of automated dashboards, self-service reporting, and executive-level analytics. •         Design, develop, and maintain reporting solutions using tools such as Power BI, Excel, SQL, and other business intelligence platforms. •         Transform manual reporting processes into scalable, automated solutions that improve efficiency, accuracy, and accessibility. •         Develop standardized reporting packages, KPIs, and dashboards to support strategic and operational decision-making. Process Automation & Operational Excellence •         Identify opportunities to streamline financial processes through automation, workflow improvements, and technology solutions. •         Design and implement automated processes utilizing VBA, Power Query, SQL, Power Automate, and other automation tools. •         Reduce manual effort by eliminating repetitive tasks and improving process consistency across the finance organization. •         Lead continuous improvement initiatives focused on increasing efficiency, strengthening internal controls, and enhancing data quality. Data Management & Analytics •         Develop, maintain, and optimize financial data models to support budgeting, forecasting, and reporting activities. •         Write and optimize SQL queries, data transformations, and data validation processes to ensure accurate and reliable financial information. •         Collaborate with IT and data management teams to improve data governance, integration, and accessibility. •         Perform complex financial and operational analyses to identify trends, risks, and opportunities. Technical Leadership & Collaboration •         Serve as the team's subject matter expert for reporting technologies, automation tools, and financial data architecture. •         Partner with finance leadership and business stakeholders to understand reporting needs and develop innovative analytical solutions. •         Mentor financial analysts on reporting best practices, automation techniques, and data analysis methodologies. •         Promote the adoption of standardized reporting tools, templates, and documentation across the finance organization. Governance & Documentation •         Develop and maintain documentation for reporting solutions, automated processes, and data models. •         Establish reporting standards and best practices to ensure consistency, accuracy, and sustainability. •         Ensure compliance with organizational policies related to financial reporting, data governance, and internal controls. Innovation & Continuous Improvement •         Evaluate emerging technologies and analytical tools that can enhance the finance function. •         Lead initiatives to modernize financial systems, reporting capabilities, and business processes. •         Recommend and implement innovative solutions that improve financial planning, forecasting, reporting, and decision support. •         Foster a culture of continuous improvement by identifying opportunities to leverage technology and analytics to drive organizational performance. Job Summary Lead efforts to create multi-year plans and utilize university planning and modeling tools to support sound financial decision-making at the University. Essential Functions Reporting Transformation & Business Intelligence. Process Automation & Operational Excellence. Technical Leadership & Collaboration. Governance & Documentation. Innovation & Continuous Improvement. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Financial Analysis Manager Job Family Finance & Procurement Job Sub-Family Financial Planning & Analysis Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $78,501 to $111,209 annual Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006109": {
      "title": "Senior QC Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior QC Specialist - Laboratory Manager II (26006109) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior QC Specialist - Laboratory Manager II (26006109) Job Description Senior QC Specialist - Laboratory Manager II Health Sciences Core Research Facilities - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006109 ) Perform cell-based procedures that support product development, characterization, and release testing. Activities may include thawing and handling of primary human cells and cell therapy products, cell culture and expansion, cell selection and enrichment, activation, transduction, transfection, sample preparation, flow cytometry-based characterization, and functional assays.  Participate in or lead analytical method qualification and validation activities. Develop study protocols, establish appropriate assay performance criteria, execute studies, analyze results, and prepare qualification or validation reports. Depending on the intended use of the assay, studies may include evaluation of accuracy, precision, specificity, sensitivity, linearity, range, robustness, system suitability, limits of detection or quantitation, and appropriate controls and reference materials.  Support implementation and lifecycle management of analytical procedures in a regulated environment. Review analytical data for completeness, accuracy, traceability, and compliance with approved procedures, specifications, and acceptance criteria.  Participate actively in the IMCPL Quality Management System. Responsibilities will include support for deviations, laboratory investigations, out-of-specification and out-of-trend results, corrective and preventive actions, change control, risk assessments, document control, equipment-related investigations, and continuous improvement activities.  Author, review, and revise controlled documentation including Standard Operating Procedures, analytical methods, test procedures, batch records, worksheets, specifications, qualification and validation protocols, validation reports, technical reports, investigation reports, and training materials. Documentation must be clear, scientifically accurate, reproducible, and appropriate for a regulated cell and gene therapy environment.  Train laboratory personnel in analytical procedures. Participate in analyst competency and proficiency programs, support qualification of staff for independent assay execution, and help maintain consistent analytical performance across the laboratory. Collaborate with Manufacturing, Quality Assurance, investigators, and product development teams to support analytical strategy, product characterization, specification development, manufacturing changes, comparability assessments, and regulatory activities. The Senior QC Specialist may contribute technical and analytical information used in CMC documentation and regulatory submissions. Support technology transfer of analytical methods into IMCPL and assist with implementation of new analytical platforms, instrumentation, and laboratory capabilities. Participate in inspections, audits, laboratory readiness Job Summary Manages day-to-day laboratory operations while ensuring compliance with safety regulations and best practices. Works with, adapts, and installs scientific equipment in research laboratories. Develops and collaborates on routine projects and procedures. Manages inventory and equipment and performs budget functions. Essential Functions The Senior QC Specialist will support the development, qualification, validation, execution, and lifecycle management of analytical procedures used for the characterization and release of cell and gene therapy products at the Immunologic Monitoring and Cellular Products Laboratory (IMCPL). The position requires a strong foundation in molecular biology and hands-on experience with analytical and cell-based methods used to assess product safety, identity, purity, impurities, potency, biological activity, and other relevant quality attributes.  This is a hands-on laboratory role that combines routine and non-routine QC testing with analytical development, troubleshooting, documentation, investigation, training, and quality-system responsibilities. The successful candidate will work closely with Quality Control, Quality Assurance, Manufacturing, and product development teams and will be expected to understand the relationship between assay performance, manufacturing processes, product quality, and clinical release. Develop, optimize, qualify, validate, execute, and maintain analytical procedures supporting cell and gene therapy products. Assays may include molecular, cellular, biochemical, and functional methods used to evaluate safety, identity, purity, process- and product-related impurities, potency, biological activity, gene or transgene expression, vector- or genome-related attributes, residual materials, stability, and product comparability. Perform molecular biology assays including PCR, qPCR, DNA- and RNA-based analyses, gene-expression assays, and related analytical procedures. Troubleshoot assay performance, investigate atypical results, identify sources of analytical variability, and implement appropriate corrective strategies. Physical Effort Sitting and standing for long periods at the bench.  Reading small print on tubes, vials and other things.  Walking around campus and between labs and walking to attend meetings when necessary.  Bending and lifting up to 30 pounds.  Bending and lifting to put away lab supplies.  Working under standard laboratory and office lighting. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Manager II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification NA Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., schedule as set with supervisor Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006132": {
      "title": "Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Director - Finance & Operations  (26006132) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director - Finance & Operations  (26006132) Job Description Director - Finance & Operations Office of Administration-Health Sciences - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006132 ) The Director - Finance & Operations will lead financial strategy, budgeting, and planning across the Schools of Health Sciences, while serving as a key leader in driving transformative change across the finance organization. This role will lead the team in reimagining how financial processes, reporting, and decision-making are delivered - streamlining operations, eliminating manual work, and leveraging innovative technology and Power BI to create modern, data-driven tools and insights. The ideal candidate will be a strategic, forward-thinking leader who can inspire teams, challenge traditional approaches, and build scalable solutions that fundamentally improve how finance supports the organization. Job Summary Directs the budgeting process and oversees the analysis and review of financial information. Leads team and establishes the direction, goals, and implementation strategy of the department. Formulates, implements, and ensures compliance with policies, procedures, and regulations. Collaborates with key stakeholders and evaluates success of department. Essential Functions Ability to work autonomously with minimal supervision. Ability to exercise discretion and independent judgement in significant matters. Ability to set policies, anticipate trends, and possess a high level of problem solving skills. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Director - Finance & Operations Job Family Business Operations & Administration Job Sub-Family Operational Leadership Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $86,351 - $122,330 annual Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006128": {
      "title": "Industrial Engineer",
      "description": "Job Description - Industrial Engineer (26006128) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Industrial Engineer (26006128) Job Description Industrial Engineer Facilities Management AVC - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006128 ) •    Analyzes and evaluates operational processes, workflows, and systems; identifies inefficiencies and areas for improvement; develops and implements solutions to optimize performance and reduce costs in the most economical and effective manner. •    Applies industrial engineering practices including process mapping, time-and-motion studies, statistical analysis, and simulation modeling; collects and interprets operational data to support evidence-based decision making. •    Oversees comprehensive annual facility condition assessment program and manages all associated data to identify, plan, and prioritize short-and long-term facility preservation and renewal investments. •    Works closely with University stakeholders to ensure collaborative planning, prioritization and coordination of annual capital preservation needs. •    Serves as a key strategist for Facilities Management (FM) senior leadership to identify, prioritize, and lead initiatives to optimize performance and ensure responsible resource allocation. Collaborates closely with FM finance team to help define options for budget reallocations or reductions. Coordinates with stakeholders to determine project needs, scope, budgets, and timelines;establishes performance criteria and generates cost estimates; communicates findings and recommendations clearly to all levels of the organization. Continued below •    Leverages disparate data sources and digital tools to inform decisions related to resource optimization, process improvement, service quality and customer satisfaction. •    Maintains proficiency with data analysis and visualization tools, and explores and utilizes new technologies as they become available •    Manages assigned projects from initiation through completion; coordinates with FM operations, maintenance and engineering staff, Planning, Design and Construction professionals, contractors, IT professionals and other related stakeholders; ensures project compliance with established goals, budget, schedule, and University standards. •    Develops, plans, and monitors project budgets; determines fiscal requirements for process improvement initiatives; identifies risks and mitigation strategies. •    Assists in the development and maintenance of operational standards and guidelines to support future planning, design, and continuous improvement efforts across facility operations. •    Prepares reports and analyses to document findings, progress, trends, and recommendations. •    Clearly and effectively presents project objectives, analysis findings, and recommendations to stakeholders and departmental/university leadership. •    Works with FM leadership to establish a defined set of performance metrics and develops means and methods to track and report data over time; helps to identify corrective actions to improve performance and reverse unfavorable trends. •    Supervises staff, including hiring, performance reviews, and documenting disciplinary actions and other human resource administration; manages work schedules and approves timecards; provides professional development opportunities; distributes and reviews work. Job Summary Analyzes and improves operational processes, systems, and workflows to enhance efficiency, reduce costs, and optimize resource utilization across University facilities and campus operations. Applies industrial engineering and data analytics to evaluate existing operational processes and systems and develop solutions for improvement. Coordinates with stakeholders to identify needs and establish performance metrics. Oversees annual comprehensive facility condition assessment program and analyses all associated data to identify, plan, and prioritize short-and long-term preservation and renewal investments. Works closely with University stakeholders to ensure collaborative planning, prioritization and coordination of annual capital preservation needs. Manages project timelines, budgets, and compliance with University standards and best practices. Essential Functions Please see Posting Details Physical Effort Minimal lifting. Standing, walking, sitting as required per need. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Manager - Industrial Engineering Job Family Campus Operations Job Sub-Family Facilities Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday through Friday 8am to 4:30pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005871": {
      "title": "Nighttime Information Desk Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Nighttime Information Desk Coordinator (26005871) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Nighttime Information Desk Coordinator (26005871) Job Description Nighttime Information Desk Coordinator Research & Learning - Pennsylvania-Johnstown - ( 26005871 ) Owen Library is the University of Pittsburgh at Johnstown's library. It is part of the University of Pittsburgh's Library System.  This position has three primary responsibilities: coordinating Information Desk activities, managing student assistants, and recording Owen Library statistics. Additional responsibilities include: Work with the Pitt-Johnstown campus Facilities Department to maintain the library facility. Assist library colleagues with projects. Manage library displays. Work with the University Library System Communications & Technology staff and the Pitt-Johnstown campus Information Technology staff to provide tech support for the library’s networks and equipment (including computers and printers). This position coordinates the Owen Library Information Desk activities from 4:00 PM to 10:30 PM Monday through Thursday, and 2:00 PM to 10:30 PM on Sundays. The work hours for this position are generally Sunday through Thursday, 2:00 PM to 10:30 PM. These are subject to change as department needs arise, with advance notice. There are occasional work hours on University holidays as required. The tasks and responsibilities for the ULS Nighttime Information Desk Coordinator must be performed on-site and in person; this position is not eligible for a flexible work arrangement or remote work. Job Summary Assists personnel, answers inquiries, locates materials, and provides guidance related to library services. Researches and identifies resources to support informational needs. Maintains and updates online library systems and guides student employees. Essential Functions This position's essential functions include: Working at the library’s Information Desk. Working with Information Desk resources (including books and laptop computers). Communicating effectively with work-study students. Working with the University Library System IT Department and the Pitt-Johnstown IT department to resolve network ad equipment issues. Working with the Pitt-Johnstown Facilities Department to resolve issues with the library facility. Working with Owen Library’s statistics spreadsheets. Working with Owen Library’s calendar databases. Physical Effort This position is mostly sedentary. It does require the ability to move boxes of books and carry one ream of paper. The library has equipment and other team members available to help move heavy items. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Library Public Service Specialist Job Family Library Job Sub-Family Library Operations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule The work hours for this position are generally Sunday through Thursday, 2:00 PM to 10:30 PM. These are subject to change as department needs arise, with advance notice. There are occasional work hours on University holidays as required. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $16.50 to $20.63 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006052": {
      "title": "Director, IT Infrastructure & Operations",
      "description": "Job Description - Director, IT Infrastructure & Operations (26006052) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director, IT Infrastructure & Operations (26006052) Job Description Director, IT Infrastructure & Operations Pitt IT Operations - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006052 ) Pitt Digital is seeking a Director, IT Infrastructure & Operations to lead combined network & systems operations organization responsible for infrastructure the University runs on — PittNet wired, wireless, & telecom; network architecture, engineering, & security enforcement; data center services; server virtualization platforms; enterprise storage; backup & recovery; patching & platform lifecycle; identity svcs; endpoint mgmt; disaster recovery svcs; cloud infrastructure; 24x7x365 monitoring operations. The organization supports Oakland & Regional Campuses delivering infrastructure & IT operational services to Univ schools, depts, health sciences units, & research centers that support delivery of academic, research, & administrative services. You will lead three Assistant Directors & their functional groups: Asst Director, Network Operations: network architecture, engineering, installation, configuration, & optimization; LAN/WAN, wireless, & VoIP operations; firewalls, load balancing, DNS, & network security enforcement; network capacity planning & effectiveness analysis; & telecom. Asst Director, IT Operations: systems engineering for compute & data (server hosting, VMware, storage, backups, cloud, web hosting); Monitoring Operations, a 24x7x365 monitoring & Tier 1 security operations. Asst Director, Service Delivery: On-premise field & cable plant operations. Required qualifications - Seven yrs progressively responsible experience IT infrastructure operations; demonstrated prior experience leading a large IT operations organization, including accountability for multi-service production portfolio & a staff of comparable size & complexity; demonstrated technical depth in both network operations & server or systems ops, with credibility to direct senior engineers in each; experience with formal change management & incident management processes in a production environment, including major incident command; experience owning a service budget and vendor relationships, including capacity and lifecycle planning. Applicants must include complete employment history on application and attach a current resume specifically to this requisition #.  Include salary requirements in cover letter. The University offers a robust retirement savings plan with 100% employer match, 150% after vesting.  11 Paid Holidays.  Paid Vac, Sick,  Personal.  Add'l Winter Recess Paid Time Off.  Paid Parental Leave.   Above-average Employer Contribution toward Medical, Prescription Drug, Dental, Vision, Life, and more.  Education benefits for staff, spouses/partners, dependents.  Student loan assistance.  Free transit pass. Aug 2026 - Forbes listed Pitt among the 100 best employers in the commonwealth, ranking third among higher education institutions.  This is the 6th year Pitt has been on Forbes' America's Best-in-State Employers list for PA. Join the team responsible for strategy, implementation, and maintenance of technology at the University of Pittsburgh—ranked by Forbes among Amazon, CDW, Cisco Systems, Google, LinkedIn, and Microsoft as one of “America’s Best Large Employers.” Job Summary Oversees all facets of University network operations relating to architecture, engineering, storage, security, development, and maintenance. Establishes and ensures compliance with procedures and protocols. Directs evaluations of network effectiveness and oversees forecasting and completion of capacity planning. Essential Functions Must have the ability to work with PC equipment and related hardware/software and telephony video-conferencing systems. Must have good written and verbal communication skills, as well as, analytical, organizational, planning, and strong leadership skills.  Must have a proficient knowledge of IT. Physical Effort Generally sedentary desk work with computer-keyboard-video phone other than traveling to other buildings on campus for meetings/events on occasion.  Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Director - Information Technology Network Operations Job Family Information Technology Job Sub-Family Network & Telecommunication Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F bus hrs EST.  On occasion, some evening and weekend work may be necessary depending on business load, project timeline requirements, urgent support, or scheduled downtime changes.  Responsible for manning an escalation/on-call phone number. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered Yes Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006077": {
      "title": "CSB Financial Administrator",
      "description": "Job Description - CSB Financial Administrator  (26006077) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - CSB Financial Administrator  (26006077) Job Description CSB Financial Administrator Med-Computational and Systems Biology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006077 ) Job Summary Performs pre- and post-award accounting duties for small grants and contracts. Prepares, negotiates, and monitors grants and contracts. Assists with maintaining award-related schedules, preparing government applications and reports, and policy and procedure interpretation. Monitors account activity and prepares routine financial documents. Essential Functions This position provides support for pre- and post-award grant administration and department accounts, including monitoring account activity, preparing routine financial documents, account reconciliation, purchasing and reimbursement, and related fiscal and office duties. The incumbent should have a background in accounting or finance. Experience in pre and post award grant administration is preferred. The incumbent will also collaborate with the administrative team in the Department of Computational and Systems Biology on strategic projects, daily and long-term operational tasks, and other duties as assigned by the supervisor. The ideal candidate is proficient in SharePoint, OneDrive, Excel, other core Microsoft Office applications, and Adobe Acrobat. Familiarity with Pitt systems such as MyFunding, Concur, Tableau, PantherExpress, and PRISM is preferred but not required. A hybrid work schedule is available; the specific schedule is to be agreed with the department administration. Physical Effort Minimal physical effort associated with this position. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Grants & Contracts Specialist I (Pre & Post-Award) Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Grants & Contracts Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $21.00 to $26.00 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
