    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005943": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Nurse",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse (26005943) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse (26005943) Job Description Clinical Research Nurse Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005943 ) This position is for the Division of Genetic and Genomic Medicine within the Department of Pediatrics.  Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Supports clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews lab results, patient data, and lab specimens; administers medications and protocol-specific treatments. Performs general laboratory duties and specialized nursing duties, trains new staff, and ensures regulatory adherence. Essential Functions • Coordinates clinical research projects and drug trials. Assesses patients for qualification/enrollment in research projects and subject groups. Implements research protocols. Monitors patient assessments. • Collects and reviews lab results; monitors results for adverse reactions. • Collects patient data, including medical histories and physical assessments. Maintains and enters data into databases/logs in a timely and accurate manner. • Performs general laboratory duties including, but not limited to, monitors supply inventory, monitors temperatures of freezers and refrigerators, cleans equipment, and disposes of biological waste. Performs specialized nursing duties such as arterial puncture, venipuncture, and operation of electronic monitoring equipment; assists with surgical and/or invasive procedures. • Administers treatment and/or medication in accordance with research protocol. • Collects, prepares, and processes lab specimens. • Ensures all protocol and regulatory standards adherence. • Participates in the development of internal review board submissions as requested. • Collaborates with multiple investigators, sponsors, and research coordinators. • Assists with training of new staff and ongoing guidance of newer staff. Physical Effort Medium. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Nurse II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research - Nursing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor of Science in Nursing Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification RN Work Schedule Regarding flexibility with shift/hours and working on evenings and weekends: Potentially, on special occasions, but with notice; most of the time, this will be a standard M-F daylight position. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005966": {
      "title": "Project Manager I",
      "description": "Job Description - Project Manager I (26005966) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Manager I (26005966) Job Description Project Manager I Med-Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005966 ) The Department of Surgery is a major academic surgical department supporting foundational educational activities for medical students, residents, and fellows in conjunction with its extensive research and clinical portfolio. The Preclinical and Clerkship Medical Student Coordinator will provide critical support for the educational mission of the department, helping to integrate medical student activities into the function of the department and serving as a key liaison between students and teaching faculty and residents. Job Summary Oversees all aspects of planning, design, and execution of assigned small, routine projects and coordinates with project stakeholders to define project scope, goals, and deliverables. Assists in timeline development, ensures adherence to timeframes, and adjusts project deliverables to avoid issues. Performs budgetary functions and administrative tasks. Assists with external consultant and vendor selection, negotiation, and management. Essential Functions Responsibilities will include maintenance of the MS3 Core Surgical Clerkship Elentra Site including Launch Week, Wednesday morning Didactic sessions, Wrap-Up week activities, and coordination tools for medical student activities while on clerkship. Collecting and collating student preferences for specific site assignments. Ensuring appropriate onboarding of students at their individual rotation sites, including scrub machine access, badge access, parking access (if applicable), locker access, and call room access (if applicable). Following and enforcing guidelines for placement of students (ensuring that faculty on rotations have the capacity to place students at rotation sites). Fielding student requests, concerns, and questions regarding the surgery clerkship and directing them to appropriate answers or faculty. Managing grade evaluations and ensuring timely reporting of student grades. Working collaboratively with other clerkship coordinators to provide cross coverage in times of need and standardize practices across the school of medicine. Proctoring of the NBME subject exam (once per rotation). Attending all meetings for clerkship faculty and participating in continuous quality improvement for the clerkship. Administration of Foundations (Preclinical) Medical Student Activities in Department of Surgery. Coordinating with Interest group student leaders and faculty. Arranging space for meeting and coordination of supplies, guests, and educational opportunities. Coordinate, along with Flex week course directors and primary student leaders, room assignments, faculty, and activities for flex week offerings for students interested in participating in general surgery flex week experiences. Work alongside Clerkship Director and Clerkship faculty team to develop, test, and collect data regarding new curricular innovations and implementation for the MS3 Core Clerkship, Flex Week experiences for MS1/MS2, and other activities. Physical Effort Must be able to sit and stand to perform desk-based administrative duties for extended periods of time. Will be required to assist in the transport of materials via wheel cart to and from Scaife Hall for suture sessions and other didactics, not to exceed 30 lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Project Manager I Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Program & Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification A degree or formal training in education, educational sciences, higher education, health professions education, or a related discipline is preferred. Prior administrative or program coordination experience is also preferred, particularly within higher education, academic medicine, healthcare, or another complex educational environment. Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:00 am - 4:30 pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006018": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator II",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator II (26006018) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator II (26006018) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator II Med-Neurological Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006018 ) Job Summary Conducts research assessments on study participants. Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Assists with training staff. Ensures adherence to protocols and corrects issues with data collection. Essential Functions The University of Pittsburgh, Department of Neurological Surgery, is hiring a Clinical Research Coordinator II at the Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh. The research will focus on clinical outcomes in pediatric patients with congenital neurosurgical disorders such as hydrocephalus, spina bifida, tethered cord and Chiari malformation. Conducts research assessments on study participants. Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Assists with training staff. Ensures adherence to protocols and corrects issues with data collection. Conducts research assessments on study participants. Assists with and adheres to study protocols, and Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Assists with training staff on proper and best study research techniques as directed. Mentors and educates staff and student workers as directed. Ensures proper protocols are followed and quality assurance of research and related work. Corrects data collection issues. The job duties outlined in this job description include common job responsibilities for this title and level of jobs and are not intended to cover every duty. The University reserves the right to assign other duties to employees that are not listed in this job description. Minimum education to be considered for this position is a bachelor's degree in a related field. Interested candidates, please go to Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh and use requisition #26006018 to apply for this position. The University of Pittsburgh is an Affirmative Action/ Equal Opportunity Employer and values equality of opportunity, human dignity, and diversity, EOE, including disability/vets. Physical Effort Must be able to walk, stand, or sit for long periods of time. Must be able to use computer, telephone, copier, fax, and other essential office equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F 8:30am-5pm Occasional Mornings, Evening and Weekends as needed Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005894": {
      "title": "Project Manager IV",
      "description": "Job Description - Project Manager IV (26005894) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Manager IV (26005894) Job Description Project Manager IV Med-Trivedi Institute - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005894 ) The University is partnering with Systems One / Joulé to assist in the recruitment of this position. If interested in this opportunity and to be considered, please apply through this link: Project Manager IV - Apply Today Oversees all aspects of planning, design, and execution of simultaneous complex and diverse projects. Assists in developing timelines and ensures adherence to deadlines. Manages financial aspects of projects and other administrative duties. Handles external correspondence and drafts reports and other communications. • Conducts administrative tasks, leads meetings, and drafts communications. Specifically triaging the institute director's inbox. • Oversees all aspects of planning, design, and execution of assigned simultaneous, large, diverse, and complex projects. Coordinates with project stakeholders to define project scope, goals, and deliverables. • Assists in developing a timeline and ensures adherence to all deadlines. Anticipates potential problems and adjusts project deliverables as needed. • Drafts and manages the project budget, ensures timely submission of vendor payment requests, manages expense reimbursements, and purchasing. • Tracks project progress and maintains accurate records and files; provides detailed reports to senior management. • Assists with selection, negotiation, and management of activities regarding external consults or vendors. Job Summary Oversees all aspects of planning, design, and execution of simultaneous complex and diverse projects. Assists in developing timelines and ensures adherence to deadlines. Manages financial aspects of projects and other administrative duties. Handles external correspondence and drafts reports and other communications. Essential Functions Ability to complete tasks autonomously with minimal supervision. Ability to exercise discretion and independent judgement in significant matters. Advanced problem solving skills required. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Project Manager IV Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Program & Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 6 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $78,501-$117,750.50 annually Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided Yes Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006098": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator I",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator I (26006098) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator I (26006098) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator I Med-Cardiovascular Institute - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006098 ) Under the direction of Dr. Malamo Countouris, the Clinical Research Coordinator I will work in the lab based out of the Magee Research Institute.  This lab incorporates a multidisciplinary, versatile team to study cardiac disease in pregnancy and postpartum. Specifically, the lab focuses on investigating the cardiovascular sequelae of hypertensive disorders of pregnancy and opportunities for cardiovascular risk factor modification and cardiovascular disease prevention in this high-risk population. The applicant will be able to work a hybrid schedule by allowing two half days to work remotely in Pittsburgh area. The remainder of the full-time position must be work on sites including but not limited to Magee Women's Hospital, Magee Women's Research Institute, Presbyterian Hospital, as well as conducting home visits. Main Duties include but are not limited to: Assisting with conducting clinical research studies including clinical trials Recruiting and consenting study participants Running study visits and collecting data Managing IRB applications and databases Working with a dynamic team that partners with women of diverse backgrounds to understand their health and risk for disease. Job Summary Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Recruits research subjects and conducts interviews and research assessments. Essential Functions The successful applicant is required to have extremely strong communication skills, pay close attention to detail, strong organizational skills, and time management. Physical Effort Must be able to move easily between university, offices, hospitals and clinics and locations where patient enrollment is taking place including possible home visits. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule mon-friday standard Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006073": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26006073) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26006073) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator Med-Cardiovascular Institute - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006073 ) The Department of Medicine seeks a Clinical Research Coordinator I to participate in an innovative program in cardiovascular disease research and clinical trials supported by the NIH and foundations. The individual will collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to implement clinical trial protocols. Primary duties will entail that the Clinical Research Coordinator screens potential research participants; recruits participants; conducts informed consent; engages in administration of study procedures either in person or remotely; and enters relevant data into web-based interfaces for data entry and capture. This member of the study team will travel to multiple clinics in the Pittsburgh, PA, region, and interface with clinical and research staff. Specific responsibilities are: 1. Have a comprehensive understanding of research objectives and prescreen research study participants accurately and consistently by applying inclusion and exclusion criteria. 2. Conduct procedures according to standardized protocols. Activities include discussing research aims and activities with community members and potential participants, conduct of informed consent, and administration of study-related measures and assessments. 3. Engage with partner collaborative sites with professionalism. 4. Participate in community engagement and collaborative activities. Duties may include attending health fairs for recruitment or assisting in presenting the research to community members. 5. Serve as a member of a collaborative, multidisciplinary team and contribute to fostering a culture of integrity. 6. Maintain rigorous attention to clinical trial implementation, including accurate and comprehensive data entry and operational procedures. 7. Participate in communication with multiple internal and external partners and research program collaborators under the supervision of team lead ership. Job Summary Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Recruits research subjects and conducts interviews and research assessments. Essential Functions The successful Clinical Research Coordinator will demonstrate a high level of engagement, focus on adherence to protocols and integrity of research methods, and have excellent communication skills to interact with research participants, collaborating investigators, administrative staff, and staff and health care providers at clinical sites. The candidate will have a commitment towards community engagement and advancement of cardiovascular disease prevention with lifestyle and behavioral interventions. Professionalism is a requirement, as is the capacity to work independently at community sites for specified durations. Physical Effort Must be able to move between university offices and multiple clinical sites in the Pittsburgh area.  May require periods of walking and standing. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule mon-friday standard Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006074": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician II",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Technician II (26006074) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Technician II (26006074) Job Description Laboratory Technician II Med-OB-Gyn & Reproductive Science - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006074 ) Magee Womens Research Institute (MWRI) is the largest research institute in the US dedicated to women's health and reproductive biology.  Prior experience working in a research environment is preferred.  Degree in a science field is preferred. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions Performs a variety of laboratory experiments such as histology, flow cytometry, molecular techniques, gene sequencing, and related technical functions, testing, troubleshooting, and analysis, and may perform microsurgical procedures. Ensures conformity to specifications. Identifies and prepares specimens. Oversees supply management: ordering, procurement, tracking estimates, and receiving items. Operates and maintains applicable laboratory equipment for job functions. Keeps detailed, accurate, and timely data and log books. Organizes and documents results. Maintains, calibrates, cleans, and tests sterility of laboratory equipment. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006060": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Nurse II",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse II - Neuroimaging Research Program (26006060) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse II - Neuroimaging Research Program (26006060) Job Description Clinical Research Nurse II - Neuroimaging Research Program Med-Radiology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006060 ) Supports positron emission tomography (PET) neuroimaging research studies in alcohol and cocaine use disorder by recruiting participants through community treatment partners, assessing participant eligibility, and implementing imaging protocols. Places intravenous lines and manages arterial catheters. Administers pharmacologic challenge agents and protocol-specified medications under the supervision of the Principal Investigator (PI). Performs arterial blood sampling during PET acquisitions and pre-processes blood specimens for analyses. Assesses participants for substance withdrawal prior to brain imaging and monitors for relapse and psychiatric symptom exacerbation, including suicidal ideation, throughout study participation. Monitors participants for adverse events, maintains regulatory documentation, trains new staff, and ensures protocol and regulatory adherence. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in clinical research, neuroimaging, or a critical care/procedural setting Experience with arterial line management, removal, and arterial blood sampling BLS certification Clinical experience in addiction medicine, behavioral health, or medically managed withdrawal, including use of standardized withdrawal assessment tools Training or experience in suicide risk assessment and crisis response Familiarity with IRB submission processes and electronic data capture systems Experience working with participants with substance use or other psychiatric disorders Job Summary Supports clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews lab results, patient data, and lab specimens; administers medications and protocol-specific treatments. Performs general laboratory duties and specialized nursing duties, trains new staff, and ensures regulatory adherence. Essential Functions Builds and maintains recruitment relationships with community and health system referral partners, including addiction medicine clinics, emergency rooms, inpatient and residential rehabilitation programs, medically managed withdrawal (detoxification) units, intensive outpatient and partial hospitalization programs, alcohol treatment programs, and recovery support organizations. Presents study information to clinical staff and prospective participants, coordinates referral workflows, tracks referral sources and recruitment yield, and represents the research program at community outreach activities. Coordinates clinical PET neuroimaging research studies. Recruits, screens, and assesses adult participants for eligibility and enrollment by administering diagnostic and clinical assessments, including participants with alcohol use disorder and cocaine use disorder and healthy comparison participants. Assists with obtaining informed consent under the direction of the Principal Investigator. Implements study protocols and monitors participant assessments across screening, MRI, and PET scan-day, and follow-up visits. Assesses participants for signs and symptoms of alcohol and cocaine withdrawal prior to MRI and PET imaging visits, using protocol-specified instruments and clinical judgment. Administers and scores withdrawal assessments (e.g., CIWA-Ar for alcohol), documents vital sign trends, tremor, autonomic instability, sleep and appetite disturbance, agitation, and craving, and verifies abstinence interval requirements through self-report, breath alcohol testing, and urine toxicology. Determines in consultation with the Principal Investigator or study physician whether a participant meets protocol criteria to proceed, requires rescheduling, or requires referral for clinical evaluation and management of withdrawal. Performs specialized nursing duties including radial arterial catheter and line maintenance, flushing, and removal, venipuncture, peripheral IV placement, and arterial and venous blood sampling. Assists with invasive procedures and operates electronic physiologic vital signs and EKG monitoring equipment. Assists PI with administering pharmacologic challenge agents in accordance with the research protocol and radiation safety procedures. Assists with collecting, preparing, and processing lab specimens, which may include centrifugation, plasma separation, aliquoting, well counter measurement, and preparation of samples for metabolite analysis. Maintains chain-of-custody and specimen accountability documentation. Monitors participants before, during, and after radiotracer and challenge agent administration. Records vital signs, ECG, and symptom assessments; collects and reviews clinical laboratory results, urine drug screens, breath alcohol measurements, and pregnancy testing; and monitors results for adverse reactions. Recognizes, documents, and escalates adverse events to the PI, for IRB filing, and to the sponsor per policy. Collects participant data, including medical and psychiatric histories, substance use histories, concomitant medications, and physical assessment findings. Maintains and enters data into case report forms, study databases, and logs in a timely and accurate manner. Performs general laboratory duties including, but not limited to, monitoring supply and study drug inventory, monitoring, cleaning and maintaining medical equipment. Physical Effort Light to moderate. Position requires prolonged standing and repositioning during PET acquisitions, frequent movement between the PET suite, laboratory, and office areas, and occasional lifting of supplies up to 25 pounds. Requires manual dexterity for catheter placement and specimen handling. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Nurse II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research - Nursing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor of Science in Nursing Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification RN Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004378": {
      "title": "EMOC Coordinator Trainee",
      "description": "Job Description - EMOC Coordinator Trainee (26004378) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - EMOC Coordinator Trainee (26004378) Job Description EMOC Coordinator Trainee Work-in Process Labor - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004378 ) Job Summary The EMOC Coordinator Trainee will be provided with on-the-job training in the 24/7/365 EMOC Command Center under the supervision of a full-time member of the EMOC staff, i.e. a Coordinator, Technician, or Senior Manager. The apprentice program shall consist of 4,160 hours of on-the-job training while attending classes at Local 95 in their off-hours for two years. Under supervision, the trainee will be assisting with and eventually responsible for continuous monitoring of campus wide BAS/EMS networks, systems, and devices, as well as providing supervised coordination and support of any campus infrastructure event or emergency involving Facilities Management. The Trainee will also be trained and expected to participate in job duties including monitoring the operation of building MEP and Utility function through the centralized Building Automation System, reviewing and respond to system alarms by coordinating appropriate field support, responding to any campus situation and/or emergency by contacting appropriate management team members and coordinating support and response activities, receive off hour customer calls placed to Facilities Management and respond accordingly by coordinating and dispatching FM staff. The EMOC Coordinator Trainee will be required to learn and apply all aspects of the Coordinator’s responsibilities in order to complete the program. The full training schedule, as outlined in the Local 95 – 95A CBA, consists of (4) six-month steps. Placement within schedule is based on experience. Any person selected to be a Trainee from within or from outside the University shall be on a probationary status for 6 months. Following successful completion of the Coordinator Trainee program days and hours worked will convert to Rotating shifts as assigned. Essential Functions EMOC Coordinator Trainee, you will be required to learn and apply all aspects of the Coordinator's responsibilities. The full training schedule, as outlined in the Local 95 – 95A CBA, consists of (4) six-month steps. Placement within schedule is based on experience. Any person selected to be a Trainee from within or from outside the University shall be on a probationary status for 6 months. University shall be on a probationary status for 6 months. Following successful completion of the Coordinator Trainee program days and hours worked will convert to Rotating shifts as assigned. Duties and responsibilities are as assigned by FM Management. Position reports to EMOC Building Automation/Energy Management Systems Manager. Position requires the ability to be mobile around campus and able to lift 50 pounds, crawl into confined spaces (including manholes and utility tunnels), maneuver in and around tight areas, climb ladders and work from heights, and the ability to lift equipment and supplies. Position requires alternate shift work. Position is part of a Collective Bargaining Agreement with IUOE Local 95. Physical Effort Position requires the ability to be mobile around campus and able to lift 50 pounds, crawl into confined spaces (including manholes and utility tunnels), maneuver in and around tight areas, climb ladders and work from heights, and the ability to lift equipment and supplies. Position requires alternate shift work. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Union Eligible.95 Pittsburgh.EMOC Coordinator Trainee Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 7:00 a.m. - 3:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Per Collective Bargaining Agreement Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004544": {
      "title": "Police /Academy",
      "description": "Job Description - Police /Academy (26004544) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Police /Academy (26004544) Job Description Police /Academy Bradford Security - Pennsylvania-Bradford - ( 26004544 ) Job Summary Gains the necessary skills to successfully graduate from the Police Academy and attain MPOETC certification. Accompanies police officers in conducting patrols, enforcing laws, and responding to calls. Develops and enhances skills and understanding of laws, policies, and procedures. Recruits potential candidates, provides program information, and attends promotional events. Essential Functions Develop skills in law enforcement. Accompany officers in conducting foot and vehicular patrols of a university campus. Build strong relationships in a multi-cultural environment. Grow a comprehensive understanding of local, state, and federal laws. Gain skills in police reporting, investigation, and court testimony Physical Effort Ability to communicate over phone/radio. Provide security protection for the campus community. Requires prolonged periods of walking, standing and sitting. Ability to operate a motor vehicle, all-terrain vehicle and successfully pass any required firearms qualification required by the department. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Police Officer - Academy Job Family Safety & Security Job Sub-Family Police Campus Bradford Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Required: Background investigation & Child Protective Clearances - psychological evaluation - physical & 5 panel drug screen - reading test - physical fitness test (run, pushups-sit-ups must meet 30th percentile or above) - Final appointment is contingent upon admission to the Act 120 Police Academy at IUP. Failing to graduate from the Academy or attaining MPOETC certification within 30 days because of conduct, ethics, or policy violations will result in termination Work Schedule Schedule varies by need Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005973": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Technician (26005973) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Technician (26005973) Job Description Laboratory Technician Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005973 ) A Laboratory Technician is needed to work on a funded research project studying bacteriophage therapy for the treatment of antibiotic-resistant infections. The Laboratory Technician will assist with screening bacterial strains for phage susceptibility, manufacturing phages for clinical use, and processing biospecimens collected from patients who receive this new therapeutic modality. Tasks will include molecular assays like qPCR, phage susceptibility testing, phage purification and testing, genomic DNA extraction, laboratory supply management and ordering, and preparation of research reports. The Laboratory Technician key duties will include but not limited to: •Performing laboratory testing and some analysis, including organizing, preparing, and testing multiple types of human biospecimens. •Operating and maintaining applicable laboratory equipment for job functions. •Keeping detailed, accurate, and timely data and log books. Organizing and documenting results. •Sterilizing, maintaining, and cleaning lab equipment; preparing work areas; and maintaining cleanliness throughout the laboratory. •Maintaining inventories and assisting with ordering proper supplies and chemicals. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions Perform and document routine laboratory procedures and experiments while maintaining equipment, ensuring safety compliance, and supporting accurate, reliable research operations. Physical Effort Standing for extended periods, lifting and carrying equipment or supplies up to moderate weights, and performing repetitive hand and arm motions during laboratory procedures. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:30am-5:00pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $18 - $22 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
