    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006049": {
      "title": "Social Worker-MSW",
      "description": "Job Description - Social Worker-MSW (26006049) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Social Worker-MSW (26006049) Job Description Social Worker-MSW Med-Neurology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006049 ) The University of Pittsburgh Department of Neurology (ADRC) is seeking a qualified Social Worker - MSW. This position will provide research social work support and cognitive/ functional assessments to the NIA-funded University of of Pittsburgh Alzheimer’s Disease Research Center and clinical trials program in the Department of Neurology. The person will conduct psychosocial and/or cognitive assessments and research evaluations of subjects/families/study partners for ADRC programs, participate in consensus conferences and organize family diagnostic meetings as required. Conduct independent global rating evaluations for federal and industry-sponsored drug studies; serve as liaison to research consortia; work with recruitment coordinators to develop a recruitment network; serve as a resource to research participants/families/study partners and health professionals and trainees. Participate in research participant /family support groups and assist with community outreach programs. Provide education on ADRC brain donation program and assist with coordination of cases as needed. Provide mentorship and training to social work students and trainees. Education: Master’s degree in Social Work or comparable Master’s degree. Job Summary Performs psychosocial and neuropsychological assessments of patients and families as well as project-directed qualitative interviews; presents assessment findings. Provides referrals for patients, screens individuals for research registry eligibility, develops research project materials, and provides crisis intervention counseling. Serves as a resource and assists in obtaining research grants and funding. Essential Functions Conduct psychosocial assessments of participants and their families/ study partners and /or cognitive/ functional assessments and complete standardized assessment forms (including the UDS required by NIA) for use in clinical research analyses. Conduct independent global assessments for federal and industry-sponsored clinical drug trials. Conduct behavioral assessments and telephone interviews for ADRC projects. Participate and present assessment findings at consensus conference and study recruitment meetings.onduct screening procedures for eligibility into research registry and clinical trials program. Perform on-line assessment form data entry (eCRFs). Serve as a resource to research participants /study partners and health professionals and trainees. Develop project materials for participant /study partners. Provide referral information upon request. Provide education on ADRC brain donation program and assist with coordination of cases as needed. Work with recruitment coordinators from various programs to develop a recruitment network. Participate in ADRC support groups, lead discussions as needed. Participate in community outreach programs and provide resource materials at health fairs and other aging wellness programs. Physical Effort Must be able to get around a university setting. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Social Worker - MSW Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Behavioral & Mental Health Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification MSW + LSW Work Schedule M-F, 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006041": {
      "title": "Research Dietitian",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Dietitian (26006041) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Dietitian (26006041) Job Description Research Dietitian Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006041 ) This position is for the Division of Genetic and Genomic Medicine within the Department of Pediatrics. Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. The salary range for this part-time position will be prorated based on 60% effort as the position is 22.5 hours per week. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Prepares accurate patient nutritional care and designs and implements diets to align with study protocols. Trains dietary data coordinators, collects and enters study data, analyzes nutritional records, and oversees the certification of all nutrition research assistants. Assists physicians and faculty with regulatory documents, study preparation, and grants and reports. Develops tailored materials and provides assistance with nutrition-related tasks. Essential Functions • Prepares patient nutritional care in accordance with diagnosis, research protocols, and all applicable regulations. Designs and implements diets to align with study protocols. • Trains dietary data coordinators to customize a nutrient analysis database as directed; collects and enters study dietary data as directed. Oversees the certification of all nutrition research assistants. • Acquires documents to conduct and complete study forms; collects and analyzes nutritional records. • Assists physicians and other faculty with preparation of regulatory documents, planning, subject recruitment, enrollment, scheduling, study conduct, agendas, manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, grants, and reports. • Collaborates with study staff to develop tailored materials and integrate the nutrition information with the other components of the study. • Provides technical assistance to study staff on nutrition-related tasks. Physical Effort Light – needs to be able to carry large binders. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Part-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Dietitian Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification Registered Dietitian Work Schedule This position is part-time (60% effort, 22.5 hours per week) and will require flexibility with shift/hours; incumbent may need to occasionally work evenings or weekends to attend meetings or conduct patient visits. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005426": {
      "title": "Academic Labor Relations Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Academic Labor Relations Specialist (26005426) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Academic Labor Relations Specialist (26005426) Job Description Academic Labor Relations Specialist Employee/Labor Relations - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005426 ) Job Summary The Academic Labor Relations Specialist provides management and staff with day-to-day guidance regarding labor relations matters, including University policies, procedures, and the provisions of collective bargaining agreements; acting as an advisor/consultant to managers, staff and union officials. Essential Functions • Contract interpretation and application of provisions of a collective bargaining agreement. • Assist management with investigating, answering, and resolving grievances and responding to requests for information. • Attend or assist with union grievance meetings, including preparation and drafting responses to unions; assist managers and represented faculty in interpreting labor contract provisions. • Establish and build effective relationships with labor unions. • Provide labor relations support in preparation for and during contract negotiations. • Conduct training for staff and management on labor relations issues. • Make recommendations on matters related to workplace conflict and discipline. • Exercise judgment consistent with university standards, policies, and procedures within the bounds of federal, state, and local laws. • Works with management, human resources staff, legal counsel to investigate, document, and resolve alleged violations of law and policy; complaints including equity, misconduct, discrimination, harassment, and others; if applicable, the merits of labor grievances. • Investigate or assist in the investigation of incidents and complaints involving represented faculty and University staff members, as well as alleged misconduct by represented faculty. • Assists in the development and implementation of human resources policies and procedures. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Labor Relations Specialist Job Family Human Resources Job Sub-Family Employee & Labor Relations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006067": {
      "title": "Animal Care Technician I",
      "description": "Job Description - Animal Care Technician I (26006067) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Animal Care Technician I (26006067) Job Description Animal Care Technician I DLAR-Animal Husbandry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006067 ) The Division of Laboratory Animal Resources (DLAR) Animal Care Technician I will provide husbandry and care of laboratory animals with a commitment to animal welfare and well-being. The candidate will: • provide food, water and enrichment • perform cage changes including cleaning and sanitizing animal housing enclosures, equipment and rooms • complete daily health observations and administer basic medical treatments, procedures and unique diets and • maintain logs documenting animal care activities and verification of environmental parameters and equipment function • provide facility support tasks including laundering scrubs, performing general cleaning, sweeping, mopping, stocking supply areas and assisting with cagewash operations The successful candidate must consistently demonstrate positive interpersonal and customer service skills; be proficient with technology in order to use common applications (e.g. email, Microsoft Office, Pittworx); be available to work weekends and holidays; stand for extended periods of time; lift 50 pounds; push/pull heavy equipment; and pass the mandatory criminal and social background checks. Candidates working in the Rangos Research Building at Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh will need to obtain Child Protection Clearances. Vaccinations and TB testing may be required. Pay rate is $18.63/hour. Job Summary Provides animal care to laboratory animals, including feeding, watering, enrichment, health observations and basic medical treatments. Performs cage cleaning and facility sanitization procedures in accordance with standard operating procedures and maintains timely and accurate documentation. Essential Functions The employee must be able to: • read, understand, and follow DLAR and other institutional guidance documents (SOPs, policies), including IACUC approved animal protocols when applicable • follow written and verbal instructions • demonstrate sufficient fine motor skill to manipulate animals and equipment; negotiate around equipment within close quarters; move between rooms and workspaces • have sufficient visual acuity to observe animal behavior and recognize animals inadvertently left in cages as well as automated equipment notifications and printouts • have sufficient audible acuity to hear equipment alarms and other warnings. • wear facility specific Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) for extended periods of time required by the job duties based on risk assessment from EH&S • work directly with live or dead animals and clean or soiled bedding and caging with reasonable accommodations if necessary • accurately and legibly document written information in English in a timely manner, including electronic formats and applications (e.g., PRISM, CAMS) • effective written and verbal communication in English, including the use of email • successfully enroll in University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program (AESP) and other medical surveillance/immunization programs as dictated by current research activities • receive vaccinations and health assessments, including TB testing, required to work in some animal holding or procedure areas in accordance with DLAR and/or EH&S policies and practices Physical Effort The employee must be able to: • stand for extended periods of time for the majority of the workday • lift and move objects weighing up to 50 pounds including, but not limited to, caging and equipment, bags or boxes of animal diet and animal bedding • operate flatbed hand trucks or pallet jacks to push/pull heavier objects or weights exceeding 50 pounds • perform repetitive motion tasks that involve pushing, pulling, twisting, reaching, and/or bending • physically handle and restrain a variety of small and large laboratory animals and • negotiate and navigate around animal facility caging, equipment, and the physical plant. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Animal Care Technician I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Animal Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification None required. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.; some weekends and holidays Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $18.63/hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005976": {
      "title": "Outreach Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Outreach Coordinator (26005976) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Outreach Coordinator (26005976) Job Description Outreach Coordinator Pitt Serves - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005976 ) The Office of PittServes within the Division of Student Affairs at the University of Pittsburgh serves as a catalyst for students and communities to engage in action that creates impactful change. The Outreach Coordinator will be joining a team working to realize the vision of achieving resilient and equitable communities and inspire civically minded individuals. The Office of PittServes focuses on engaging and educating Pitt students about civic action, with student leaders key to engaging their peers. Working with partners in the greater Pittsburgh community, as well as on-campus entities, current programs range from (but are not limited to) Pitt Impact Ambassadors, campus and community-based sustainability initiatives, Signature Days of Service, Alternative Break trips, PittVotes, the Pitt Civic Engagement Council, and other partnerships engaging students in community-identified projects. All employees within the Division will be asked to perform duties outside of their department. Additional assignments may include, but are not limited to Welcome Week Activities, Divisional committees, events, etc. A successful candidate will possess: Civic engagement skills — connects with student organizations and helps them explore ways to get involved in community and civic activities, offering guidance and useful resources along the way. Relationship-building — reaches out to and builds trust with local agencies and partners, keeping communication open so those relationships can grow over time. Event coordination — helps plan and organize student-facing events, such as sustainability initiatives and days of service, handling the logistics and administrative details. Data tracking and trend awareness — keeps outreach records current in the tracking system and stays alert to shifts in community needs at the local, state, and national level. Budget and grant skills — oversees program budgets responsibly and pursues grant funding and fundraising opportunities to keep initiatives running smoothly. Job Summary Implements a comprehensive outreach plan and plays a crucial role in expansion programs and service-based initiatives. Performs targeted outreach to engage new partners and identifies opportunities to expand the depth of the organizations providing episodic and long-term service projects to the University community. Identifies service trends and needs and provides comprehensive support for student-facing sustainability events. Performs budgetary functions and grant writing. Essential Functions Implements a comprehensive outreach plan that is designed to increase the number of community-agency partners and provide service opportunities. Plays a crucial role in expansion programs and service-based initiatives. Attends to community partner needs and performs targeted outreach to engage new partners based on student interest. Identifies opportunities to expand the depth and breadth of the organizations providing episodic and long-term service projects to the University community; communicates with these organizations and consistently updates the online data management/service database. Assists in identifying local, state, and national trends of service and need. Advises and supports student organizations and groups exploring community and civic engagement opportunities; creates relationships and identifies resources and tools that connect and expose students to civic and community engagement programs, events, issues, and organizations connected with the community and civic engagement. Provides administrative, program planning, logistical, and budget assistance for student-facing sustainability events; collaborates with students on program initiatives, marketing, and outreach. Manages the budget for the initiative, which includes additional fundraising and grant writing opportunities. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Outreach Coordinator II Job Family Community & Government Job Sub-Family Community Outreach Program Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005974": {
      "title": "Student Engagement Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Student Engagement Coordinator (26005974) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Student Engagement Coordinator (26005974) Job Description Student Engagement Coordinator Pitt Serves - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005974 ) The Office of PittServes within the Division of Student Affairs at the University of Pittsburgh serves as a catalyst for students and communities to engage in action that creates impactful change. The Student Engagement Coordinator will be joining a team working to realize the vision of achieving resilient and equitable communities and inspire civically minded individuals. The Office of PittServes focuses on engaging and educating Pitt students about civic action, with student leaders key to engaging their peers. Working with partners in the greater Pittsburgh community, as well as on-campus entities, current programs range from (but are not limited to) Pitt Impact Ambassadors, campus and community-based sustainability initiatives, Signature Days of Service, Alternative Break trips, PittVotes, the Pitt Civic Engagement Council, and other partnerships engaging students in community-identified projects. All employees within the Division will be asked to perform duties outside of their department. Additional assignments may include, but are not limited to Welcome Week Activities, Divisional committees, events, etc. Skill requirements for this position: Event & Program Coordination: Strong organizational and project management skills to plan, coordinate, and execute student events, activities, and leadership-development programs, including facility, equipment, and logistics arrangements. Advising & Student Development: Ability to advise and mentor student organizations, governance groups, and clubs on program planning and decision-making, with knowledge of student development principles and group facilitation. Financial & Policy Oversight: Proficiency in basic accounting/budget reconciliation and a working knowledge of institutional policies (organization registration, solicitations, concessions) to monitor compliance and serve as a policy resource. Communication & Marketing: Excellent written and verbal communication skills for creating promotional materials, publicizing events, and building community/media relationships to enhance university visibility. Interpersonal Flexibility & Availability: Strong interpersonal skills to engage diverse students, faculty, and staff, paired with willingness to work evenings/weekends to attend student-sponsored meetings and events. Job Summary Assists in the organization and development of student activities and coordination of special events. Advises student organizations and students on programs and services. Attends student-sponsored social events, monitors organizations' financials and performs reconciliations, and ensures compliance with all University policies. Publicizes student events, assists in developing promotional materials, and registers and monitors new student organizations and requests. Essential Functions Assists in organizing student activities, which may include social events, Greek programs, student government committees, newspapers, clubs, and organizations. Assists in developing, planning, and coordinating special events including student/faculty events, recreational activities, and student-leadership-development opportunities. Assists and advises student organizations regarding program planning, use of facilities, program arrangements, services and available equipment. Advises students in developing, coordinating, implementing and scheduling organization programs of a co-curricular nature. Promotes responsible student decision-making and encourages wide student participation. Attends meetings and other student-sponsored social events. Monitors organizations’ accounting procedures and advises regarding proper procedures; reconciles and verifies accuracy of accounts. Explains and monitors compliance with University policies and procedures pertaining to student activities; serves as a resource to faculty and other staff in matters of program development, policy, and procedures. Seeks to publicize student events in the local community and to increase community awareness of the University. Assists in developing and designing informational and promotional materials and publications about student activities, student affairs, and the campus in general including publishing the events calendar. Registers new student organizations and reviews, approves, and monitors requests for  concessions and solicitations. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Student Activities Coordinator Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005999": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Project Coordinator (26005999) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Coordinator (26005999) Job Description Project Coordinator Psychology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005999 ) A Project Coordinator is needed to coordinate two studies focused on clarifying the role of socioaffective processing in risk for internalizing psychopathologies and suicidal thoughts and behaviors (STBs) in adolescents. The first study, led by Dr. Kiera James in collaboration with Dr. Cope Feurer (UNC-Chapel Hill), is a multi-site project including both Pitt and UNC, funded by the NIMH and involves the co-design, development, and validation of a new adolescent emotional faces stimulus set. This study will also test whether neural responses to these new stimuli improve prediction of depression, anxiety, and STBs in adolescents compared to previously validated adult stimuli. The second study, also funded by the NIMH, uses EEG,  ecological momentary assessment (EMA), and donation of text/social media data to understand the relations between internal attention to cues of social threat, day-to-day social connectedness, and STBs. Across both studies, the coordinator will 1) recruit participants, 2) schedule and conduct EEG and/or dyadic study visits, 3) conduct suicide risk assessments and safety planning procedures, 4) assist with data processing and management, 5) interact with the Institutional Review Board to prepare and modify protocols, consent forms, and reports, 6) maintain regulatory binders and standard operating procedure binders to assure compliance with Governmental and University regulations, 7) manage a small team of undergraduate research assistants, and 8) assist with manuscript preparation and publication. Additionally, for the first study, the coordinator will 1) oversee recruitment of adolescents across both Pitt and UNC sites to pose for new stimuli, 2) conduct and oversee photography sessions for stimulus development, 3) manage a team of undergraduates to coordinate the validation of these stimuli using online research platforms, and 4) schedule Youth Advisory Board meetings for stimulus feedback. Required Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in Psychology, Neuroscience, or related field • Minimum of 2 years of human subjects research experience • Evidence of excellent organizational, interpersonal, communication, and leadership skills • Experience working with adolescents The Dietrich School is committed to building a culturally diverse staff. Excellent interpersonal and relationship-building skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of individuals and constituencies in support of a diverse community are required. All applicants must submit a CV/resume and a cover letter. Job Summary Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Recruits research subjects and conducts interviews and research assessments. Essential Functions Must be able to complete all necessary IRB trainings and provide Act 33/34 clearances in order to interact with research participants. Physical Effort The position is primarily sedentary, although walking to lab spaces in other buildings in Oakland will be required for conducting assessments. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule 37.5 hours/week (variable, with flexibility for weekend and evening hours) Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $17.74 to $22.17 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005683": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to the Dean",
      "description": "Job Description - Executive Assistant to the Dean (26005683) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Executive Assistant to the Dean (26005683) Job Description Executive Assistant to the Dean Social Work-Academic Programs - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005683 ) Required Qualifications • Bachelor's degree and a minimum of 3–5 years of progressively responsible administrative or executive support experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. • Demonstrated experience supporting senior leadership (e.g., dean, vice president, executive director) in a higher education, nonprofit, or comparable professional setting. • Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to draft polished, professional correspondence with minimal oversight. • Proven ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality regarding sensitive personnel, academic, and administrative information. • Strong organizational skills and demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. • Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and calendar management tools. Preferred Qualifications • Experience within a university setting, particularly supporting an academic dean's or department chair's office. • Familiarity with University of Pittsburgh systems and processes (e.g., PeopleSoft/Pitt Worx, Concur, PantherExpress). • Experience coordinating events, Board relations, or donor/alumni engagement. • Master's degree in a relevant field. Job Summary Serves as the primary support to executive level roles and/or departments and acts as liaison and ensures confidentiality of high-level, sensitive information. Manages office workflow. Assists with strategic planning processes and administrative goals and priorities. Prepares budgetary functions and plans special events. Essential Functions The Executive Assistant to the Dean provides high-level, confidential administrative support to the Dean of the School of Social Work, serving as a key point of coordination between the Dean's Office and internal and external stakeholders. This position manages the Dean's calendar and correspondence, coordinates School-wide initiatives and events, prepares briefing materials and communications, and exercises independent judgment and discretion in handling sensitive academic, personnel, and administrative matters. The Executive Assistant serves as a trusted advisor on office operations and represents the Dean's Office with professionalism in interactions across the University and with external partners. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Executive Assistant Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006001": {
      "title": "Email Marketing Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Email Marketing Specialist (26006001) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Email Marketing Specialist (26006001) Job Description Email Marketing Specialist Office of the SVC and Provost - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006001 ) Pitt EDGE is the University of Pittsburgh’s central hub for digital education, housed within the Office of the Provost. This inaugural Center advances the University’s strategic vision for online, hybrid, and continuing education by partnering with Pitt’s 16 schools to expand access and improve quality for diverse learners. Pitt EDGE supports the full lifecycle of digital learning through services such as marketing support and analysis, technology integration, instructional design, academic planning, recruitment, and quality assurance. If you are detail-oriented and enjoy building the systems that connect prospective students to the information they need, we welcome you to become an Email Marketing Specialist on our team. In this role, you will hold a crucial position in building and maintaining email communications, managing send execution and data accuracy, and contributing to the marketing infrastructure that supports enrollment across the University of Pittsburgh Center for Excellence in Digital Education/Pitt Online. Job Summary Manages and facilitates targeted email campaign processes utilizing email marketing automation and multiple software programs. Manages email campaign calendar, email messaging, and provides result analysis of campaigns. Supports marketing campaigns by designing and hosting landing pages. Ensures consistent messaging and maintains University brand and style. Essential Functions •    Build and deploy email journeys for pillar programs and EDGE Recruitment team, including trigger setup, entry criteria, and send configuration •    Support build and deployment of email journeys for school partners as assigned •    Populate and maintain school-specific dynamic content blocks; update as program information changes •    Manage send schedules, suppression lists, and test deploys for all assigned sends •    Complete QA checklist before every send; document and resolve or escalate as needed •    Utilize and maintain data tracking protocols including but not limited to UTM parameters, email tagging, and campaigns •    Support Email Marketing Manager in answering execution questions from school-based staff (template use, suppression, scheduling) as needed •    Monitor email performance data and compile reports upon journey close •    Ensure all content meets accessibility standards Physical Effort Must be able to sit for prolonged periods of time while working at a computer. Must be able to occasionally lift and/or move up to 15 pounds (e.g., files, equipment) The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Communications Coordinator Job Family Communications & Marketing Job Sub-Family Communications Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday- Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Remote: Teams working from different locations (off-campus). Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006042": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Digital Enrollment",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Director of Digital Enrollment (26006042) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Director of Digital Enrollment (26006042) Job Description Assistant Director of Digital Enrollment Office of the SVC and Provost - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006042 ) Pitt EDGE is the University of Pittsburgh’s central hub for digital education, housed within the Office of the Provost. This inaugural Center advances the University’s strategic vision for online, hybrid, and continuing education by partnering with Pitt’s 16 schools to expand access and improve quality for diverse learners. Pitt EDGE supports the full lifecycle of digital learning through services such as enrollment management, instructional design, technology integration, market analysis, academic planning, recruitment, and quality assurance. If you are an experienced enrollment professional who thrives on coaching teams, delivering effective training, and turning pipeline data into action, we welcome you to become an Assistant Director of Digital Enrollment on our team. In this role, you will hold a crucial leadership position supervising Enrollment Specialists, overseeing daily enrollment activity across an assigned school portfolio, facilitating training for new and existing staff, and ensuring prospects move through the funnel with consistency and accountability at the University of Pittsburgh Center for Excellence in Digital Education/Pitt Online. Job Summary Facilitates the recruitment, evaluation, and selection of all students seeking entrance to a school or college of the University. Serves on management team to initiate new programs and procedures; represents the school/college internally and externally. Essential Functions •    Directly supervise Enrollment Specialists, monitoring individual and team pipeline activity in CRM •    Support onboarding and ongoing training of Enrollment Specialists •    Oversee daily enrollment activity across assigned school portfolio; escalate stalled prospects or process breakdowns to Director •    Run weekly pipeline aging reports to identify prospects stalled at each funnel stage beyond defined thresholds; assign re-engagement actions to Enrollment Specialists and monitor follow-through •    Review lead source attribution data in CRM; escalate findings to marketing team •    Coordinate with program contacts to maintain accurate intake requirements, deadlines, and program intel for specialist use •    Maintain working relationships with program directors and graduate coordinators •    Surface program-level feedback from specialists to Director for strategic adjustment •    Facilitate enrollment training for school and EDGE new hires and refreshers; co-facilitate with external training partners as applicable •    Maintain and update Enrollment Specialist playbooks, FAQ docs, and program-specific intake guides Physical Effort Must be able to sit for prolonged periods of time while working at a computer. Must be able to occasionally lift and/or move up to 15 pounds (e.g., files, equipment) The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Assistant Director - Admissions Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Admissions, Enrollment, & Recruitment Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday- Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Remote: Teams working from different locations (off-campus). Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005979": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Job Description - Financial Aid Counselor (26005979) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Financial Aid Counselor (26005979) Job Description Financial Aid Counselor Admissions & Financial Aid - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005979 ) Job Summary Analyzes applicant financial aid information, selects candidates, and determines awarded financial aid. Assists in financial aid policy preparation and in applications for government loan program federal funds. Conducts applicant interviews and administers assigned financial aid programs. Essential Functions Analyzes financial information submitted by applicants using established federal and University standards and guidelines to determine financial needs; selects candidates and determines the type and amount of financial aid to be awarded. Assists in the preparation of student financial assistance policies for the University. Corresponds and conducts interviews with applicants and their parents, counsels’ students, and answers inquiries from various sources on financial aid policies and procedures. Assists in making application for federal funds for government loan programs; administers rules and regulations set forth by the federal government concerning government funds. Coordinates and administers assigned financial aid loan programs such as private loans, federal plus loans; develops and implements new initiatives within assigned program areas. Reviews detailed reports to stay in compliance and resolve loan errors to avoid longer loan disbursing delays. Physical Effort Most work is sedentary, completed within an office setting. Some counseling/presenting is performed at other campuses and off-campus sites. Employee must be able to move about the campus to meetings and travel to locations outside of the University of Pittsburgh. Employee may be required to carry a box of material up to 50 lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Financial Aid Counselor Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Financial Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., some mornings, evenings and weekends may be required Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004845": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator (26004845) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator (26004845) Job Description Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004845 ) The Clinical Research Nurse is a full-time position expected to travel to long-term care facilities at the discretion of the project PI, Dr. Chrissy Kistler. Job Summary Supports clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews lab results, patient data, and lab specimens; administers medications and protocol-specific treatments. Performs general laboratory duties and specialized nursing duties, trains new staff, and ensures regulatory adherence. Essential Functions This role involves supporting clinical research studies by working directly with participants throughout the study process. Responsibilities include recruiting and coordinating participants, conducting monthly study visits, administering intravenous medications and infusions (including IV insertion), and performing health and function assessments. The position also includes collecting and processing biological samples, scheduling and coordinating appointments, educating participants on study procedures, and providing ongoing guidance and support to ensure a smooth, personalized study experience. Physical Effort Valid driver's license and vehicle required to travel to long-term care facilities. Must be able to make multiple stops in one day. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Nurse II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research - Nursing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor of Science in Nursing Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification RN Work Schedule TBD Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005472": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005472) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005472) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician GSPH-Infectious Diseases & Microbiology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005472 ) The University of Pittsburgh's School of Public Health, Department of Infectious Diseases and Microbiology has a long and distinguished history as a leader in graduate education, transformative research, implementation science, and education in infectious diseases. A central component of our mission involves training the next generation of scientists and public health professionals to lead in the effort to reduce the impact of infectious diseases worldwide. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions Candidate should have experience working with laboratory mice, standard and quantitative real-time PCR assays, DNA extractions, gel electrophoresis, and managing large datasets. The candidate should have good organizational skills and experience managing students in the lab. Experience ordering supplies using PantherExpress system is favorable. Additionally, experience with writing reports and manuscript preparation are a plus. Physical Effort Must be able to sit and stand for prolonged periods of time in laboratory setting.  Light physical effort required. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005934": {
      "title": "Post Award Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Post Award Specialist (26005934) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Post Award Specialist (26005934) Job Description Post Award Specialist Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005934 ) Job Summary Performs post-award accounting duties for complex grants and contracts. Monitors account activity, performs internal audits, resolves complex issues, and provides policy and procedure interpretation. Prepares complex government reports and reviews routine reports. Facilitates accounting techniques and procedures to improve operations. Assists with managing special projects and budgeting functions. Essential Functions The position is accountable for post-award functions, both operational and financial. Will provide support for the financial activities of a large academic department. The position requires the application of a broad knowledge of principles, practices, and procedures in research accounting, post-award administration, and budgeting. The individual in this position works with department leadership in the development and implementation of policies, procedures, and methods to handle unusual or complex situations. Physical Effort This is a fairly sedentary position but may require walking to other locations on campus. Occasional lifting of files and light office equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Post-Award) Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Grants & Contracts Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005965": {
      "title": "Director of Research Operations",
      "description": "Job Description - Director of Research Operations (26005965) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director of Research Operations (26005965) Job Description Director of Research Operations Clinical and Translational Science Institute - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005965 ) The Clinical and Translational Science Institute (CTSI) at the University of Pittsburgh is looking for a Director of Research Operations. This researcher will be responsible for: - Showing representation at scientific meetings: Formally representing the team at various scientific conferences and professional gatherings. - Collaborative Initiatives: Engaging directly on strategic initiatives within the Precision Medicine, International Initiatives, Primary Care, and Precision Community Engagement teams. - Grant and Manuscript Development: Leading/co-leading grant writing for upcoming projects, such as the R01. - Project Oversight/leadership: Managing the design and implementation of research projects and oversee diverse teams of students and staff. There will be potential for patient/participant exposure with the need to work in multiple settings including clinical and research spaces. Candidate must be able to complete all CITI modules and obtain relevant access as needed for credentialling in the UPMC electronic health record. Job Summary Leads a team and directs & oversees all operational aspects of the research program. Establishes and drives the vision, policies, fiscal functions, administration, and strategic plan of a research program to support the delivery of high-quality research services and ensure compliance with established professional, regulatory, and organizational standards and requirements. Formulates budgets and performs associated financial duties. Collaborates with and advises internal and external stakeholders and ensures adherence to regulations. Translates strategic plans into research operational plans oversees administrative matters. Essential Functions Ability to operate a PC and communicate effectively verbally and in written form with a various people. Telephone skills, computer and keyboard skills, strong written and verbal communication skills, and strong organizational skills. Ability to be flexible in location assignment. Ability to participate in face to face or virtual meetings. Ability to connect with diverse groups of people. Physical Effort Position will require standing or sitting for work with reasonable mobility to navigate location site and clinical exam space. Ability to move throughout campus to attend face to face meetings and or participate in virtual meetings or lift reports weighting approximately 15lbs The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Director - Research Operations Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Operations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F 8-4:30pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004260": {
      "title": "Resident Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Resident Director (26004260) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Resident Director (26004260) Job Description Resident Director Greensburg College Hall Dormitory - Pennsylvania-Greensburg - ( 26004260 ) The Resident Director is a member of the professional, live-in Residence Life staff within the Office of Student Life and Success at the University of Pittsburgh at Greensburg. The Office of Student Life and Success oversees a range of services that support students' holistic development outside the classroom, including Residence Life, Student Activities & First-Year Experience, Counseling, and Career Services, as well as support for commuter students, who make up a significant percentage of the student population. In this role, the Resident Director will be responsible for the overall management of one to two residence halls on campus, each housing approximately 100–125 students, and will support the Office of Student Life and Success and the University in advancing its mission, goals, and policies. APPLICATION DEADLINE IS OCTOBER 2, 2026 Job Summary Oversees and manages the University’s residential facilities, residence life educational programs, residentially-based academic communities, residence life student and professional staff, and all promotional communications for the department. Ensures the safety and security of residents and development of the departmental comprehensive emergency management plan. Facilitates operational decisions within broadly defined parameters that require a high level of judgement. Establishes the direction, goals, implementation strategy, and policies of the department. Performs budgetary functions. Essential Functions In order to provide a high level of coverage and support for our students across multiple residential communities, the Resident Director will be responsible for, or share responsibility for, the following: Student Support & Community Development Assisting students and maintaining regular office hours Managing roommate and/or staff conflicts within their assigned residence hall Enforcing residence hall policies and procedures fairly and consistently Meeting with students and conducting student conduct hearings Developing community-building and educational programs and initiatives as part of the department's residential curriculum Serving as advisor/co-advisor to departmental-related organizations and as a liaison to student organizations, including staffing evening and weekend programs Staff Supervision Supervising and supporting a staff of 4–8 Community Assistants (CAs), including programming, supervision, and personal/professional development Assisting the Director with CA recruitment, selection, and training Daily Operations & Safety Overseeing daily operations of the assigned residence hall, including room assignments and occupancy processes, in coordination with Student Life and Success, Facilities Management, and Campus Police to ensure a safe living environment Participating in the professional staff's on-call/duty rotation and responding to concerns as they arise Assisting with housing procedures and the opening/closing of residence halls at the start and end of each semester and during scheduled break periods Assisting with summer residence life activities Programming & Assessment Planning and implementing student activities, orientation programs, and leadership development initiatives Creating content and consistent messaging for communications and programs Designing, developing, and implementing assessments and/or surveys; reviewing results and recommending changes and improvements APPLICATION DEADLINE IS OCTOBER 2, 2026 Physical Effort Work Hours: This position requires nontraditional work hours, including evenings and weekends, due to the needs of campus residents and activities related to enhancing student life and experiences. Physical Demands: This position requires the ability to walk to and between on-campus buildings, meetings, and events, sometimes at a brisk pace or in response to time-sensitive situations. The role may also require standing for extended periods during programs and move-in/move-out, as well as climbing stairs in residence halls that may not have elevator access. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Housing & Residence Life Officer Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Housing & Residence Life Campus Greensburg Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. with evening and weekend hours required. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Starting salary of $43,894.56/year Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005991": {
      "title": "Enrollment Services Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Enrollment Services Assistant (26005991) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Enrollment Services Assistant (26005991) Job Description Enrollment Services Assistant Bradford Enrollment Services - Pennsylvania-Bradford - ( 26005991 ) Pitt-Bradford is welcoming applications for Enrollment Services Assistant in the Office of Enrollment Services. Reporting to Registrar and Director of Enrollment Services, this full-time position serves as a key point of contact, in person, by phone, and by email, for students and parents regarding tuition, fees, registration, related account and academic matters. This position also works closely with faculty and other staff to support students through their educational experience. Job Summary Applies knowledge of programs, procedures, and policies to provide administrative support and assistance in a student services function. Assists current and prospective students and parents. Essential Functions Provides administrative support to the Registrar, including correspondence, reports, and office supply management. Handles daily student payment processing and cash management for the office. Answers questions from students and parents and resolve problems related to invoicing, registration, and academic policies and procedures. Manages course registration and records management for approximately 1,400 students each term. Requirements: High school diploma or GED required; formal business school training helpful. One year of relevant experience required. Strong analytical skills, with the ability to learn and work confidently within student accounting and student records systems. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to handle sensitive and confidential information appropriately. Strong organizational skills, accuracy, and flexibility in a dynamic work environment. We offer an outstanding benefits package designed to support your long-term wellbeing, including: Robust retirement savings: Pitt matches 100% of eligible employee contributions between 3–8% of base salary. After three years, that match increases to 150% — one of the most competitive retirement benefits in higher education. Comprehensive health coverage, including group medical, life, vision, and dental insurance. Generous paid time off, including vacation, sick, and personal time. Education benefit (university-paid tuition) for employee and dependents Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Student Services Assistant Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Services Campus Bradford Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $16.50 - $20.50/hr. Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005941": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator I",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator I - Neuroimaging Research Program (26005941) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator I - Neuroimaging Research Program (26005941) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator I - Neuroimaging Research Program Med-Radiology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005941 ) Coordinates human PET neuroimaging research studies of central nervous system disorders, including substance use and other psychiatric disorders. Recruits and screens research participants, conduct structured clinical interviews and research assessments, and schedule multi-modality study visits. Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) initial submissions, renewals, modifications, and approved protocols. Maintains source documentation, case report forms, and study tracking systems, and supports scan-day operations under the supervision of the Principal Investigator and Clinical Lab Manager. Opportunity for meaningful research contributions and direct mentorship by Principal Investigator. Preferred Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in neuroscience, biology, psychology, or a related field • Prior research, clinical, or volunteer experience with individuals affected by substance use or other psychiatric disorders • Strong organizational skills and comfort coordinating multi-site, time-sensitive schedules • Interest in neuroimaging or a research career in the neurosciences Job Summary Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Recruits research subjects and conducts interviews and research assessments. Essential Functions Recruitment and Screening Recruits research participants through community and health system referral partners, including addiction medicine clinics, rehabilitation and medically managed withdrawal programs, intensive outpatient programs, and recovery support organizations, as well as through advertising, registries, and community outreach activities. Conducts telephone and in-person pre-screening, reviews inclusion and exclusion criteria against the approved protocol. Assists with the informed consent process under the supervision of the Principal Investigator, including reviewing consent documents with prospective participants, documenting the consent discussion, and confirming comprehension and voluntariness. Tracks recruitment sources, screening outcomes, enrollment, and retention; prepares enrollment and accrual summaries for investigator and sponsor reporting. Clinical Interviews and Research Assessments Conducts structured and semi-structured clinical interviews with research participants, including individuals with psychiatric, substance use, and trauma-related disorders, following protocol-specified training and certification requirements. Administers, scores, and documents protocol-specified research assessments, including substance use history and timeline follow-back measures, symptom rating scales, and neuropsychological or self-report instruments. Collects protocol-required screening measures such as vital signs, electrocardiograms (ECGs), urine toxicology, breath alcohol testing, and self-reported substance use, and reports results to the study nurse, Principal Investigator, or study physician for clinical interpretation and eligibility decisions. Recognizes participant distress or safety concerns raised during interviews and immediately escalates to the study nurse, Principal Investigator, or covering study physician in accordance with the protocol’s safety and escalation pathway. Study Visit Coordination Schedules and coordinates multi-modality research visits across the PET facility, MRI facility, aligning participant arrival with radiotracer production and injection timing. Prepares scan-day materials, source documents, and worksheets; confirms pre-visit requirements such as abstinence intervals, fasting, medication holds, and MRI safety screening questionnaires. Provides clinical research support during PET and MRI visits, clinical assessments and questionnaires, timing and documentation of protocol events, sample labeling and logging, and specimen transport to the laboratory. Explains study components to subjects in an understandable manner. Ensures knowledge of next steps and comfort with upcoming study procedures. Regulatory and Data Management Assists with IRB applications, modifications, continuing reviews, reportable events, and study closure documents; maintains submission tracking and approval records. Ensures studies are conducted as outlined in the approved protocol and in accordance with Good Clinical Practice, HIPAA, and University and sponsor requirements; identifies and reports protocol deviations. Maintains investigator documentation in audit-ready condition; supports monitoring visits and internal quality reviews. Maintains physical and electronic study tracking and data files; performs timely and accurate data entry into case report forms and electronic data capture systems, resolves queries, and supports data submission to sponsor-required repositories. Physical Effort Must be able to stand or sit for long periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005702": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005702) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005702) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician Med-Radiation Oncology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005702 ) Seeking a research technician to work in a dynamic and fast-paced Translational Oncology research laboratory at the Hillman Cancer Center of the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center. The candidate is expected to work independently following the guidance of a physician-scientist in the Department of Radiation Oncology and will carry out experiments investigating pediatric brain tumor cancer biology and radiopharmaceutical therapy.  Roles will include cell culture, in vitro cell viability assays, flow cytometry, Western Blot, mouse work including orthotopic tumor implantation, treating tumor-bearing mice with radiation, monitoring tumor growth, and harvesting mouse tissues for further analyses. The candidate is also expected to work with collaborators at the Hillman Cancer Center and the SaMIRA radiopharmacuetical core to perform radiopharmaceutical therapy, SPECT/PET/CT imaging, and MRI and image analysis. Experience in doing basic science research and cell culture is required more specific training will be provided. Good written and communication skills are required. Candidates should have at least a Bachelors of Science in biology, biochemistry, neuroscience, bioengineering, biomedical engineering, and one year of post-graduate research experience. Job Summary Performs a variety of independent laboratory work and experiments such as determining experimental protocols and preparation of specimens and cultures. Prepares reports of findings subsequent to compilation and analyzation. Oversees specimen inventory. Develops documentation for publication; crafts manuscripts and grant proposals. Essential Functions Duties may include some or all the following: •    Maintain an organized and complete lab notebook of experiments that are performed. •    Propagate cells in cell culture and perform in vitro viability assays and clonogenic assays. •    Perform flow cytometry on murine and human cells (with Hillman flow core) to characterize surface receptor expression. •    Perform Western blots to characterize cell lines, tumor tissues, and mouse tissues. •    Extract DNA and RNA from mouse tumor tissue for next generation sequencing. •    Orthotopic injection of tumor cell lines into mice (training will be provided) •    In-vivo bioluminescence imaging to track tumor growth •    Collecting tumor tissue from mice. •    Treatment of tumor bearing mice with radiation using both external beam and/or radiopharmaceutical therapy •    Work with Pitt’s advanced imaging core to deliver brain specimens for MRI studies. •    Work with the SaMIRA imaging facility at Hillman to design novel radiopharmaceutical therapies •    Work with the SaMIRA imaging facility at Hillman to perform SPECT/PET/CT imaging. •    Work with the SaMIRA imaging facility at Hillman to perform image analysis •    Generate protocols, standard operating procedures, maintain specimen inventory, documentation for publication, help with manuscripts and grant proposals, prepares data, graphs, tables, and charts to document experimental results for publication, analyzes and interpret experimental data, compiles results, and writes reports and summaries of findings. •    Meet or communicate by e-mail with principal investigator on a regular basis to plan experiments, troubleshoot problems, and discuss results. •    Assist in recruiting new lab members by informing them about the lab and your research. •    Help maintain reagents or equipment in the laboratory with specific jobs, which might include tasks like making buffers, 70% ethanol, etc •    Maintain and operate standard laboratory equipment required for specific tests. •    Prepare culture media, chemicals, reagents and solutions. •    Contribute to a collegial and inclusive environment for the laboratory. •    Work with collaborators at UPMC Hillman and Children’s Hospital. Physical Effort Moderate physical effort Moderate physical effort required. May be required to stand/move for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am-5 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided Yes Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005700": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005700) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005700) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician Med-Radiation Oncology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005700 ) Seeking a research technician to work in a dynamic and fast-paced Translational Oncology research laboratory at the Hillman Cancer Center of the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center. The candidate is expected to work independently following the guidance of a physician-scientist in the Department of Radiation Oncology and will carry out experiments investigating pediatric brain tumor cancer biology and radiopharmaceutical therapy.  Roles will include cell culture, in vitro cell viability assays, flow cytometry, Western Blot, mouse work including orthotopic tumor implantation, treating tumor-bearing mice with radiation, monitoring tumor growth, and harvesting mouse tissues for further analyses. The candidate is also expected to work with collaborators at the Hillman Cancer Center and the SaMIRA radiopharmacuetical core to perform radiopharmaceutical therapy, SPECT/PET/CT imaging, and MRI and image analysis. Experience in doing basic science research and cell culture is required more specific training will be provided. Good written and communication skills are required. Candidates should have at least a Bachelors of Science in biology, biochemistry, neuroscience, bioengineering, biomedical engineering, and one year of post-graduate research experience. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions Duties may include some or all the following: •    Maintain an organized and complete lab notebook of experiments that are performed. •    Propagate cells in cell culture and perform in vitro viability assays and clonogenic assays. •    Perform flow cytometry on murine and human cells (with Hillman flow core) to characterize surface receptor expression. •    Perform Western blots to characterize cell lines, tumor tissues, and mouse tissues. •    Extract DNA and RNA from mouse tumor tissue for next generation sequencing. •    Orthotopic injection of tumor cell lines into mice (training will be provided) •    In-vivo bioluminescence imaging to track tumor growth •    Collecting tumor tissue from mice. •    Treatment of tumor bearing mice with radiation using both external beam and/or radiopharmaceutical therapy •    Work with Pitt’s advanced imaging core to deliver brain specimens for MRI studies. •    Work with the SaMIRA imaging facility at Hillman to design novel radiopharmaceutical therapies •    Work with the SaMIRA imaging facility at Hillman to perform SPECT/PET/CT imaging. •    Work with the SaMIRA imaging facility at Hillman to perform image analysis •    Meet or communicate by e-mail with principal investigator on a regular basis to plan experiments, troubleshoot problems, and discuss results. •    Assist in recruiting new lab members by informing them about the lab and your research. •    Help maintain reagents or equipment in the laboratory with specific jobs, which might include tasks like making buffers, 70% ethanol, etc •    Maintain and operate standard laboratory equipment required for specific tests. •    Prepare culture media, chemicals, reagents and solutions. •    Assist in the development and optimization of new research procedures and techniques. •    Contribute to a collegial and inclusive environment for the laboratory. •    Work with collaborators at UPMC Hillman and Children’s Hospital. Physical Effort Moderate physical effort Moderate physical effort required. May be required to stand/move for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am-5 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided Yes Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004473": {
      "title": "Quality Assurance and Training Supervisor",
      "description": "Job Description - Quality Assurance and Training Supervisor (26004473) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Quality Assurance and Training Supervisor (26004473) Job Description Quality Assurance and Training Supervisor Facilities Management AVC - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004473 ) Job Summary Devises and implements comprehensive training programs and ensures compliance with goals and policies. Delivers training, supports employees, and resolves issues. Tracks various customer metrics and prepares reports. Monitors departmental activities and identifies discrepancies in practices. Essential Functions Devises and implements comprehensive training programs for use across the department. Ensures all training programs align with departmental goals and policies. Delivers training to employees in an effective and efficient manner. Supports employees through training processes. Attends to problems as they arise. Tracks and reports various customer metrics. Prepares reports; shares findings with upper-level management. Monitors departmental activities for accuracy and quality. Identifies potential discrepancies in practices. Escalates issues when necessary. Develops corrective action plans when quality standards aren't met, and follows up to confirm resolution Identify root causes of recurring deficiencies (staffing, equipment, scheduling, training gaps) and recommend fixes. Pilot and evaluate new cleaning products, equipment, or methods for efficiency/quality gains. Physical Effort Extended walking/standing. Climbing stairs. Bending, reaching, kneeling. Occasional lifting/carrying.Visual acuity. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Quality Assurance & Training Supervisor Job Family Campus Operations Job Sub-Family Facilities Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday through Friday 7:30am to 4pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
