    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005949": {
      "title": "Dispensary Clerk",
      "description": "Job Description - Dispensary Clerk (26005949) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Dispensary Clerk (26005949) Job Description Dispensary Clerk Dent Med-Dental Instruments - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005949 ) Job Summary Issues dental instruments and equipment to dental students utilizing proper sterilizations protocols and an electronic database. Inspects cassettes for missing instruments and stocks dispensary and operatories. Assists clinic staff and assists in dental sterilization. Essential Functions Job Summary: The Dispensary Clerk’s primary responsibility is distributing instruments and supplies in our DMD student dental clinic, where D3 and D4 student dentists treat patients with oversight and direction from faculty. As a member of the broader Instrument Management Service staff, the incumbent will also be expected to learn and participate in all phases of preventive maintenance of instrumentation and essential steps of sterilization. Essential Skills:· Managing instruments and supplies, basic computer tasks. This position requires basic computer skills, strong service orientation, and the ability to work as an effective member of a team. Experience in healthcare and knowledge of standard sterilization practices within a clinic setting are desirable, though not mandatory. Job Responsibilities: Perform duties in Central Sterile, following infection control practice· Maintain instrumentation and operate sterilization equipment. Issue instruments to dental students in the assigned clinic module, electronically. Checking cassettes out and back in through the electronic health record dispensary module. Check cassettes for missing instruments and engages promptly with the student dentist to minimize loss. Maintain optimal level of supplies of other necessary items to ensure ready availability with minimal waste.  Dispenses supplies as needed. Use downtime to assist IMS projects or other duties as assigned by supervisor.  Perform other duties assigned related to the operations of the department. Physical Effort Incumbent will be required to move around within building and in dispensary to access necessary supplies and instruments. Limited lifting may be required. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Dental Dispensary Assistant Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Clinical Dental Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00am-4:30pm Fall & Spring  ONLY Tuesday 8:30am-5:00pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $16.50 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001274": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator (26001274) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator (26001274) Job Description Clinical Research Nurse Coordinator Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26001274 ) Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Supports clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews lab results, patient data, and lab specimens; administers medications and protocol-specific treatments. Performs general laboratory duties and specialized nursing duties, trains new staff, and ensures regulatory adherence. Essential Functions • Coordinates clinical research projects and drug trials. Assesses patients for qualification/enrollment in research projects and subject groups. Implements research protocols. Monitors patient assessments. • Collects and reviews lab results; monitors results for adverse reactions. • Collects patient data, including medical histories and physical assessments. Maintains and enters data into databases/logs in a timely and accurate manner. • Performs general laboratory duties including, but not limited to, monitors supply inventory, monitors temperatures of freezers and refrigerators, cleans equipment, and disposes of biological waste. Performs specialized nursing duties such as arterial puncture, venipuncture, and operation of electronic monitoring equipment; assists with surgical and/or invasive procedures. • Administers treatment and/or medication in accordance with research protocol. • Collects, prepares, and processes lab specimens. • Ensures all protocol and regulatory standards adherence. • Participates in the development of internal review board submissions as requested. • Collaborates with multiple investigators, sponsors, and research coordinators. • Assists with training of new staff and ongoing guidance of newer staff. Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Nurse II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research - Nursing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor of Science in Nursing Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification RN Work Schedule This position will require flexibility with shift/hours and will be required to work on the evenings and weekends. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005736": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician III",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician III (26005736) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician III (26005736) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician III Med-Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005736 ) The Starzl Transplantation Institute at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine is seeking a dedicated and highly motivated Laboratory Research Technician III to join our research team. Master's degree preferred. Job Summary Performs a variety of independent laboratory work and experiments such as determining experimental protocols and preparation of specimens and cultures. Prepares reports of findings subsequent to compilation and analyzation. Oversees specimen inventory. Develops documentation for publication; crafts manuscripts and grant proposals. Essential Functions The incumbent will be responsible for coordinating human studies, running flow cytometry on human PBMCs, learning and performing human tissue staining (IHC/IF), RNA and DNA extraction. Will also be responsible for managing the lab. Physical Effort Must be able to sit, stand and walk for prolonged periods of time.  Must be able to see and have use of both hands. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30am - 5pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005857": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Scientist (26005857) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Scientist (26005857) Job Description Research Scientist Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005857 ) This position is for the Division of Genetic and Genomic Medicine within the Department of Pediatrics.  This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Conducts independent scientific research projects from inception to presentation. Prepares and crafts various documentations of research results into manuscripts, proposals, grant applications, and presentations. Trains undergraduates and research technicians. Manages laboratory policies and coordinates project development in collaboration with other specialists. Essential Functions • Conducts independent scientific research projects from inception to presentation, including planning, organizing, conducting experiments, assessing protocol feasibility, processing and analyzing data, and conference presentations. • Prepares manuscripts, research proposals, articles, grant applications, work for publications, and presentations based on research results. • Trains undergraduates and/or research technicians. • Recommends, drafts, and manages laboratory policies and procedures. • Facilitates work and project development in collaboration with other industry and academic specialists. Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Scientist Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Science Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Professional Doctorate Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Position will require flexibility with shift/hours; evenings and weekends possible depending on cell culture and mice experiment needs. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005950": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Technician (26005950) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Technician (26005950) Job Description Laboratory Technician Med-Orthopedic Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005950 ) In lieu of educational requirements, additional years of relevant experience may be considered, as per University guidelines. The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery is committed to equity, diversity, and inclusion. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will be considered without regard to race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender, sexual orientation, age, disability, or veteran status. The University offers comprehensive benefits to eligible employees. Aside from our great health plans, we have a generous match to our 403B retirement savings plan, vacation, sick and personal days. We have Paid Winter Recess (Christmas to New Year’s Day). Finally, we offer generous educational benefits for eligible employees, their dependents and spouse/domestic partner. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions This is an ideal position for individuals looking to complete a gap year of research prior to medical school. This is a full-time position and in-person work is required (no remote work). Must have previous experience working on research involving direct interactions with humans- either in a laboratory or in clinic setting. Must attach a resume or the application will not be considered. -assist in human motion capture data collection -use custom data processing software to track bone motion in radiographic images -create 3D bone and soft tissue models from medical images (CT and MRI) -Organize data and results in spreadsheet -Review literature related to ongoing research Physical Effort Must be able to work at a desk for extended periods of time (sitting or standing); must be able to lift 50 pounds, must be able to navigate through a room lined with wires and cables on the floor without assistance or tripping. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F 8-4 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005827": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Scientist (26005827) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Scientist (26005827) Job Description Research Scientist Med-Neurology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005827 ) The University of Pittsburgh, Department of Neurology , would like to hire a Research Scientist. We are seeking applications for an upcoming project investigating divergent and convergent mechanisms of Parkinson’s disease following exposure to disease relevant environmental toxicants. The successful candidate will be expected to design and carry out properly powered in vitro assays using various cell lines under direct supervision of the PI. The candidate will also be expected to analyze / graph data and prepares data figures and assist in grant writing. Interact closely with all lab members. This candidate will receive on the job training though prior cell culture experience and invivo handling is preferred. Tasks the scientist will perform include, cell culture maintenance, live imaging microscopy, RTqPCR, and western blotting. Job Summary Conducts independent scientific research projects from inception to presentation. Prepares and crafts various documentations of research results into manuscripts, proposals, grant applications, and presentations. Trains undergraduates and research technicians. Manages laboratory policies and coordinates project development in collaboration with other specialists. Essential Functions RS performs assays and keeps apprised of technical innovations and implement new techniques when appropriate. RS analyzes and graphs data generated by themselves or others in the lab, prepares data figures and illustrations for presentations and publications, and presents data at lab meetings and conferences. RS also writes manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals, writes scientific abstracts for conferences, and assists in grant proposal writing. RS reviews literature and keeps the laboratory reference database updated. RS interacts closely with the PI, supervises and trains technicians and undergraduate students in the lab, and communicates with collaborators. Knowledge of in vivo rodent work, molecular biology (generating new plasmids, cell lines, sh/siRNA, CRISPR Cas9 technologies), cell culture (cell line, maintenance and engineering), resonant scanning confocal microscopy, live imaging microscopy are essential. Experience preferred in mitochondrial specific assays (eg. Seahorse), RTqPCR, Western Blotting, in situ proximity ligation, development of plate reader assays. Physical Effort Must be able to get around a university setting. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Scientist Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Science Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Professional Doctorate Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule M-F, 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005900": {
      "title": "Research Facilitator",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Facilitator (26005900) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Facilitator (26005900) Job Description Research Facilitator Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005900 ) The HEALing Measures Center, supported by grant 1RM1DA059395-01, is dedicated to advancing the measurement, quality, and equity of care in community opioid treatment programs (OTPs) through the sustained implementation of measurement-based care (MBC). Our comprehensive approach involves collaborative efforts with community partners to improve tools, enhance measurement quality, and bridge critical research gaps in the real-world application of evidence-based measurement and systems. We will co-design the implementation blueprint with key community partners (e.g., policy makers, payers, OTP providers) that will serve as the foundation for a stepped-wedge, hybrid type II effectiveness-implement. 1. Collaboration and Stakeholder Engagement: Excellent communication skills to foster collaborative relationships with community partners, policymakers, payers, and OTP providers to facilitate successful implementation and dissemination of research findings. 2. Project Management: Maintain alignment of the project's overarching goals and timelines with community partnership engagement, research activities, etc. This includes administrative tasks such as overseeing various organizational, managerial, and logistical aspects of the research projects including timeline/milestone tracking and adhering to IRB protocols. 3. Implementation: Execute the implementation activities with fidelity to the implementation blueprint, including trainings, technical assistance, etc. 4. Data Collection and Analysis: Experience with conducting and analyzing qualitative interviews, collecting survey data, etc. 5. Dissemination and Reporting: Support the preparation and dissemination of findings to local partners as well as through publications, presentations, and other channels, contributing to ongoing measurement quality initiatives and reporting within Pennsylvania. Job Summary Supports researchers through all aspects of the research process and oversees the development, creation, and implementation of reports, processes, and guidelines. Creates and leads research design training programs and identifies needed resources and services. Creates development strategies. Maintains databases and provides guidance and support. Essential Functions Requires the ability to visualize a computer screen, to work with computer hardware and software, to communicate verbally and in writing, and to use a phone. The candidate must have strong working knowledge of English. Physical Effort Position is mostly sedentary work. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Facilitator Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005929": {
      "title": "Director, Staff Community and Inclusion",
      "description": "Job Description - Director, Staff Community and Inclusion (26005929) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director, Staff Community and Inclusion (26005929) Job Description Director, Staff Community and Inclusion Student Affairs DEI - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005929 ) Develops and implements initiatives that strengthen employee engagement, foster an inclusive and welcoming workplace, and build community across the Division of Student Affairs. Coordinates divisional community-building activities and celebrations, supports employee engagement initiatives, and collaborates with departments to promote a positive organizational culture in which all employees feel connected, supported, and valued. Serves as a resource to divisional leadership on workplace climate, staff engagement, and organizational effectiveness. Required Skill Sets Employee Engagement & Culture Building — Demonstrated ability to design and implement programs that increase staff engagement, morale, and sense of belonging within a large, multi-department organization. Inclusion & Belonging — Working knowledge of inclusive workplace practices and the ability to foster a welcoming environment for staff from a wide range of backgrounds and experiences. Event & Program Planning — Skill in planning, coordinating, and executing community-building activities, celebrations, and recognition events for a large staff population. Relationship Building & Collaboration — Ability to build trust and partner effectively with directors, senior leaders, and staff across departments to advance shared culture and engagement goals. Organizational Climate Assessment — Ability to gather input (e.g., surveys, listening sessions) and translate findings into actionable recommendations for divisional leadership. Master's Degree preferred Job Summary Executes strategic alignment, long-term planning, operational planning, and management oversight of major college, campus, or University-wide student affairs functions. Establishes the direction, goals, implementation strategy, evaluation means, student initiatives, and policies of the department. Maintains responsibility for budgetary matters. Directs effective communications, promotions, and public relations for the department. Essential Functions Develop and implement staff engagement and inclusion initiatives. Plan and coordinate community-building activities and celebrations for staff. Collaborate with departments to strengthen workplace culture. Assess workplace climate and advise leadership on engagement. Support staff recruitment, retention, and collaboration efforts. Coordinate communications and resources for engagement initiatives. Serve on divisional committees supporting culture and staff success. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Student Affairs Director Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004502": {
      "title": "Lab Manager",
      "description": "Job Description - Lab Manager (26004502) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Lab Manager (26004502) Job Description Lab Manager Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004502 ) Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Manages day-to-day laboratory operations while ensuring compliance with safety regulations and best practices. Works with, adapts, and installs scientific equipment in research laboratories. Collaborates on routine projects and procedures. Manages inventory and equipment and performs budget functions. Essential Functions • Manages daily laboratory operations of a division, department, function, or program, including conducting and overseeing quality assurance and quality control. • Collaborates to develop routine projects and procedures. Researches, evaluates, and repairs specialized and routine products and equipment as needed. • Maintains and adapts scientific equipment for experimental needs of the department. Troubleshoots, installs, and adapts electronic devices and other samples for research investigations. • Confers with researchers and faculty concerning research needs and methods. • Prepares budget requests and manages approved budget. • Keeps accurate and timely data logbooks. • Managing the mammalian specimen colony is a critical part of this position. • Ensures compliance with all applicable regulations for waste disposal; acts as department safety officer Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Manager I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule This position may be required to work on the evenings and weekends but this will only occasionally happen depending on the experiments designed. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
