    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004081": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator, Student Success Team (SST)",
      "description": "Job Description - Project Coordinator, Student Success Team (SST) (26004081) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Coordinator, Student Success Team (SST) (26004081) Job Description Project Coordinator, Student Success Team (SST) Office of the SVC and Provost - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004081 ) The Student Success Team within the University of Pittsburgh's Office of the Provost is seeking a detail-oriented and collaborative professional for the role of Project Coordinator on the Student Success Team in the Office of the Provost. Our mission is to “advocate and create opportunities for students by providing a system of academic support to boost retention, persistence, and graduation.” High School Diploma/GED required; Bachelor’s degree preferred. Two (2) years’ experience in administration, project management, budget, and/or business operations required. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, participating in a team environment, and knowledge of MS tools is a plus. Job Summary Serves in an administrative capacity and provides administrative support to the project manager and other team members. Assists with fiscal management and compliance with federal regulations and the contracts. Manages day-to-day office operations and interacts with key stakeholders. Essential Functions The Project Coordinator will serve in an administrative capacity and provide administrative support to team leadership. They will also assist with fiscal management, grant compliance, and contracts; manage office operations (correspondence, notetaking, calendaring, scheduling meetings, processing orders, travel arrangements); interact with key stakeholders; other duties as assigned. Physical Effort Must be able to sit and stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Project Coordinator Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Program & Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday- Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005883": {
      "title": "Major Gifts Officer",
      "description": "Job Description - Major Gifts Officer (26005883) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Major Gifts Officer (26005883) Job Description Major Gifts Officer Medical and Health Sciences Foundation - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005883 ) The Division of Philanthropic & Alumni Engagement (PAE) builds relationships with donors, alumni, and constituents to advance the missions of the University of Pittsburgh and UPMC. Through philanthropy and alumni engagement, PAE supports innovation, research, education, and patient care. UPMC Hillman Cancer Center seeks a Major Gifts Officer (MGO) to develop and implement fundraising strategies that increase philanthropic support for cancer research and clinical care initiatives. Reporting to the Executive Director of Development, the MGO will identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward major gift prospects and donors while advancing the Center's fundraising priorities. Responsibilities Manage a portfolio of 100+ major gift donors and prospects with capacities beginning at $100,000, including seven-figure prospects. Achieve annual fundraising goals beginning at $1 million, with growth expectations over time. Develop and execute donor cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship plans. Conduct donor visits, meetings, and engagement activities to build lasting relationships. Identify and qualify new major gift prospects. Collaborate with physicians, researchers, clinicians, faculty, and volunteer leaders to connect donor interests with funding opportunities. Prepare proposals, stewardship reports, donor correspondence, and other fundraising materials. Maintain accurate records, donor strategies, and activity reports in Salesforce Affinaquest CRM. Support fundraising events, meetings, and regional travel as needed. Collaboration The MGO will work closely with senior leaders, including the Director and Chairman of UPMC Hillman Cancer Center, University advancement leadership, faculty, researchers, clinicians, and volunteer leaders. The position will also engage members of the UPMC Hillman Cancer Center Council and other key volunteers in fundraising efforts. Qualifications Experience in major gift fundraising, development, or related relationship-based roles. Strong communication, relationship-building, and organizational skills. Ability to work independently, manage multiple priorities, and exercise sound judgment. Attention to detail and commitment to achieving fundraising goals. Dedication to the mission of UPMC Hillman Cancer Center and advancing cancer research and patient care. Why Join Us? Impactful Work: Play a crucial role in supporting the University's mission. Collaborative Environment: Work within a supportive, innovative, and dynamic team. Professional Growth: Opportunities for continuous learning, professional development, and career advancement. Competitive Benefits: Enjoy a comprehensive benefits package, including health insurance, retirement plans, and paid time off. Ready to make a difference? Learn more about PAE and apply today. Join us in shaping the future of education, research, and healthcare at the University of Pittsburgh! Job Summary Plans, implements, and manages fundraising programs for assigned area of responsibility; develops proposals and coordinates fundraising efforts within the department; and identifies, cultivates, stewards, and solicits current and potential donors. Collaborates with executive leadership, leadership, and faculty on strategic initiatives and campaign management. Crafts major donor recognition collateral and recruits and leads volunteer solicitors. Essential Functions Cumulatively raise at least $1,000,000 each fiscal year from assigned clinical divisions through direct cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship; cultivate relationships with clinical physicians, researchers, surgeons, and other medical personnel; and design comprehensive solicitation programs that generate financial support for Center goals. Visit prospects face-to-face; accompany volunteers and internal leaders to prospect meetings; prepare proposals following cultivation meetings; provide follow-through via successful completion of solicitations; and develop and implement fundraising concepts that support divisional fundraising needs. Serve as a primary advisor to identify and cultivate leadership annual gifts from individuals by conducting meetings, making presentations to constituent groups, developing informational materials, and performing related activities. Train on and regularly use the Salesforce Affinaquest CRM database to document fundraising contacts, conversations, proposals, and strategies. Physical Effort Light - Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Major Gifts Officer III Job Family Philanthropy & Engagement Job Sub-Family Major & Principal Gifts Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 6 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Valid driver's license\n\nPrimarily local/regional travel- as much as is necessary to work a portfolio and cultivate donors. Some instances of further domestic travel (VWA, NACCDO annual conference, and donor work as needed) Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005835": {
      "title": "Financial Administrator",
      "description": "Job Description - Financial Administrator (26005835) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Financial Administrator (26005835) Job Description Financial Administrator SHRS-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005835 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences (SHRS) is a nationally renowned leader in the field of health care education, research, and clinical practice preparation. With 14 different disciplines related to health and rehabilitative care, SHRS shapes future generations of health care professionals—therapists, counselors, advocates, scientists, providers, and practitioners—trained to serve the needs of all people regardless of background, levels of health, or mobility. We are built on a legacy of academic excellence and innovation and fueled by passionate educators and researchers, allowing us to meet the health care and rehabilitation needs of today and drive meaningful change in the future. Learn how bold moves SHRS. https://www.shrs.pitt.edu/about/how-bold-moves-shrs The Financial Administrator provides centralized financial administration services to assigned departments within the School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences (SHRS) under the direction of the SHRS Office of Dean Finance Director. The Financial Administrator serves as the primary financial point of contact for assigned departments, delivering consistent, high-quality financial support across account reconciliation, budget monitoring, purchasing compliance, payroll oversight, and financial reporting. The position also supports Dean's Office financial operations. This position provides dedicated financial support across SHRS departments with the Financial Administrator maintaining strong working relationships with department chairs, faculty, and administrative staff. The position functions with a high degree of independence on routine matters and exercises sound judgment in identifying issues requiring escalation. Job Summary Prepares and analyzes financial data for senior leadership in budgetary and financial planning. Tracks and analyzes budgetary developments. Reviews financial and budgetary proposals and assists in preparing complex reports and statements. Essential Functions Account Management & Reconciliation: Monthly reconciliation of operating, continuing ed, discretionary, and assigned accounts against trackers/POs/expense reports; investigate discrepancies; distribute monthly account analysis reports; enter forecasts vs. actuals. Budget & Reporting: Monitor budgets, flag variances; prepare fund transfers (NSCT/SWCT); support annual budget prep; assist Dean's Office financial reporting. Payroll & Effort: Verify payroll registers against salary worksheets/Fiscal Panther effort data; maintain SPAR changes; support quarterly grant-ending reviews; assist effort certification. Purchasing Compliance: Review/approve Concur expense reports and Panther Express transactions for accuracy/policy compliance; manage OneCard program (approvals, limits, reconciliation). Fund & Scholarship Admin: Monitor scholarship/discretionary balances; maintain principal/interest trackers; coordinate with scholarship committees; process awards in PittFund$Me. Cost Center Oversight: Support continuing ed account reconciliation and labor/income review; manage Major Fee proposals, tracking, and usage reviews. Compliance & Admin: Complete SOX questionnaire; support audits; manage capital asset inventory; maintain financial records; track overload payments for compliance. Dean's Office Support: Support cross-functional financial projects; provide cross-coverage with other financial staff. Physical Effort Must be able to sit for prolonged periods of time and lift no more than 25 pounds. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Financial Analyst II - Budget Job Family Finance & Procurement Job Sub-Family Financial Planning & Analysis Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Required: Bachelor's in finance/accounting/business; 3+ yrs financial admin/budgeting; account reconciliation, budget monitoring, reporting experience; strong Excel; organized, confidential, good communicator.\n\nPreferred: Higher ed/academic medical experience; knows Pitt systems (Fiscal Panther, PRISM, Panther Express, Concur); scholarship/endowment fund experience; knows Pitt fiscal policies. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005917": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Job Description - Administrative Assistant II (26005917) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administrative Assistant II (26005917) Job Description Administrative Assistant II Dent Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005917 ) Since 1896 the School of Dental Medicine has been educating students to take their places among the best dental practitioners in our region and across the country.  Each day the school's faculty and staff contribute to its mission to advance the future of dental medicine through teaching, research and service. In addition to being a great place to work the University offers robust benefits including: * 11 Paid Holidays, Paid Vacation, Sick and Personal Days *  Additional Paid Time off (Winter Recess) during the period between Christmas and the New Year  * Paid Parental Leave *  Educational benefits for eligible employees, their dependents and spouse/domestic partner * Above-average Employer Contribution towards Medical, Prescription Drug, Vision, Life, STD, and LTD Insurance plans * A robust retirement savings plan option.  Including 100% match on employee contributions of 3-8%(150% after vesting) and enhanced match for those nearing retirement * Free PRT bus pass. Job Summary Performs administrative assistant support work of moderate complexity. Essential Functions Front desk receptionist duties at multi-provider dental clinic responsible for managing front desk area, including scheduling appointments, greeting patients, updating patient information, collecting required documentation, taking cash and credit card payments, maintaining patient charts/EHR, and assist with charge submission and follow up as needed.  Scheduling post ops as needed as well. Confirming appointments. Controlling the patient flow between the waiting room and clinic area. Providing clerical support for the department, including correspondence and other assignments assigned by the supervisor. Physical Effort Position is front office position which requires sitting for prolonged periods of time. Very minimal lifting 5-10 pounds; organizing supplies and inventories. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Administrative Assistant II Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005865": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Administrative Assistant (26005865) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administrative Assistant (26005865) Job Description Administrative Assistant Falk Library - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005865 ) Qualifications Prior administrative or office support experience, preferably in a higher education or library setting. Familiarity with University administrative policies and financial systems preferred. Demonstrated attention to detail and accuracy. Proven organizational and time management skills, with the ability to balance multiple priorities independently. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with an ability to build productive working relationships across diverse stakeholder groups. Job Summary Supports senior level roles in a wide variety of complex administrative and office functions as well as specialized technical support for academic or administrative departments. Essential Functions The Administrative Assistant provides essential operational, clerical, and data management support to the HSLS Director’s Office, contributing to the smooth functioning of Falk Library leadership and day-to-day operations. In this role, the incumbent maintains accurate records, verifies data, organizes documentation, and assists with routine reporting and project tracking in support of library initiatives. Serving as a knowledgeable resource on University, Health Sciences, and HSLS policies and best practices, the position plays a key role in triaging and resolving administrative requests and directing inquiries to the appropriate office or personnel. Key Responsibilities Scheduling & Meeting Coordination: Manage calendars and coordinate meetings for library leadership; provide internal and external scheduling and logistical support for library-wide meetings. Purchasing & Financial Processing: Process departmental and library acquisition purchases; reconcile monthly expense reports and Vincent card payments in accordance with University policy. Invoice & Travel Management: Monitor, verify, and process vendor invoices; arrange staff travel logistics and process reimbursement requests efficiently. Facilities & Space Management: Serve as the primary liaison and point of contact for facilities, space management, and housekeeping matters. Inventory & Office Logistics: Monitor and maintain office and operational supply inventory, coordinating replenishment as needed. General Administrative Support: Perform a wide range of administrative, recordkeeping, and filing functions independently. Assist with special projects and other duties as assigned by HSLS leadership. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Administrative Assistant III Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 - 5 Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $20.50 to $25.64 per hour. Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004879": {
      "title": "Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center)",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center) (26004879) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center) (26004879) Job Description Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center) University Child Development Center - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004879 ) The Assistant Teacher will work in an early childhood classroom at the University Child Development Center with children ranging in age from six weeks through five years of age. The position involves a collaborative effort in supporting the functions of the classroom under the supervision of a Head Teacher and an Associate Teacher. The Assistant Teacher is responsible for supporting daily activities and programming in the classroom, interaction with and supervising a group of children and maintaining daily communication with families. Some supervision of University students is required. Assistant Teachers are required to maintain 12 hours of professional development annually during their employment and maintain all DHS, NAEYC, Keystone STARS requirements. They are also required to attend all five professional development days at UCDC annually. Candidates must meet one of the following: High school diploma or GED and 30 credit hours from an accredited college or university in early childhood education, child development, special education, elementary education, or the human services field , High school diploma or GED, including 600 or more hours of secondary training as described in §3270.31(c) High school diploma or GED, 15 credit hours from an accredited college or university in one of the above fields, and 1 year of experience with children High school diploma or GED and completion of a post-secondary training curriculum described in §3270.31(c) High school diploma or GED and 2 years of experience with children Job Summary Supports head and associate teachers in a child development center. Prepares fine and gross motor activities for effective child development. Maintains a safe classroom conducive to learning and engagement. Guides student and temporary workers. Essential Functions The Assistant Teacher supports the Head Teacher in the planning and implementation of a child development program for a class of children. Incumbent may act as supervisor when the Head Teacher and Associate Teacher are not in the classroom. Physical Effort The work involves occasional, and at times sustained performance of heavier physical tasks such as traversing over rough or uneven surfaces, bending, stooping, traversing space quickly, and lifting and/or carrying 40-pound children. Work exposes the employee to potentially non disabling injuries or illnesses. Duties require regular exposure to the outside. Bloodborne and airborne pathogens present a potential hazard. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Assistant Teacher Job Family Child Development Job Sub-Family University Child Development Center Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Candidate must have a high school diploma/GED and two years of verified experience with young children OR a high school diploma/GED, 15 credits in a human service field and one year of verified experience with young children. Work Schedule M-F, 7:30-5:30 (varied shifts) Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
