    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005805": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005805) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005805) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician Med-Neurology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005805 ) The University of Pittsburgh Department of Neurology is interested in hiring a Laboratory Research Technician to join a translational neuromuscular research group. The laboratory technician will perform a variety of independent laboratory work including executing experimental protocols, collecting and analyzing data, and generating research figures for neurodegenerative diseases such as Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis and Frontotemporal Dementia. The technician will assist with inventory, ordering, and training of fellow lab members. To perform these tasks well, meticulous record keeping of research data and excellent interpersonal and communication skills are prerequisites. Following training from the principal investigator and/or senior research staff, the research assistant is expected to perform tasks with minor supervision. A qualified candidate should have at least a bachelor’s degree in biological science or equivalent and at least 2 years’ experience in a biomedical research setting. Candidates with demonstrated expertise in human iPSC culture, immunofluorescence microscopy, molecular biology and murine colony management will be preferred. This is a full-time, in-person position; experimental timelines (cell and tissue culture, live-cell imaging, and animal work) require consistent daily presence and occasional flexibility outside standard hours. Job Summary Performs a variety of independent laboratory work and experiments such as determining experimental protocols and preparation of specimens and cultures. Prepares reports of findings subsequent to compilation and analyzation. Oversees specimen inventory. Develops documentation for publication; crafts manuscripts and grant proposals. Essential Functions 1. Assist with experimental procedures, data collection, and analysis (80%): • Perform a variety of experimental procedures independently after training. Procedures may include molecular biology (molecular cloning, PCR, genotyping, & RT-PCR), biochemistry (western blotting, immunoprecipitation, & proteomics), and cell biology (cell/tissue culture, immunofluorescence staining, & confocal microscopy). • Analyze research data and generate graphs using tools such as GraphPad Prism, MATLAB, Python, Fiji, and Imaris. • Generate scientific figures using BioRender and Adobe Illustrator. • Maintain a detailed lab notebook and records of experimental procedures. • Maintain a detailed archive of digital research records using the laboratory server.2. Oversee mouse colony management, breeding, genotyping, and record-keeping (10% effort): • Maintain and update records of the animal colony. • Coordinate genotyping and weaning. • Communicate with vivarium staff and veterinarians as needed to ensure animal wellbeing. Physical Effort Must be able to get around a university setting. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F, 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005733": {
      "title": "Histology Laboratory Manager 1 -PBC",
      "description": "Job Description - Histology Laboratory Manager 1 -PBC (26005733) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Histology Laboratory Manager 1 -PBC (26005733) Job Description Histology Laboratory Manager 1 -PBC Health Sciences Core Research Facilities - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005733 ) The Pitt Biospecimen Core Histology Lab is an institutional research resource that supports University of Pittsburgh and UPMC faculty through high-quality tissue processing, paraffin embedding, sectioning, staining support, tissue microarray construction, and related histology services. Located within Shadyside Hospital, with satellite pick-up and drop-off stations at Scaife Hall and Magee-Women’s Hospital, the lab supports research activity across the University’s campus and affiliated clinical research sites.   The Research Histology Technician – Laboratory Manager I supports the full lifecycle of histology laboratory operations, from project accessioning, cassette labeling, slide printing, processing, embedding, routine and frozen sectioning, and project compilation to distribution and submission for whole slide imaging through the Digital Pathology Resource Center. The incumbent works independently and collaboratively on routine and complex research projects, applying histological guidelines and customer requirements while maintaining workflow, turnaround time, sample integrity, and service quality.mmThis role also provides technical and operational support for specialized laboratory workflows, including gross dissection, review of control tissues for histochemical staining, immunohistochemical staining, TUNEL assays, and construction of tissue microarrays from submitted samples and identification lists. The incumbent uses laboratory-integrated software to accession projects, support billing accuracy, track pending work, maintain supply and chemical inventories, program and maintain equipment, monitor chemical waste disposal, and assist laboratory management with troubleshooting, process improvement, and workflow enhancements, order and manage laboratory supplies. Success in this position requires strong attention to detail, effective communication with management, team members, and customers, sound organizational judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a high-volume research service environment. Job Summary Manages day-to-day laboratory operations while ensuring compliance with safety regulations and best practices. Works with, adapts, and installs scientific equipment in research laboratories. Collaborates on routine projects and procedures. Manages inventory and equipment and performs budget functions. Essential Functions The Pitt Biospecimen Core Histology Lab is an institutional research resource that supports University of Pittsburgh and UPMC faculty through high-quality tissue processing, paraffin embedding, sectioning, staining support, tissue microarray construction, and related histology services. Located within Shadyside Hospital, with satellite pick-up and drop-off stations at Scaife Hall and Magee-Women’s Hospital, the lab supports research activity across the University’s campus and affiliated clinical research sites.   The Research Histology Technician – Laboratory Manager I supports the full lifecycle of histology laboratory operations, from project accessioning, cassette labeling, slide printing, processing, embedding, routine and frozen sectioning, and project compilation to distribution and submission for whole slide imaging through the Digital Pathology Resource Center. The incumbent works independently and collaboratively on routine and complex research projects, applying histological guidelines and customer requirements while maintaining workflow, turnaround time, sample integrity, and service quality.mmThis role also provides technical and operational support for specialized laboratory workflows, including gross dissection, review of control tissues for histochemical staining, immunohistochemical staining, TUNEL assays, and construction of tissue microarrays from submitted samples and identification lists. The incumbent uses laboratory-integrated software to accession projects, support billing accuracy, track pending work, maintain supply and chemical inventories, program and maintain equipment, monitor chemical waste disposal, and assist laboratory management with troubleshooting, process improvement, and workflow enhancements, order and manage laboratory supplies. Success in this position requires strong attention to detail, effective communication with management, team members, and customers, sound organizational judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a high-volume research service environment. Physical Effort The role also requires walking between Shadyside Hospital, Hillman Cancer Center, and The Assembly building; standing and sitting for extended periods at the bench; reading small print on cassettes, sample identification lists, and labels; and lifting up to 30 pounds.  Working under standard lab building lighting all day.  Bending and lifting to put away lab supplies. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Manager I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., schedule as set with supervisor Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005849": {
      "title": "Communications & Marketing Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Communications & Marketing Coordinator (26005849) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Communications & Marketing Coordinator (26005849) Job Description Communications & Marketing Coordinator Office of Health Sciences Engagement & Enrichment - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005849 ) The Office of Health Sciences Engagement & Enrichment (HSEE) is searching for a talented individual with a passion for building and maintaining an engaging brand through creative marketing, communications, design, and storytelling. Creating dynamic content across a variety of media is paramount to attracting and retaining faculty, students, and staff to the Health Sciences. The role of the Marketing and Communications Coordinator within the Office of Health Sciences Engagement & Enrichment encompasses the effective management of various concurrent initiatives and endeavors aimed at enhancing the branding, communication, and marketing efforts of the Office. Under the supervision of the Director of HSEE, this position will play a pivotal role in marketing various programs, HSEE events, faculty, staff, and student recruitment materials, trainings, and more. The incumbent will oversee the dissemination of digital and print-based marketing collateral through multiple channels to reach intended target audiences and stakeholders, while also executing all other facets of the overarching marketing strategy. For a more comprehensive understanding of our organization, please explore our website at https://hsee.pitt.edu/. The responsibilities of this position include but are not limited to the following: •    Coordinating marketing strategies and functions for HSEE across all platforms, channels, and strategies while maintaining adherence to strict branding and style guidelines. •    Employing writing, design, and multimedia skills to target specific audiences across a variety of digital and print media. •    Coordinating strategies and tactics that capture meaningful and actionable marketing analytics for the purposes of measuring and improving results. •    Developing content marketing campaigns in coordination with a myriad of internal and external partners and collaborators. •    Utilizing varied platforms (e.g. Campaign Monitor, Paperless Post etc.) to disseminate information and invitations. •    Managing the HSEE website and newsletter, producing timely updates, and creating new content. Ability to refine content for best practices in search engine optimization. Additional capabilities in WordPress and/or Drupal website management are preferred. •    Showcasing their commitment to understanding and being inclusive to allyship with the communities for whom we serve. Job Summary Creates written editorial content across print and electronic mediums and manages web content. Institutes procedures for timely information gathering. Ensures consistent messaging and maintains University brand and style. Essential Functions The ideal candidate will be a proactive and creative individual with strong writing skills, the ability to work effectively within a team, and be willing to contribute their knowledge and abilities to maintaining an environment where all feel welcomed and are positioned for success. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Communications & Marketing Coordinator Job Family Communications & Marketing Job Sub-Family Public Relations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $19.07 - $26.00 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Writing Sample, Media Sample Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005829": {
      "title": "Research and Evaluation Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Research and Evaluation Specialist  (26005829) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research and Evaluation Specialist  (26005829) Job Description Research and Evaluation Specialist LRDC - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005829 ) This position is at the Learning Research and Development Center (LRDC), a multi-disciplinary center for research to advance the science of learning by bringing together leading researchers in the cognitive, developmental, social, and educational sciences. The primary responsibility of this position is to assist with a longitudinal research study examining how family socioeconomic circumstances relate to differences in adolescent cardiovascular health. The study consists of a virtual health assessment with adolescent-parent dyads followed by a 7-day remote monitoring period for the collection of objective measures of health behaviors. Data collection will be primarily virtual. Job duties include contacting past participants for longitudinal study participation, scheduling study visits, administering physiological assessments, conducting health interviews, retaining accurate records and files, managing databases, building and maintaining rapport and communication with participating families. Baccalaureate degree required in psychology or related field; at least 1 year research experience in developmental or biological-health psychology; at least 1 year of experience working with adolescent children ages 16-19 years-old required; must be fluent in Spanish and English with native Spanish speakers preferred . Must have basic computer skills (Microsoft Office, email, internet search); attention to detail and ability to multi-task are required. PLEASE PROVIDE PROOF OF SPANISH LANGUAGE FLUENCY WITH APPLICATION. Job Summary Coordinates research and evaluation activities related to family engagement and child welfare and supports the design, development, and coordination of data collection in research and evaluation activities  Ensures accuracy and timelines of data collection procedures, conducts quality assurance processes, evaluates and summarizes findings and crafts conclusion reports. Recommends effective revisions of research procedures and ensures adherence to rules, policies, and regulations. Essential Functions The position will interview and conduct health assessments with parent and adolescent participants virtually, face-to-face over Zoom. The position requires fluency in Spanish and English, with strong preference for a native Spanish speaker. Physical Effort Position is predominately sedentary, and requires the incumbent to sit for prolonged periods of time.  Extensive computer use. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research & Evaluation Specialist I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Child Development Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:30-5:00, some evenings/weekends Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $32,175-$40,219 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter, Other (review job description for more details) Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
