    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005773": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator III",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator III (26005773) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator III (26005773) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator III Med-Neurological Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005773 ) Assist with daily human subjects experiments (lab or participant homes) — health monitoring, questionnaires, equipment setup for neural recording/stimulation, video monitoring, execution of experiments, Document experiments in daily test log, Run core clinical trial experiments independently; basic hardware/software troubleshooting, Provide skin care for percutaneous neuroprosthetic devices; train caregivers on skin care around devices, Supervise visitors/collaborators observing or participating in experiments, Professional interaction with research participants; Ensure personnel/equipment readiness for daily experiments; Ensure experiments conducted per University, IRB, and FDA regulations. Track milestones/deliverables for ongoing projects, facilitate meetings and information sharing, identify risks to study completion, Coordinate reporting; serve as primary point of contact for collaborators, Assist PIs/Operations Manager with visitor coordination, materials transfer agreements, data sharing agreements. Lab and physical space management (preparing, maintaining, organizing), Develop software/hardware to facilitate experiments or documentation, test all equipment/paradigms prior to participant arrival, navigate code/configuration versions using Git, Coordinate study staff/trainee coverage; maintain lab wiki and written protocols, Communicate with participants/families regarding scheduling, Schedule equipment service calls Data management: transfer data to lab server, summarize for scientific/regulatory reports, Lead efforts to fulfill data sharing requirements (funding/publication), Train new team members; evaluate readiness to lead experiments, run data analysis scripts to generate figures, liaise between participants, trainees, and regulatory/fiscal staff, provide information for scientific/regulatory reporting, Assist with participant payments/reimbursements Job Summary Prepares grant applications, manuscripts, Institutional Review Board (IRB) applications, research papers, and assists with complex research papers. Audits research studies, monitors study budgets, resolves complex data collection issues, and implements protocol-specific study recruitment plans. Trains staff and oversees student workers; leads team meetings. Monitors study budgets and orders supplies. Essential Functions The University of Pittsburgh, Department of Neurological Surgery, is hiring a Clinical Research Coordinator III. This position manages day-to-day laboratory operations while ensuring compliance with safety regulations and best practices. Works with, adapts, and installs scientific equipment in research laboratories. Collaborates on routine projects and procedures. Manages inventory and equipment and performs budget functions for clinical trial management. The incumbent will be responsible for all aspects of operating a human neuroprosthetics research laboratory focused on sensorimotor neuroscience and the restoration of motor function, as well as management of grant and project-related milestones, deliverables, and reporting requirements. Primary duties include clinical trial management and ensuring milestones are met in time as well as complying to FDA timelines and regulation, this include managing the team of researchers and engineers to ensure timely execution of clinical and scientific outcomes,  monitoring participant reports and basic health characteristics, maintaining inventory of clinical supplies, writing SOPs, tracking grant milestones and deliverables, contributing to grant/project reports, leading data sharing efforts, and ensuring experiments comply with University, IRB, and FDA policies. Preference given to candidates with human subjects clinical research experience. The job duties outlined in this job description include common job responsibilities for this title and level of jobs and are not intended to cover every duty. The University reserves the right to assign other duties to employees that are not listed in this job description. Minimum education to be considered for this position is a master's degree in engineering, biology, neuroscience, or related field or a bachelor's degree in engineering, biology, neuroscience, or related field with 2 years of relevant experience. Interested candidates, please go to Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh and use requisition #26005773 to apply for this position. The University of Pittsburgh is an Affirmative Action/ Equal Opportunity Employer and values equality of opportunity, human dignity, and diversity, EOE, including disability/vets. Physical Effort Moderate physical activity; extended standing/sitting Movement required between Mercy, MWRI, Presbyterian, Benedum, McGowan sites The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F 8:30am-5pm Occasional Mornings,  Evenings and Weekends as needed Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004935": {
      "title": "Faculty & Research Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty & Research Administrative Coordinator - IMCPL (26004935) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty & Research Administrative Coordinator - IMCPL (26004935) Job Description Faculty & Research Administrative Coordinator - IMCPL Health Sciences Core Research Facilities - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004935 ) Assist with preparation and submission of foundation, institutional, and other sponsored proposals in coordination with University pre award offices. Collect, organize, format, and maintain biosketches, curricula vitae, current and pending support documents, facilities and resources information, institutional attachments, letters of support, collaborator documents, and other proposal materials. Review proposal materials for completeness, formatting, consistency, and sponsor requirements. Maintain proposal calendars and communicate internal and sponsor deadlines. Support the faculty member’s participation as Principal Investigator, Co Principal Investigator, or Co Investigator on sponsored projects by coordinating requested documents and communications. Draft, edit, format, and route correspondence, letters of support, presentations, reports, meeting materials, and other administrative documents. Organize seminars, retreats, faculty meetings, workshops, and special events including scheduling, logistics, invitations, meeting technology, and follow up communications. Maintain organized electronic records for grants, faculty documents, meetings, billing, correspondence, and program activities. Coordinate monthly billing activities with operational teams. Maintain lab billing trackers, gather required documentation, follow up on outstanding information, identify delays, and ensure timely submission of billing. Track commitments, approvals, deliverables, and deadlines and proactively follow up to ensure timely completion. Assist with travel, reimbursements, purchasing requests, visitor coordination, and other administrative transactions. Identify opportunities to improve administrative workflows, templates, tracking systems, and communication processes. Perform other related administrative and research support duties as assigned. Job Summary Manages and monitors financial components of center research labs and coordinates repair and maintenance of equipment. Essential Functions Provides comprehensive administrative and research support to faculty leadership and associated academic, research, and operational programs. Serves as liaison among faculty, students, collaborators, research administration, and operational teams. Coordinates calendars, meetings, events, documents, communications, proposal materials, and recurring administrative deadlines. Supports preparation of foundation and other grant applications by collecting and formatting institutional documents, maintaining biosketches and investigator materials, coordinating letters of support, monitoring submission requirements, and working with University pre award personnel. Provides administrative support for the faculty member’s participation as Principal Investigator, Co Principal Investigator, or Co Investigator on sponsored projects. Coordinates monthly billing activities with program, finance, and University administrative teams. Tracks required inputs, follows up on outstanding items, and ensures billing packages are complete and submitted on schedule. Requires excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, discretion, independent judgment, and the ability to manage multiple concurrent priorities. University of Pittsburgh experience preferred.  Works under general direction and independently manages routine administrative activities, establishes priorities, monitors deadlines, and escalates issues requiring faculty or institutional decisions. Exercises judgment in coordinating schedules, communications, proposal materials, meetings, and billing workflows while following University policies and established procedures. Requires strong organizational and problem solving skills together with professionalism and discretion when handling confidential information. Ability to work independently required. Physical Effort Reading small print, bending and lifting to put away lab and office supplies. Sitting and standing for long periods.  Walking around campus to attend meetings and make deliveries when necessary.  Lifting up to 20 pounds.  Ability to work in an office cubical setting under standard lighting. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Central Fiscal Administrator Job Family Finance & Procurement Job Sub-Family Financial Planning & Analysis Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004335": {
      "title": "Animal Care Technician I",
      "description": "Job Description - Animal Care Technician I (26004335) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Animal Care Technician I (26004335) Job Description Animal Care Technician I Med-Neurobiology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004335 ) Department of Neurobiology | University of Pittsburgh Job Summary Provides animal care to laboratory animals, including feeding, watering, enrichment, health observations and basic medical treatments. Performs cage cleaning and facility sanitization procedures in accordance with standard operating procedures and maintains timely and accurate documentation. Essential Functions The Systems Neuroscience Animal Research Lab (SNARL) Animal Care Technician I will provide husbandry and care of laboratory animals with a commitment to animal welfare and well-being. The candidate will provide food, water, and enrichment, perform cage changes including cleaning and sanitizing animal housing enclosures, equipment, and room,  complete daily health observations and administer basic medical treatments, procedures, and unique diets and maintain logs documenting animal care activities and verification of environmental parameters and equipment function. Duties also include facility support tasks including laundering scrubs, performing general cleaning, sweeping, mopping, stocking supply areas, and assisting with cage wash operations. The successful candidate must consistently demonstrate positive interpersonal and customer service skills, be available to work weekends and holidays and pass the mandatory criminal and social background checks.  Vaccinations, and TB testing is required. Physical Effort Must be able to stand for extended periods of time, lift 50 pounds, push/pull heavy equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Animal Care Technician I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Animal Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday to Friday 7:00a.m. - 3:00p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004515": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician IV",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV (26004515) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV (26004515) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician IV Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004515 ) The University of Pittsburgh, Division of Rheumatology and Clinical Immunology is seeking a Laboratory Research Technician IV to work with irreplaceable human lung explants from Pitt’s transplant service to generate publication-quality data supporting single-cell/spatial analyses in fibrotic lung disease. Ideal for independent technicians seeing impactful immunology research. Required: Bachelor’s +3 years lab experience with primary human tissue processing, flow cytometry, immune cell culture, and molecular assays, data analysis experience. Job Summary Performs a variety of independent and complex laboratory work and experiments. Analyzes and interprets data, compiles results, and prepares reports. Maintains inventory, ordering, and logs. Writes manuscripts and grant proposals and prepares data visualizations. Essential Functions · Independently design/execute complex lab experiments; provide experiment design expertise · Analyze/interpret experimental data; prepare graphs/tables/charts for publication · Execute molecular (qPCR), protein (westerns), flow cytometry, immunofluorescence assays · Maintain specimen/chemical inventories, ordering, detailed lab notebooks, biosafety · Draft manuscript/grant sections; conduct literature searches to support research · Optimize protocols; troubleshoot chronic experimental issues; train junior staff · Communicate complex findings/strategies to PI Physical Effort Must be able to stand or sit for prolonged periods at the laboratory bench, use pipettes and manual manipulators for extended times, lift/move equipment up to 25 lbs, and work in a BSL-2 environment requiring PPE. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician IV Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003753": {
      "title": "Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Coordinator - PMR Neuropsychology (26003753) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Coordinator - PMR Neuropsychology (26003753) Job Description Research Coordinator - PMR Neuropsychology Med-Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003753 ) The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation (PM&R) is recruiting for a Clinical Research Coordinator to assist the research teams in the Division of Neuropsychology and Rehabilitation Psychology and the Division of Pediatric Neuropsychology. This position supports the research of senior investigators, which could include administrative activities and administration of neuropsychological assessments to study participants, as well as assisting with database development and maintenance using REDCap (Research Electronic Data Capture). This position is based out of UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh, Lawrenceville Campus and/or UPMC Mercy. The issuance of satisfactory Pennsylvania State Child Protection Clearances and TB testing will be required upon hire. (A preemployment TB test is utilized to pre-emptively prevent the spread of tuberculosis to medical and healthcare professionals as well as patients.) This is a benefits eligible position. Aside from our great health plans, we have a generous match to our 403B retirement savings plan, vacation, sick and personal days. We have Paid Winter Recess (Christmas to New Year’s Day). Finally, we offer generous educational benefits for eligible employees, their dependents and spouse/domestic partner. Job Summary Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Recruits research subjects and conducts interviews and research assessments. Essential Functions This position will require on-site work at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh campus in the Lawrenceville section of Pittsburgh as well as at UPMC Mercy. Hybrid work options will be available after successful completion of the new hire provisional period. Independently creates and carries out research studies as assigned Assists with study start-up (preparing training materials, setting up data collection platforms, ordering supplies/equipment, etc.) Recruits, screens, enrolls and consents participants Conducts study visits, administers study protocol including specialized assessments that require certification, scores assessments and, monitors and compensates participants Creates and maintains data collection systems and study databases, processes and enters data Provides regular study updates to the project manager and investigators and assists with communications with subcontracted data    collection sites, if applicable Assists with regulatory (IRB) and sponsor reporting, prepares site for sponsor monitoring visits Assists Study Coordinator with writing of protocols and completion of IRB applications for new projects, and completes IRB SCRs, amendments, ORIOs, and AEs Assists in the development and maintenance of the REDCap databases for projects within the Division of Neuropsychology and Rehabilitation Psychology Serves as the primary point of contact, coordinates meetings, and independently creates and delivers presentations for organizations who advocate/support the populations of the studies they are working on. Attends national and local meetings, support groups and other community events as our lab's representative, does qualitative coding of data and conducts analyses of this data Completes other duties as assigned Physical Effort Mostly sedentary. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range Starting salary range is $17.74/hr to $$22.17/hr Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005739": {
      "title": "Director, Global Programs",
      "description": "Job Description - Director, Global Programs (26005739) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director, Global Programs (26005739) Job Description Director, Global Programs Pitt Global Experience Office - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005739 ) The University of Pittsburgh's Global Experiences Office (GEO) is seeking a Director of Global Programs. The Director of Global Programs is responsible for the strategic development and management of academic and experiential global programs supporting schools and campuses without school-embedded GEO staff, including UCIS area studies programs. The position will oversee the management, execution, and continued refinement of new and existing program offerings, as well as support of non-credit bearing experiences abroad to meet desired goals and capacity.  The position is responsible for managing professional team members, program-specific operations including budgets, marketing and promotions plans, and other administrative functions relevant to program development. The individual may have a small portfolio of programs which they manage themselves. The position will serve as primary contact for existing and new global program opportunities for UCIS and assigned schools and will work collaboratively across the units.  This individual will also serve on the Pitt GEO steering committee.  This position reports to the Director, Pitt Global Experiences Office. Job Summary Oversees planning and execution of one or more programs and defines program scope, goals, and strategic objectives. Designs programs that satisfy the University's mission. Performs budgetary functions and approves program budgets, maintains accurate records of program progress, and conducts administrative tasks. Represents the organization and ensures all activities comply with university policies and legal guidelines. Essential Functions Oversees planning and execution of one or more programs; defines program scope, goals, and strategic objectives. Investigates the organization’s target population and design programs that satisfies their mission and needs. Drafts, manages, and approves program budgets. Establishes key performance metrics and maintains accurate records on program progress. Provides detailed reports to senior management. Ensures all activities and operations comply with University policies and legal guidelines. Represents the organization in meetings with donors, advocates, the media, or members of the community. Conducts other administrative tasks such as leading meetings and drafting communications. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Program Director Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Program & Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $85,000 - $87,000 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005685": {
      "title": "Manager of Research Administration",
      "description": "Job Description - Manager of Research Administration (26005685) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Manager of Research Administration (26005685) Job Description Manager of Research Administration Social Work-Academic Programs - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005685 ) The School of Social Work at Pitt is consistently ranked among the top schools of social work in the nation. The School is known for its strong educational programs at the BASW, MSW, and PhD levels and national leadership on race and social problems, child welfare, and health and mental health. The social work values of the School permeate into its operations as well. Our devotion to diversity begins with our staff and faculty who bring a wide variety of experiences to our classrooms and our offices. Our excellent leadership and supervisors are people-focused, communicative, and supportive of your professional development – funding is set aside to help employees pay for development opportunities (training seminars, conferences, etc.). Job Summary Manages administrative and financial operations for Research Grants & Contracts and reviews and negotiates complex grants, contracts, and subcontracts. Reviews and reconciles financial and grant documents and ensures compliance with policies, procedures, and regulations. Prepares and negotiates complex budgets and related documents. Serves as a primary contact and resource regarding all aspects of research grants and contracts, updates databases and accounts, and develops and facilitates operational policies and procedures. Essential Functions The Research Manager serves as the principal operational partner to the Faculty Director, managing the full range of administrative, personnel, financial liaison, and quality-control functions for the Faculty Director's research program. This position acts as a trusted extension of the Faculty Director — anticipating operational needs, exercising independent judgment on day-to-day matters, and ensuring the lab or research group runs efficiently, complies with sponsor and institutional policy, and is positioned for continued growth. The Research Manager oversees hiring and training of lab personnel, establishes and enforces internal systems and protocols, manages task and project workflows across the team, supports proposal development and progress reporting, and serves as the primary liaison to department/school administrators on financial and HR matters. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Grants & Contracts Manager (Pre & Post-Award) Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Grants & Contracts Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005740": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Global Experiences",
      "description": "Job Description - Program Manager, Global Experiences (26005740) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Program Manager, Global Experiences (26005740) Job Description Program Manager, Global Experiences Pitt Global Experience Office - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005740 ) The University of Pittsburgh's Global Experiences Office (GEO) is seeking a Program Manager for Global Experiences The position is primarily responsible for managing and developing a portfolio of academic and experiential global programs. This position will support the development, budgeting, and contracting of new semester, summer, and short-term global programs and experiential learning opportunities abroad. This position is also responsible for the maintenance of existing programs and redevelopment where necessary. The program manager is expected to work across different University units, including the Global Experiences Office, University Center for International Studies, and Pittsburgh campus schools and regional campuses. The individual must demonstrate strong interpersonal skills and have experience working with diverse teams. Primary duties of the position include: Managing student recruitment, advising, and application processes Program budget development, creating and managing vendor contracts Implementing pre-departure preparation and learning activities, and on-program support for faculty and students. Job Summary Oversees all aspects of planning, design, and execution of assigned small, routine projects and coordinates with project stakeholders to define project scope, goals, and deliverables. Assists in timeline development, ensures adherence to timeframes, and adjusts project deliverables to avoid issues. Performs budgetary functions and administrative tasks. Assists with external consultant and vendor selection, negotiation, and management. Essential Functions Oversees all aspects of planning, design, and execution of assigned small, routine projects. Coordinates with project stakeholders to define project scope, goals, and deliverables. Assists in developing a timeline and ensures adherence to all deadlines. Anticipates potential problems and adjusts project deliverables as needed. Drafts and manages the program budget, ensures timely submission of vendor payment requests, and manages expense reimbursements. Tracks project progress and maintains accurate records and files; provides detailed reports to senior management. Assists with selection, negotiation, and management of activities regarding external consults or vendors. Conducts other administrative tasks, leads meetings, and drafts communications. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Project Manager I Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Program & Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $50,000 - $52,000 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005775": {
      "title": "Grants & Contracts Specialist I",
      "description": "Job Description - Grants & Contracts Specialist I (26005775) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Grants & Contracts Specialist I (26005775) Job Description Grants & Contracts Specialist I Sponsored Projects Accounting - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005775 ) Sponsored Projects Accounting (SPA) provides post award financial management for the University's sponsored research portfolio, currently totaling approximately $1.3 billion in active federal and non-federal awards. SPA operates under a full lifecycle model, with staff managing awards from activation through closeout, and is organized under the Controller's Office. The department is responsible for financial compliance, reporting, subrecipient monitoring, and effort reporting in accordance with Uniform Guidance (2 CFR 200) and Cost Accounting Standards. For more information regarding Pitt Finance & Operations, please visit our website at: https://www.financeoperations.pitt.edu/ . Job Summary Performs post-award accounting duties for small grants and contracts. Monitors account activity and prepares routine financial reports. Assists with policy and procedure interpretation and government report preparation. Essential Functions Activates new sponsored awards in the Oracle financial system, setting up account structures in accordance with sponsor terms and University policy. Performs ongoing financial maintenance on active awards, including amendments, renewals, extensions, and other modifications throughout the life of the project. Prepares and submits periodic reimbursement invoices and financial reports to sponsoring agencies in accordance with award terms and reporting deadlines. Monitors the financial progress of assigned projects throughout the full award life cycle, identifying and resolving discrepancies between award terms and account activity. Serves as the financial intermediary between sponsoring agencies and University Principal Investigators or Project Directors, communicating award requirements and resolving financial questions. Performs financial close-out of completed awards, reconciling final expenditures and ensuring compliance with sponsor and University closeout requirements. Utilizes automated accounting systems, Excel, and related databases to manage award data and prepare financial documentation. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Grants & Contracts Specialist I (Post-Award) Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Grants & Contracts Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004219": {
      "title": "Lab Manager",
      "description": "Job Description - Lab Manager (26004219) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Lab Manager (26004219) Job Description Lab Manager Nurs-Health Promotion & Development - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004219 ) The Lab Director's home department is Health Promotion and Development within the School of Nursing. They support two university labs researching Alzheimer's disease and related dementias with research and administrative functions. The labs integrate epidemiologic and neuroscience methods in a population neuroscience framework. Master's Degree preferred Epidemiology training preferred Data management and analytic experience is a plus Admin tasks as needed (keep up CV, coordinate meetings, gain budget approvals and complete necessary paperwork, etc., submit manuscripts to journals) Onboard/train research staff/students Research coordination and regulatory (IRB submissions, scheduling participants, creating and administering research assessments, etc.) Data management and analytic functions (Creation and data entry of RedCap surveys, data verification, cleaning, basic stats analysis) Other duties as assigned Job Summary Oversees day-to-day management and execution of multiple complex research projects and ensures compliance with all funding agencies and sponsors. Constructs data collection instruments and crafts promotional materials. Troubleshoots data and manages database. Assists with screening, recruitment, and enrollment of study participants. Performs budgetary and purchasing functions. Essential Functions Oversees day-to-day management and execution of multiple complex research projects including recommending and implementing project procedures; tracks project progress, assesses project needs, assigns tasks, and evaluates team performance. • Trains consultants, subcontractors, clerical/technical staff, and graduate student researchers. • Documents and assures compliance with all requirements of funding agencies and sponsors that support ongoing research activities. • Constructs data collection instruments and promotional materials; collects, analyzes and troubleshoots data and manages database. Compiles reports and present data findings as directed. • Assists with screening, recruitment, and enrollment of study participants. • Facilitates budgetary and purchasing decisions. Physical Effort -Must be able to sit for long periods of time The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Program Supervisor Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Program Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm occasional weekends or evenings for community events Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $43,894.56---$53,711.04/year Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005734": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Nurse II",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse II (26005734) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse II (26005734) Job Description Clinical Research Nurse II Med-Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005734 ) The Thomas E. Starzl Transplantation Institute in the Department of Surgery at the University of Pittsburgh has an immediate opening for a Clinical Research Nurse II. Job Summary Supports clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews lab results, patient data, and lab specimens; administers medications and protocol-specific treatments. Performs general laboratory duties and specialized nursing duties, trains new staff, and ensures regulatory adherence. Essential Functions The applicant will manage/coordinate assigned clinical research projects and drug trials, including, but not limited to, recruitment and nursing care.  Regulatory experience is preferred. The applicant should be highly motivated to learn, detail-oriented and able to prioritize multiple tasks.  Sound judgement and analytical and interpersonal skills are a must. Physical Effort The incumbent must be able to stand and walk for long periods of time.  Must be able to see and have use of both hands. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Nurse II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research - Nursing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor of Science in Nursing Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Required Licensure/Certification RN Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Regulatory experience preferred. Work Schedule M-F; 8:30am - 5:00pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005146": {
      "title": "Title IX and Section 504 Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Title IX and Section 504 Coordinator (26005146) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Title IX and Section 504 Coordinator (26005146) Job Description Title IX and Section 504 Coordinator Office of Compliance and Investigations - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005146 ) The Title IX and Section 504 Coordinator serves as the University’s Title IX Coordinator and provides strategic leadership for the University's response to complaints of sexual harassment and other forms of discrimination. Reporting to the Assistant Vice Chancellor for Compliance, Investigations & Ethics, this position directs the institutional framework for compliance with federal, state and local civil rights laws, including Title IX, the Americans with Disabilities Act, and other civil rights regulations. Job Summary Serves as main contact for sexual violence prevention and education and responds to government inquiries regarding anti-discrimination laws, regulations, and requirements. Investigates complex claims and complaints of discrimination. Manages and tracks outcomes of training and education programs. Develops, evaluates, and improves disclosures, policies, procedures, and practices. Designs climate surveys, manages complex inquiries, and organizes other files regarding compliance. Essential Functions Compliance Support: Helps to direct compliance with civil rights laws and serves as an advisor to the Vice Chancellor for Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing regarding civil rights compliance, risk mitigation, and best practices. Works with appropriate campus units/departments to support institutional policies and procedures for addressing Title IX, and ADA complaints and related civil rights matters. Complaint Management: Works with program liaisons and investigators to help guide the University’s response to Title IX and sexual harassment complaints. This includes receiving and screening complaints, maintaining confidential records, and recommending appropriate interventions. The coordinator will also receive, review, and approve investigative reports and Section 504 grievances following a complaint. Monitoring and Reporting: Work with the compliance team to track, maintain detailed reports, and conduct on-site reviews, if necessary, to ensure adherence to civil rights laws. Training and Awareness: Coordinates with the Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing to design and deliver training programs to staff, students, or faculty about civil rights laws, anti-discrimination policies, and inclusive practices Physical Effort Duties are primarily sedentary. Must be able to use a computer at a desk or similar workstation, and travel to on-campus meetings as needed. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Title IX Coordinator III Job Family Human Resources Job Sub-Family Institutional Engagement & Wellbeing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005749": {
      "title": "Dispatcher",
      "description": "Job Description - Dispatcher (26005749) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Dispatcher (26005749) Job Description Dispatcher Public Safety - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005749 ) Monitors and responds to all radio communications; dispatches calls for service; provides assistance, direction and information via telephone and radio; enters all relevant data into the department's records management system; provides assistance to the communication specialist as needed; performs special projects as needed which includes training other dispatchers. APCO certification and previous dispatch experience is preferred. Job Summary Monitors and responds to all radio communications; dispatches calls for service; provides assistance, direction and information via telephone and radio; enters all relevant data into the department’s records management system; provides assistance to the communication specialist as needed; performs special projects as needed which includes training other dispatchers. APCO certification and previous dispatch experience is preferred. Essential Functions Monitors and responds to all radio communications; interacts with all persons in a courteous and respectful manner; responds immediately to all requests for service. Operates the University’s central alarm system (emergency phones, opening and closing of electronic doors, fire, and burglar alarms). Operates and maintains the state National Crime Information Center computer; queries system for criminal histories, stolen vehicles, and property, and distributes information through chain of command. Monitors all CCTV monitoring equipment within the communication room. Maintains all files and paperwork documentation as directed. Assesses dispatch media log, notifies supervisor of shift report of media log. Records personnel who have called off work; notifies administration and supervisors. Assists with dispatcher duties when necessary; answers emergency calls when necessary; enters appropriate data into the Department’s record management system. Performs special projects as needed. Physical Effort Monitors and responds to all radio communications; dispatches calls for service; provides assistance, direction, and information via telephone and radio; enters all relevant data into the department's records management system; provides assistance to the communication specialist as needed; performs special projects as needed which includes training other dispatchers. APCO certification and previous dispatch experience is preferred. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Union Eligible.Police.Dispatcher Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule 40 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Per Collective Bargaining Agreement Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005710": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Dental Assistant (26005710) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Dental Assistant (26005710) Job Description Dental Assistant Dent Med-Diagnostic Sciences - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005710 ) Benefits include: *11 Paid Holidays, Paid Vacation, Sick and Personal Days * Additional Paid Time Off (Winter Recess) during the period between Christmas and the New Year * Paid Parental Leave * Education benefits for eligible employees, their dependents and spouse/domestic partner * Above-average Employer Contribution towards Medical, Prescription Drug, Vision, Life, STD, and LTD Insurance plans * A robust retirement savings plan option. Including 100% match on employee contributions of 3-8% (150% after vesting) and enhanced match for those nearing retirement. Job Summary Performs chairside dental assisting and radiography in a dental specialty clinic with patients who may have received sedation and/or outpatient general anesthesia. Provides client-based oral hygiene and appliance care and completes patient chart documentation in accordance with all applicable regulations. Maintains equipment, dispenses supplies, sets up for all procedures, and follows proper sanitization and sterilization procedures. Essential Functions 1. Clinic Duties: Chairside dental assisting for students and faculty which includes the taking of dental radiographs. The dental assistant must also be proficient at dental charting and recording patient data including the taking of patient vital signs. 2. Clerical duties: Answer the telephone; take and deliver messages. Disseminate inter & intradepartmental communication. Registering and assigning emergency patients. Incorporating patient records into the Electronic Health Record from both internal and external sources. Interfacing patient records via SDM scheduling and business software. Communicating with patients and advising them of an emergency clinic and SDM policies. Limited financial counseling of patients regarding emergency care. Maintain and file student records, including grade forms and attendance forms. Monitor student schedules and attendance. 3. Dispensary duties: Dispense equipment, instruments, and supplies to students. Restock dispensary supplies and instruments. Processing of instrument cassettes through the Instrumentation Management System (IMS) and sterilization of locally maintained instruments. Monitor and maintain clinic sterilization equipment and enforcement of disinfection methods. Monitor and maintain the dispensary inventory including supplies and instruments, ordering, and restocking. 4. Other duties: Dental assistant is responsible for opening and closing the emergency clinic. Must assume designated responsibilities of co-workers as needed. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Specialty Dental Assistant Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Clinical Dental Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Graduate of Dental Technology Program Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification Current PA dental radiology certificate. EFDA preferred. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003542": {
      "title": "Research Review Analyst",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Review Analyst (26003542) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Review Analyst (26003542) Job Description Research Review Analyst Institution Review Board - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003542 ) The Research Review Analyst (RRA) works as part of a multi¬ disciplinary team under the auspices of the University of Pittsburgh Human Research Protection Program. The RRA is responsible for maintaining a current working knowledge of federal and state regulations pertaining to the responsible conduct of human subjects research, along with ensuring compliance with University of Pittsburgh policies and procedures. The RRA will conduct a thorough review of studies based on federal regulations, state law, and University of Pittsburgh policies and procedures. As an IRB board member, the RRA has the authority to independently approve studies that qualify for exempt/expedited review seeking consultation as necessary. All decisions are documented in the online submission system. As part of a service-oriented outreach program, the RRA will provide consultation and training to members of the research community at large via telephone or through face-to-face meetings. Excellent written and verbal communication skills are essential for this position, as the RRA must personally and electronically communicate with members of the research community on a regular basis. It is preferred that the RRA has a bachelor’s degree in a related field with prior human subjects research experience preferred (2-3 years preferred). Degree in social science, bioethics, RN or related field preferred. This position is open to a flexible work arrangement which includes in-office and hybrid options. Job Summary Serves as a regulatory expert responsible for managing the protocol review process by ensuring compliance with federal regulations, state law, and University of Pittsburgh policies and procedures. Provides regulatory and ethical training and guidance for IRB members and the research community at large through consultation and education Essential Functions Protocol Review: Will be responsible for independently reviewing and approving research protocols as IRB members submitted by the research community to ensure compliance with federal and state regulations, ethical considerations, and University of Pittsburgh policies and procedures Consultations: Will lead complex consultations with investigators and research coordinators to enhance understanding of research regulations. Educational Programs : Responsible for implementing programs for the research community to ensure understanding of the regulatory requirements associated with conducting human subjects research. Other: Must demonstrate the ability to assume special assignments not otherwise described as determined by HRPO/IRB management. Physical Effort Job is primarily sedentary but may require travel on campus to attend meetings or events. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.IRB Specialist II Job Family Compliance & Audit Job Sub-Family Institutional Review Board Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m.- 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
