      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician I (26005707) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician I (26005707) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician I Med-Otolaryngology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005707 ) The Pittsburgh Hearing Research Center at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking a research technician to conduct hearing research in animal models. The technician will investigate the neural mechanisms underlying normal and pathological hearing, with an emphasis on recovery following gene therapy for congenital hearing loss and/or noise-induced hearing loss. The research technician is expected to learn, conduct, and complete experiments in auditory neuroscience, with an emphasis on behavioral and/or immunohistochemical experiments. The position offers the opportunity to develop expertise across a broad methodological range, including behavioral assays, immunohistochemistry, in vivo neural monitoring (one- and two-photon calcium imaging /optophysiology), and in vitro electrophysiology. Under the guidance of senior lab members, the technician will learn foundational and advanced concepts in hearing and auditory neuroscience while contributing to data collection, analysis, writing, and presentations, with opportunities for co-authorship on resulting publications. A Bachelor's degree in Neuroscience, Biology, Biochemistry, Genetics, or a related field with research experience is required. Wet lab, histology, and neurobiology experience is preferred but not required. The technician will troubleshoot experimental and technical problems and contribute recommendations to improve research efforts. The technician will develop experience in these tasks and learn to handle mice in accordance with the regulations set forth by the Division of Laboratory Animal Resources. Additional duties will include, but are not limited to, laboratory maintenance, equipment testing and inspection, data management, report preparation, animal procurement, and ordering of laboratory supplies. The technician will be expected to gain a working knowledge of the laboratory and to operate all laboratory systems under the direction of the Principal Investigator and senior laboratory staff. The research technician is expected to learn, conduct, and complete experiments in auditory neuroscience, with an emphasis on behavioral and/or immunohistochemical experiments. The technician is also expected to perform statistical analysis of the collected data and to prepare figures. In addition, the technician will troubleshoot experimental and technical problems and contribute recommendations to improve research efforts. Job Summary Performs laboratory testing and some analysis on multiple types of specimen samples. Operates and properly sterilizes equipment and maintains inventory and assists with ordering. Essential Functions The research technician is expected to learn, conduct, and complete experiments in auditory neuroscience, with an emphasis on behavioral and/or immunohistochemical experiments. The technician is also expected to perform statistical analysis of the collected data and to prepare figures. In addition, the technician will troubleshoot experimental and technical problems and contribute recommendations to improve research efforts. Physical Effort Must be able to perform laboratory experiments with mobility. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 9:00 to 5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
