    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005689": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator II",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator II (26005689) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator II (26005689) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator II Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005689 ) This position is for the Division of General Academic Pediatrics (GAP) within the Department of Pediatrics. The successful candidate will support clinical research and clinical trials in a busy pediatric clinical setting in Oakland, with multiple studies focused on access to pediatric healthcare, the use of cutting-edge technology in pediatric primary care (telemedicine, e-visits, e-consults, artificial intelligence), and equity in pediatric primary care delivery. Candidates with bilingual English-Spanish skills are strongly preferred. The incumbent will assist with recruitment and consent, data collection, electronic health record review, participant retention, data management, and data analysis. Data collection may include surveys, phone calls, qualitative participant interviews, and interview transcription. Data management may include maintaining password protected files with participant data and recruitment platforms (RedCap, Pitt+Me). Data analysis would include qualitative coding and thematic analysis (training will be provided) and development of dissemination tools such as infographics and posters. If travel is required for the position, and if the incumbent is not utilizing public transportation, a valid driver’s license is required. It is the expectation that the incumbent will use their own vehicle required for local travel and the owner of the vehicle must carry automobile liability insurance. The owner’s automobile liability insurance coverage is primary coverage. The University’s automobile liability insurance policy provides excess coverage only. Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Conducts research assessments on study participants. Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Assists with training staff. Ensures adherence to protocols and corrects issues with data collection. Essential Functions • Conducts research assessments on study participants. • Assists with and adheres to study protocols, and Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. • Assists with training staff on proper and best study research techniques as directed. • Mentors and educates staff and student workers as directed. • Ensures proper protocols are followed and quality assurance of research and related work. • Corrects data collection issues. Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Mainly 8am - 4:30pm; not often, but some early evenings may occur. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005642": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Technician (26005642) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Technician (26005642) Job Description Research Technician Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005642 ) Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions • Performs a variety of laboratory experiments such as histology, flow cytometry, molecular techniques, gene sequencing, and related technical functions, testing, troubleshooting, and analysis, and may perform microsurgical procedures. Ensures conformity to specifications. • Identifies and prepares specimens. • Oversees supply management: ordering, procurement, tracking estimates, and receiving items. • Operates and maintains applicable laboratory equipment for job functions. • Keeps detailed, accurate, and timely data and log books. Organizes and documents results. • Maintains, calibrates, cleans, and tests sterility of laboratory equipment. • Prior experiences with mammalian specimen research preferred. Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Shift determined by manager. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005596": {
      "title": "Program Evaluation, CQI, and Accreditation Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Program Evaluation, CQI, and Accreditation Director (26005596) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Program Evaluation, CQI, and Accreditation Director (26005596) Job Description Program Evaluation, CQI, and Accreditation Director Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005596 ) * *The University is partnering with Systems One / Joulé to assist in the recruitment of this position. If interested in this opportunity and to be considered: PLEASE APPLY THROUGH THIS LINK: Program Evaluation, CQI and Accreditation Director Preference will be given to candidates who have experience in CQI, accreditation, has performed in an intermediate or senior level position with demonstrable skills related to position responsibilities.  The department requires an experienced, effective, productive administrator who can ensure assessment and evaluation practices are fair and appropriate and the program is meeting institutional goals and regulatory standards. Significant and high-level analytical, communication and interpersonal skills are required. Ability to generate and implement solutions is essential. Must be able to assess and prioritize functions, projects, and tasks. Job Summary Leads team and directs medical education program evaluation operations. Designs and implements program evaluation measures and executes ongoing continuous quality improvement and accreditation efforts. Leads strategic planning efforts and ensures compliance with regulations. Supports personnel in the execution of program evaluation efforts, communicates recommendations and improvements, and contributes to educational research projects. Develops annual budgets and performs related financial duties Essential Functions The Program Evaluation, CQI and Accreditation Director is responsible for ensuring compliance with accreditation standards, overseeing the preparation and timely submission of requirements of the Liaison Committee on Medical Education (LCME), and developing, implementing, and monitoring continuous quality improvement (CQI) initiatives. Incumbent will be a leader within the Office of Accreditation and Continuous Improvement and will lead the accreditation and CQI efforts. This position will oversee all aspects of LCME accreditation, including self-studies, data collection, site visit preparation, and ongoing compliance monitoring. Bachelor's degree required with a minimum of 7 years experience. Physical Effort General office setting. Incumbent is expected to move about  Scaife Hall, in particular, and the University and nearby clinical facilities, in general.  Incumbent is expected to be able to lift and move, as necessary. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Medical Education Program Administration Director Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Medical Education Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 4:30pm *Will be 5 days onsite until fully trained or at the end of provisional period (whichever comes first) **After which, a hybrid work arrangement is offered with 3 days onsite and 2 days remote Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005637": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Dental Assistant (26005637) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Dental Assistant (26005637) Job Description Dental Assistant Dent Med-Orthodontics & Dentofacial Orthopedics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005637 ) Job Summary Performs chairside dental assisting and radiography. Guides patients through visits and treatments, ensures charts are complete and necessary information is collected, and coordinates patient flow. Ensures infection control in operatories and with instruments. Maintains supplies. Essential Functions The position will perform the following orthodontic/dental assistant functions: chairside assistance to residents; maintain an aseptic environment; follow OSHA, HIPAA and infection control guidelines; maintain and dispense inventory and instrument cassettes; maintain patient records; assist in ordering supplies and miscellaneous clerical duties. Physical Effort Must be able to sit and/or stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Dental Assistant Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Clinical Dental Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. -5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005561": {
      "title": "Communications & Marketing Coordinator, Falk School",
      "description": "Job Description - Communications & Marketing Coordinator, Falk School (26005561) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Communications & Marketing Coordinator, Falk School (26005561) Job Description Communications & Marketing Coordinator, Falk School Falk School - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005561 ) Falk Laboratory School , an independent K-8 school located on the University of Pittsburgh campus, is seeking a Communications & Marketing Coordinator who will be responsible for documenting and disseminating information about all aspects of Falk’s programming and activities. Qualifications: ·      Excellent written communication skills, spelling, grammar, and a creative sense of design. ·      Organization, project management abilities, and the ability to work independently. ·      A high level of professionalism and discretion. ·      Basic familiarity with Microsoft Word, with preferred proficiency in the Adobe Creative Suite. ·      A working knowledge of website content management systems and social media platforms. ·      Minimum two years of experience working in a communications role. Additionally, Falk invites candidates with other skills that would enhance school storytelling, such as basic photography and/or videography and editing, podcasting, etc. Bachelor's Degree Required. Materials can be uploaded to join.pitt.edu . For full consideration, please submit: 1. Letter of Interest 2. Resume 3. Recent writing sample (750 words, maximum) Compensation commensurate with experience. Falk Laboratory School, a department in the School of Education at the University of Pittsburgh, offers excellent benefits. Applications will be reviewed beginning in early September and will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. Offer of employment is contingent on the candidate satisfactorily obtaining and passing the following before commencement of appointment: Pennsylvania Department of Human Services Child Abuse History Clearance, Pennsylvania State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check. Candidates must also submit proof of a negative TB test before their first day of work if hired. Also, as Act 168 of 2014 requires, the candidate must satisfy the requirements on the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Department of Education Sexual Misconduct/Abuse Disclosure Release Form. Please contact Dr. Molly Hicks, Director of Administrative Operations, at MEH479@pitt.edu with questions. Job Summary Develops routine web and print content and marketing. Creates varied presentations for communications team and marketing materials for marketing team. Ensures consistent messaging and maintains University brand and style. Essential Functions Specific duties include, but are not limited to: ·      Content Development: Create unique and dynamic content that documents life at Falk to be shared on a variety of platforms, as well as outward facing media, including special interest and feature stories for the school website and social media. ·      Schoolwide Communications: Develop and publish all-school correspondences, as well as provide assistance in classroom and division messaging. This includes the weekly all-school e-mail newsletter, important school announcements, and managing the school’s emergency alert system ·      Marketing and Constituent Outreach: Collaborate with a variety of internal and external stakeholders to create compelling materials for public distribution, including admissions brochures and other print materials, as well as print, radio, and other advertising. Additionally, the incumbent will assist in the development of materials for fundraising and stewardship, as well as editing the annual alumni magazine. ·      Digital Communications: Design, manage, format, and maintain content on Falk’s website, as well as serve as the lead administrator on all of the School’s social media platforms. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Communications Specialist II Job Family Communications & Marketing Job Sub-Family Communications Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 - 4:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter, Writing Sample Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005475": {
      "title": "Web Developer",
      "description": "Job Description - Web Developer (26005475) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Web Developer (26005475) Job Description Web Developer Office of University Communications - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005475 ) As a web developer in the Office of University Communications and Marketing you'll be part of the team responsible for planning and executing highly effective and user-friendly websites and digital experiences for academic and administrative units with a focus on marketing initiatives, recruitment, and student experience. The Web Developer builds and maintains fully functional WCAG 1.1 standards-compliant websites and e-newsletters as a member of the Office of University Communications and Marketing Web team. The Developer works collaboratively with Web project managers, content specialists, designers, vendors, and supervisors to build sites and e-newsletters for strategic Univeristy initiatives, University schools, departments, and administrative units. Site are built in Drupal and WordPress CMS based on design concepts, UX/IA plans and written specifications. Position requires proficiency developing accessible and mobile-friendly sites in popular open source content management systems such as Drupal and WordPress. This requires the developer to be proficient in building sites using HTML, CSS, MySQL, PHP, LESS/SASS Twig, JavaScript, SSH, Git/GitHub, and popular CSS frameworks. Developer must accurately translate design mockups into responsive Web constructs optimized for mobile and desktop viewports. The ideal candidate is a passionate developer with three to five years of experience who enjoys working across multiple aspects of web development, enjoys team collaboration, and is excited by seeing the impact of their work. In additional to strong technical and analytical skill, the successful candidate will be a collaborative team member, an effective communicator, and a motivated problem solver with a demonstrated ability to meet deadlines. This position requires at least two days onsite per week. Pre HRCM Qualifications: - Bachelor’s degree - At least three years of web development experience, preferably with PHP, Drupal, and/or WordPress - Experience implementing large and complex websites within a content management system environment - Experience in an agency, consulting, shared-services, or other client-service web environment - Experience with responsive web design, front-end build processes, and HTML5 / CSS3 / SASS / JavaScript - Solid understanding of best practices and standards for web development, performance, security, accessibility (WCAG 2.1), and organic search engine optimization - Proficient with code versioning tools such as Github or Bitbucket - Familiar with quality assurance tools and code validation tools. Job Requirements: - Must be a good problem solver and someone who is curious and enjoys learning new skills - Must be able to communicate effectively with university partners, vendors, and co-workers from a variety of professional disciplines - Must be organized and able to manage and track time effectively - Must be able to meet deadlines - Must be versatile and able to contribute and add value to the team on a variety of tasks - Must be able to collaborate and work effectively in a hybrid or remote environment. Job Summary Contributes to the design, development, coding, testing, debugging, implementation, and maintenance of moderately complex websites and/or software. Documents development and maintenance efforts, assists in integrating assigned work with other system components, and designs and performs functional testing. Essential Functions Responsibilities Develop accessible, responsive frontend components from approved UX/IA specifications Create and modify Drupal and WordPress themes based on designs Implement the back-end of university websites in Drupal and WordPress Complete updates, support, and enhancement tasks for existing client websites Build content integrations with third-party systems Contribute to functional / technical planning Participate in quality assurance activities Preferred experience with advanced digital analytics implementation, including tag management, custom data layers, event-based tracking, consent management platforms Physical Effort Duties are primarily sedentary. Must be able to use a computer at a desk or similar workstation, and travel to on-campus meetings as needed. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Software Developer II Job Family Information Technology Job Sub-Family Programming & Development Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005629": {
      "title": "Senior Research Scientist",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Research Scientist (26005629) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Research Scientist (26005629) Job Description Senior Research Scientist Med-Organ Pathobiology and Therapeutics Institute (OPTIn) - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005629 ) The Organ Pathobiology and Therapeutics Institute (OPTIn) is searching for a Research Scientist to play a significant role in our New Approach Methodologies (NAMs) program utilizing our biomimetic human liver acinus microphysiological system (LAMPS) platform. We use both primary human cells and iPSC-derived cells for evaluating metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD) progression, identifying disease-relevant biomarkers, and testing of candidates as well as a precision medicine platform for the development of patient digital twins and patient biomimetic twins. We are one of four Translational Centers for MPS (TraCe-MPS) established in collaboration with the National Center for Advancing Translational Sciences (NCATS) and the FDA, with the goal of qualifying our liver MPS platforms as drug development tools (DDTs) for various specific contexts of use. A key focus of the current position is the detection of low-level, subclinical effects in a human based system using real-time fixed endpoint, secretome-based, and image-based readouts to identify early activation of toxicity pathways. The incumbent will primarily participate within the TraCe-MPS group for the qualification of the LAMPS platform as a DDT with the FDA to aid in the determination of drug candidate dosing in patients with MASLD. Great talent in complex, multi-cell-based experimentation, knowledge of liver physiology, experience identifying toxicity signals via phenotype and molecular level assays and high content imaging experience is required. Toxicologists, pharmacologists or cell biologists and/or biomedical engineers with experience in the design and application of liver MPS systems are also strongly encouraged to apply. PhD in toxicology, pharmacology, physiology, cell biology, biophysics, biomedical engineering, or related field required.  Strong cell based research experience; previous experience with liver MPS model systems or co-culture systems is highly valued. Working knowledge of toxicology and pharmacology is greatly desired. Experience in liver cell and organ physiology, cell and molecular biology and fluorescence imaging and quantification is desire d. Experience with primary (patient isolated) human cells and iPSCs a plus. Must Perform studies for the qualification of the LAMPS platform as a DDT, conduct and manage independent research projects from experimental design through implementation and analysis, present results in seminars and publications, prepare and draft various research documents including manuscripts, proposals, and grant applications, c ollaborate with the liver microphysiological systems team and clinician-scientists at Pitt. Job Summary Serves as subject matter expert and conducts independent scientific research projects from inception to presentation. Prepares and crafts various complex documentations of research results into manuscripts, proposals, grant applications, and presentations. Trains undergraduates, junior lab members, and research technicians. Manages laboratory policies and coordinates high-level work and project development in collaboration with other specialists. Essential Functions Computer work: walking from place to place; standing and sitting to perform essential tasks.  Good manual dexterity. Physical Effort Lifting and stacking of boxes of supplies, standing for extended periods required to fulfill workload.  Light - Maximum lifting of up to 20 lbs. With frequent lifting/carrying of up to 10 lbs. or a negligible amount; significant walking or standing may be required or may involve sitting with a degree of pushing and pulling. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Senior Research Scientist Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Science Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Professional Doctorate Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005581": {
      "title": "HR Generalist I",
      "description": "Job Description - HR Generalist I (26005581) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - HR Generalist I (26005581) Job Description HR Generalist I Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005581 ) The Human Resources Generalist I serves as a core member of the Faculty and Employee Administrative Operations (FEAO) team within the Department of Medicine (DOM) at the University of Pittsburgh. This position is responsible for the day-to-day administration of staff employment transactions across the full employee lifecycle — from new hire and onboarding through position changes, and separation — as well as student employment, and temporary staffing, as well as back up for staff supplemental pays and leave of absences. The HR Generalist I partners closely with the Manager, Academic & Staff Affairs and serves as the primary transactional HR point of contact for DOM division administrators on staff employment matters. This role requires strong organizational skills, as well as the ability to manage a high volume of concurrent actions with accuracy and timeliness. Preferred qualifications include: Strong proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word, Outlook) and document management platforms (SharePoint, OneDrive); Experience with DocuSign or a comparable electronic signature and workflow; Excellent attention to detail, organizational skills, and commitment to data accuracy and confidentiality; Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to interact professionally with employees, managers, and division administrators at all levels. Job Summary Assists in the coordination of a broad range of human resources programs and in the management of the staffing and interview process. Coordinates trainings and processes payroll and human resources transactions. Essential Functions Staff Positions • Manage & review new & replacement position requests submitted by divisions. Manage Talent Center requisitions. Coordinate new hire onboarding communications. • Maintain Tracker & personnel records to ensure all records are current and accurate • Prepare payroll backup documentation for all new hires. Terminations • Process staff terminations via PittWorx. Maintain Termination Tracker. File personnel records associated with all separation actions. Prepare payroll backup documentation. Student Employment • Manage student employment positions & offers via Talent Center. Coordinate new hire onboarding. Maintain Student Tracker & all associated personnel records. • Process actions for student employees, including salary increases, terminations, & TEAM updates. All-Temps • Manage & approve requisitions for all-temp needs. Complete onboarding documentation & maintain the All Temp Tracker and personnel records. Coordinate with All Temps department as needed. Physical Effort Primarily sedentary work performed at a computer workstation for extended periods of time. Frequent use of a keyboard, mouse, and telephone/headset. Regular participation in virtual meetings via video conferencing platforms. Occasional standing, walking, or movement within the office environment. Ability to view a computer screen for prolonged periods with or without reasonable accommodation. Minimal lifting required' may occasionally lift or carry item such as files, documents, or office supplies not to exceed 10 pounds. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Human Resources Generalist I Job Family Human Resources Job Sub-Family Employee & Labor Relations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $19.07/hr - $24.75/hr Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005356": {
      "title": "Veterinary Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Veterinary Technician (26005356) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Veterinary Technician (26005356) Job Description Veterinary Technician DLAR-Veterinary Services - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005356 ) The individual will serve as a Veterinary Technician within the Division of Laboratory and Animal Resources (DLAR). The individual will: • assist DLAR veterinarians with the provision of veterinary medical care and maintenance of animal colony health, • provide animal study support and perform animal technical procedures under the direction of a veterinarian, and • periodically provide animal husbandry and care or cage wash support to meet the operational needs of the facility. The preferred candidate will have a college degree in animal science or a similar biological science, certification by the American Association for Laboratory Animal Science (AALAS), completion of an AVMA CVTEA accredited veterinary technician program and have a licensed, certified, or registered veterinary technician status. The successful candidate must demonstrate strong attention to detail, interpersonal communication, customer service, and organizational skills. The position requires ability to: work some weekends, evenings, and holidays, travel to multiple buildings in a timely manner, pass criminal, Drug Enforcement Act (DEA[AC2.1]) and social background checks, and possibly obtain Child Protection Clearances and/or Select Agent Clearances, and successfully enrollment in the University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program, and other medical surveillance/immunization programs, as dictated by the current research activities. Vaccination and/or TB testing may be required. Job Summary Provides support to veterinarians, fellow technicians, and researchers to provide laboratory animal care and research support, daily monitoring of animal well-being, and cleaning and maintenance of clinical areas. Assists with procedures, provides surgical and anesthesia support, triages cases, performs medical imaging, administers medications, and other various related duties. Maintains documentation and ensures compliance with all applicable regulations. Orders and maintains supply inventory. Essential Functions The employee must be able to: • Perform veterinary technician skills and procedures, • Have sufficient visual acuity and manual dexterity to recognize and identify normal and abnormal species-specific clinical appearances and behavior patterns, perform veterinary technical procedures (including euthanasia), safely handle and restrain animals, and operate and maintain facility equipment and supplies, • Negotiate around equipment within close quarters, and move between rooms, workspaces, and facilities, • Work with a variety of animal species, biohazards, chemical and radiation hazards, and wear personal protective equipment (PPE), • Work directly with live or dead animals and clean or soiled bedding and caging, • Successfully enroll in the University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program (AESP) and other medical surveillance/immunization programs as dictated by current research activities, • Receive vaccinations and health assessments, including TB testing, required to work in some animal holding or procedure areas, in accordance with DLAR and/or EH&S policies and practices, • Perform computer skills including the ability to utilize common applications (e.g., email, Word, Excel) and DLAR systems (ex: CAMs), • Read, understand, and follow DLAR and other institutional guidance documents (SOPs, policies), including IACUC approved animal protocols, • Follow written and verbal instructions, • Accurately and effectively communicate in English, verbally and in writing, • Work variable scheduled during on-call coverage, and some weekends and evenings and holidays, as required to support research operations, and • Travel between DLAR facilities in a timely manner. Physical Effort The employee must be able to: • Stand for extended periods of time throughout most of the workday, • Lift and move objects weighing up to 50 pounds including but not limited to caging and equipment, bags or boxes of animal diet and animal bedding, and operate equipment to move heavier objects or weights exceeding 50 pounds, • Perform repetitive motion tasks that involve pushing, pulling, reaching, and/or bending, and • Physically handle and restrain a variety of small and large laboratory animals. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Veterinary Technician Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Animal Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification ALAT Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Required Licenses/Certifications (short open text field.) AALAS Certification at the Laboratory Associate Animal Technician (ALAT) level required. External candidates will need to attain within 12 months. Work Schedule M-F, 7AM-4PM, some evenings, weekends and holidays as determined by business need Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Commensurate with experience. Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001495": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Technician (26001495) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Technician (26001495) Job Description Research Technician Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26001495 ) Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions • Performs a variety of laboratory experiments such as histology, flow cytometry, molecular techniques, gene sequencing, and related technical functions, testing, troubleshooting, and analysis, and may perform microsurgical procedures. Ensures conformity to specifications. • Identifies and prepares specimens. • Oversees supply management: ordering, procurement, tracking estimates, and receiving items. • Operates and maintains applicable laboratory equipment for job functions. • Keeps detailed, accurate, and timely data and log books. Organizes and documents results. • Maintains, calibrates, cleans, and tests sterility of laboratory equipment. Physical Effort Medium. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule This position will require flexibility with shift/hours and occasionally be required to work on the evenings and weekends. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004115": {
      "title": "Electrical Engineer",
      "description": "Job Description - Electrical Engineer (26004115) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Electrical Engineer (26004115) Job Description Electrical Engineer Facilities Management AVC - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004115 ) Join the Facilities Management team, a division of the University of Pittsburgh’s Business & Operations. As a University Electrical Engineer, you will play a key role in maintaining the safety, vitality, and quality of our campus facilities by supporting electrical design, project management, and the maintenance and operations of campus electrical infrastructure. Facilities Management Job Summary Establishes design criteria for electrical systems and reviews plans and specifications to ensure cost-efficiency, effectiveness, and best practices. Provides electrical design and/or project management for assigned projects. Ensures contractor and trade compliance with all project details. Ascertains fiscal electrical system requirements and facilitates budgetary matters. Essential Functions • work alongside fellow electrical engineers and report to the Senior Manager of Electrical Engineering, who also oversees a team of mechanical engineers and the Energy & Utilities group. • Review construction documents and specifications for adherence to University Design Manual standards and relevant codes, and provide electrical design and/or project management on assigned projects. • When assigned as Project Manager, lead all required pre-construction activities through bid walkthrough, including the Request for Proposal, contractor interviews, site walkthroughs, and design schedule and budget management. Following bidding, construction management transitions to the Office of Planning, Design, & Construction. • Represent Facilities Management Engineering on comprehensive construction projects with electrical scope, supporting the University Project Manager with electrical-specific questions and document reviews. • Support the maintenance and operation of low- and medium-voltage electrical distribution systems, power systems studies, life safety systems, lighting systems, and on-site standby power generation, and assist with the University’s e-meter system. • Assist in the development and enforcement of electrical design standards, maintain accurate as-built documentation, and contribute to capital preservation planning for electrical infrastructure, fire alarm, elevators, and generators. Physical Effort Facilities Management The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Electrical Engineer Job Family Campus Operations Job Sub-Family Facilities Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday to Friday 7:30 am to 4:00 pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003953": {
      "title": "Housekeeping Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Housekeeping Coordinator (26003953) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Housekeeping Coordinator (26003953) Job Description Housekeeping Coordinator Facilities Management AVC - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003953 ) Job Summary Inspects custodial services in assigned areas, ensures compliance with standards, and resolves issues. Supervises team, organizes daily assignments, and oversees training. Communicates to determine needs and requests for special events. Determines, orders, and evaluates equipment and supplies. Submits and maintains forms, records, and requests. Essential Functions Inspects custodial services in assigned areas daily to ensure work completed meets department standards and ensures issues in need of improvement are corrected. Assists in planning and organizing of custodians daily assignments, reassigns positions when special coverage is needed, maintains optimal coverage efficiency. Communicates with associated personnel to determine needs and requests for special events; ensures accurate setup and cleanup; identifies and resolves any related issues. Trains new employees on proper procedures and usage of all equipment, tools, machines, cleaning solvents, and chemicals; ensures all training manuals are current and correct; retrains employees as needed; conducts meetings as requested to review proper and effective work. Manages and submits payroll for custodial staff; maintains accurate administrative records for custodians. Determines custodial equipment, supplies, tools, and materials needed; orders supplies; evaluates and recommends chemicals, products, and equipment. Submits appropriate forms and requests including accident reports, emergency repairs, daily logs, and other related requests. Physical Effort Walking and lifting The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Supervisor - Custodial Services Job Family Campus Operations Job Sub-Family Facilities Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Wednesday, Thursday, Friday 7:30am -4pm Saturday and Sunday  3pm-11:30pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
