    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005485": {
      "title": "Research Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Program Coordinator (26005485) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Program Coordinator (26005485) Job Description Research Program Coordinator UPCI Research Lab-Schmitz, Kathryn - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005485 ) This position is to serve as Research Staff for The Schmitz Lab and will lead many of the operational aspects required of multiple exercise oncology research studies. This staff person will work with clinicians and staff to identify patients, approach patients, obtain informed consent, schedule study-related appointments, collect and coordinate study data, troubleshoot issues that occur before, during and after patient visits, and ensure that all case report forms are completed thoroughly.  This position will work with several senior lab staff on several exercise oncology trials. Responsibilities: Lead data collection procedures.  Contact participants to schedule and collect data per protocol.  Use all case report forms as designed by the protocol, document all activities per good clinical research guidelines.   Ensure protocol adherence to the best of ability. Ensure the safety of research and participant information. Comply with federal, state, and sponsor policies, as well as Institutional policies, standard operating procedures (SOPs), and guidelines. Ensure data collection documentation is completed. Perform data entry into appropriate databases and organizing source documentation appropriately, as needed. Gather data for the Project Manager regarding project scheduling/timelines, coordinating meetings, preparing preliminary data, researching references, and formatting accuracy according to funding agency specifications. Additionally, assist project manager with answering any queries that are issued by the sponsor, or requested by a team member for their study. Analyze and recommend improvements to policy and procedures. Other duties as assigned by the project manager or lab manager Job Summary Executes protocol-related research procedures, activities, outreach, and education. Manages a complex program or study or multiple programs and studies. Collects and analyzes data and complies with all policies and regulations. Recommends improvements to policy and procedure. Essential Functions Executes protocol-related research procedures, activities, outreach, and education. Manages a complex program or study or multiple programs and studies. Collects and analyzes data and complies with all policies and regulations. Recommends improvements to policy and procedure. Physical Effort This staff person will conduct exercise testing and will need to be able to demonstrate all exercises in the testing protocols for multiple studies. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Program Coordinator II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Program Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification ACSM-ACS Cancer Exercise Specialist Certification preferred Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am-5 pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005543": {
      "title": "Research Project Manager",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Project Manager (26005543) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Project Manager (26005543) Job Description Research Project Manager UPCI Research Lab-Schmitz, Kathryn - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005543 ) This position is to serve as a Research Project Manager for the Schmitz Lab and will lead many of the operational aspects required for several exercise oncology research projects. This position requires a highly self-directed professional who exercises sound judgment, takes ownership of outcomes, and requires minimal supervision. The Research Project Manager will coordinate research activities involving multiple sites. These exercise oncology studies require the development and maintenance of connections with members of the study team, including principal investigators and clinicians, as well as research participants, IRB members, and clinical staff. The Research Project Manager will use Good Clinical Practice (GCP) guidelines to help develop techniques and procedures that promote the efficient completion of complex research projects and tasks. Other responsibilities include: - Managing project budgets - Overseeing the work of interns and junior study staff - Using national and institutional research policies to recruit subjects - Obtaining informed consent - Scheduling study-related appointments - Collecting and coordinating study data - Troubleshooting issues that occur before, during and after patient visits - Managing regulatory documents - Analyzing data - Assisting with the preparation and submission of grant applications and scientific manuscripts -Coordinating study activities across multiple research sites Job Summary Manages all aspects of one or more projects for a research program and oversees all aspects of the project lifecycle. Provides leadership, technical direction, coordination, and expertise across projects. Analyzes progress and/or performance and prepares reports. Ensures compliance with budget, scope, timeline, and regulations. Assists with external communications. Essential Functions Primarily sedentary. May be required to stand for extended periods of time at lab bench. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Project Manager Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Program Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification ACSM-ACS Cancer Exercise Specialist Certification preferred Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am-5 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005585": {
      "title": "Research Nurse (SOMMA)",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Nurse (SOMMA) (26005585) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Nurse (SOMMA) (26005585) Job Description Research Nurse (SOMMA) GSPH-Epidemiology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005585 ) Job Summary Supports clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews lab results, patient data, and lab specimens; administers medications and protocol-specific treatments. Performs general laboratory duties and specialized nursing duties, trains new staff, and ensures regulatory adherence. Essential Functions The Health Studies Research Center (HSRC), Department of Epidemiology is seeking a Research Nurse Coordinator to work on several research projects within HSRC focusing on healthy aging and prevention of disability and mobility loss. Projects will include observational studies and clinical trials, and will involve all aspects of research including recruitment, screening, clinical measures, safety monitoring, data management and outcomes investigation, staff training and supervision. The Research Nurse Coordinator will also serve as a Medical Safety Officer.  Responsibilities may include the following: Train, certify and supervise study staff and student research assistants on the study protocol, conduct periodic refresher training sessions as needed, and conduct performance evaluations on study staff Assist PI and Project Director with IRB submissions, grant management, NIH reporting and other regulatory and administrative activities Conduct clinical measurements (anthropometric measures, blood pressure, heart rate, vision, physical performance and cognitive function testing, etc.) and administer study-related questionnaires. Work with the study data manager and the main study coordinating center to ensure data collection, entry and editing is accurate and complete, and all required data elements are transferred to the study coordinating center Coordinate and monitor the study visit schedule (including scheduling participants) Work with recruitment coordinator to ensure goals are met Perform telephone and in-person eligibility screening Conduct telephone visit reminder calls and follow-up assessments Attend to study participant incidents that may arise during study visits and communicating these to the study MDs. Address study alerts, adverse events, and incidental findings as per protocol Compile study endpoint documentation to support participant-reported health events. Perform phlebotomy, processing and shipment of biological samples as needed Participate in study working groups and virtual and in-person meetings as requested Physical Effort Generally sedentary The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Nurse II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research - Nursing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor of Science in Nursing Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification RN Work Schedule 8:30a-5:00p, M-F Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005521": {
      "title": "Institutional Engagement and Learning Development Assistant Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Institutional Engagement and Learning Development Assistant Director (26005521) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Institutional Engagement and Learning Development Assistant Director (26005521) Job Description Institutional Engagement and Learning Development Assistant Director Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005521 ) The Engagement and Wellbeing Assistant Director advances Pitt’s commitment under Plan for Pitt 2028 to cultivate a welcoming, engaged community (Pillar 3). This serves as a strategic consultant for the community and leads the design and delivery of education, training, professional development, and workshops that help build a culture of belonging, connection, and wellbeing among all stakeholder groups across the university. The individual in this role will be a skilled facilitator, educator, and program designer who is energized by building the conditions for people and the university community to thrive. Situated within the Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing, this role sits at the intersection of organizational culture, learning, and engagement strategy. The incumbent in this role will support a broader range of campus community-building initiatives including the Pitt Inclusion Network. The Assistant Director works collaboratively with campus partners, including Human Resources and Student Affairs, to ensure that campus engagement and wellbeing education aligns with the university’s broader talent, retention, and organizational development landscape. Required Qualifications •      Bachelor’s degree in organizational development, human resources, education, or a related field. •      Minimum of four (4) years of experience designing and facilitating education, professional development, training, or workshop programming in an organizational or higher education setting. •      Demonstrated experience collaborating with subject matter experts and cross-functional partners to develop curriculum and programming content. •      Strong facilitation and presentation skills with the ability to engage diverse audiences across a variety of formats and settings. •      Excellent project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously. •      Knowledge of adult learning principles and evidence-based approaches to education and professional development. •      Commitment to equity, inclusion, and creating learning environments where all people feel seen and supported. Preferred Qualifications •      Master’s degree in a relevant field. •      Experience in workplace wellbeing, employee engagement, or organizational culture initiatives. •      Familiarity with assessment tools, program evaluation, and data-driven approaches to learning design. •      Experience working in a complex, decentralized institution such as a research university. Job Summary Manages an overall organization educational engagement for faculty, staff, and students with respect to institutional engagement and wellbeing. Works with leadership on engagement strategies and to support efforts to retain students, faculty, and staff. Assists in the strategic planning of educational outreach, educational initiatives for faculty and staff, and policy. Executes comprehensive cross-cultural educational opportunities. Essential Functions •      Design and deliver education, professional development, and workshop programming for the Pitt community that directly advances a culture of belonging, wellbeing, and engagement within the university community. •      Develop and help facilitate workshops, seminars, and learning series—both in-person and virtually—on topics such as psychological safety, inclusive workplaces, resilience, and community connection. •      Identify, engage, and collaborate with internal and external subject matter experts to co-develop strategies to impact the campus •      Conduct ongoing needs assessments to ensure programming remains relevant, accessible, and responsive to the evolving needs of a diverse campus community. •      Build and maintain a library of educational and professional development resources to support asynchronous and self-directed learning aligned with the office’s culture and wellbeing priorities. •      Coordinate with Human Resources to ensure programming complements—without duplicating—existing workforce development and training efforts. •      Establish evaluation frameworks and track metrics to assess programming reach and effectiveness, contributing to the office’s data-informed culture. •      Stay current on research and best practices in workplace wellbeing, belonging, and adult learning in higher education contexts. •      Represent the office in relevant university committees and working groups related to engagement and wellbeing. Physical Effort Duties are primarily sedentary. Must be able to use a computer at a desk or similar workstation, and travel to on-campus meetings as needed. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Institutional Engagement & Wellbeing Assistant Director Job Family Human Resources Job Sub-Family Institutional Engagement & Wellbeing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005442": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Clinical Research Operations",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Director, Clinical Research Operations (26005442) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Director, Clinical Research Operations (26005442) Job Description Assistant Director, Clinical Research Operations Med-Critical Care Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005442 ) The Multidisciplinary Acute Care Research Organization (MACRO) within the Department of Critical Care Medicine, is seeking an Assistant Director, Clinical Research Operations. This managerial position is responsible for directing the implementation of multiple study sites, directing multiple projects across varying timelines, using established and newly developed procedures at new enrolling clinics and surgical sites, related training, troubleshooting, and developing recommendations. Workforce management duties include but are not limited to study site service management, workload assignment, performance and training management, data collection, recruiting, forecasting, and analysis. Position requires the ability to regularly travel within and outside of Oakland to study sites. Incumbent will be required to perform on-call duties 7-10 days per month. Job Summary Manages the administrative aspects of the department, including budget and financials, and oversees all clinical research activities and trials. Assists with operational and strategic planning. Crafts clinical research grant proposals and subsequently oversees administrative and financial functions of sponsored projects. Essential Functions Position requires the ability to make independent decisions regarding study operations. Must be able to work at a computer using multiple software programs and make frequent visits to various ICUs and other campus locations to facilitate enrollment in research studies. Physical Effort The incumbent must be able to stand for extended periods and walk for extended distances. No heavy lifting required. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Assistant Director - Clinical Research Operations Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30am - 5:00pm; hours may vary based on business needs Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005415": {
      "title": "Education & Compliance Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Education & Compliance Coordinator (26005415) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Education & Compliance Coordinator (26005415) Job Description Education & Compliance Coordinator Educational and Compliance Office - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005415 ) The Education and Compliance Support for Human Subject Research (ECS-HSR) Coordinator will be responsible for monitoring clinical research protocols associated with faculty held investigational drugs and devices, conducting Quality Assurance Reviews, Research Investigator Start-up Education and performing audits as requested. All compliance activities must be summarized in a written report, provided to the applicable Principal Investigator and presented as applicable to the Compliance Activity Review Subcommittee. The ECS-HSR Coordinator will also be responsible for providing education to the research community. Involvement in educational events ranges from one-on-one trainings provided during compliance reviews to presentations at seminars involving faculty, staff and students. Job Summary Serves as regulatory liaison for all clinical sites, coordinating centers, and data management centers and performs grant approval reviews and assists with regulatory reviews. Coordinates investigator training sessions, assists with compliance investigations, maintains databases, and develops approval guidelines to ensure institutional compliance with all regulations, policies, and applicable regulations. Essential Functions Monitor clinical trials conducted under inversigator-sponsored IND or IDE applications. Perform quality improvement initiatives/compliance reviews of IRB approved protocols throughout the University. Review and analyze research records and medical records for protocol adherence, adverse events and unanticipated problems involving risks to human sujects or others. Review IRB correspondence for complex clinical trials. Communicate with all levels of faculty and research staff. Attend monthly meetings of the Compliance Activity Review Subcommittee. Attend IRB Executive Committees as necessary. Participate in ECS-HSR educational programs for the research community. Maintain up-to-date information regarding federal regulations and ehtical considerations, and IRB policies related to the use of human subjects in research. Perform audits as requested by the IRB Executive Committee and Office of Research Protection (ORP) leadership. Assist with other ORP activities as needed. Computer skills, and excellent verbal and wrtiten communication skills. Physical Effort Must be able to lift 10 pounds and travel to various locations on the Oakland and Shadyside campuses. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Compliance Specialist II Job Family Compliance & Audit Job Sub-Family Research Compliance Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification BSN or MSN with prior human subject biomedical research experience or BS with applicable experience in clinical trials.  CCRC Certification through the Association of Clinical Research Professionals and/or CCRP certification through SOCRA and/or CIP certification though PRIM&R are desirable.  Prior clinical research experience is preferred.\n\nRN, CCRC, CIP  preferred. Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m.- 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003380": {
      "title": "Research Compliance Specialist I",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Compliance Specialist I  (26003380) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Compliance Specialist I  (26003380) Job Description Research Compliance Specialist I Med-Neurological Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003380 ) Job Summary Assists to serve as regulatory liaison for all clinical sites, coordinating centers, and data management centers and assists with grant approval reviews and regulatory reviews. Coordinates investigator training sessions, assists with compliance investigations, maintains databases, and collaboratively assists with developing approval guidelines to ensure institutional compliance with all regulations, policies, and applicable regulations. Essential Functions The University of Pittsburgh Department of Neurological Surgery is hiring a Research Compliance Specialist I. This position will be responsible for Regulatory duties for neurological surgery research studies and assist as needed with study coordination, not as primary coordinator. Manage regulatory responsibilities for research efforts in the Department of Neurosurgery, including coordinating with study team members to prepare and submit IRB applications (study start-up, modifications, continuing reviews, and required reporting). Maintain well-organized regulatory documentation to ensure compliance with institutional and federal guidelines.  FDA reporting experience is preferred but not required. Collaborate with external sites to obtain regulatory approvals and support the management of regulatory files for multisite sIRB studies. Assist other study staff with duties related to overall study execution to ensure efficient and compliant project operations.  The University reserves the right to assign other duties to employees that are not listed in this job description. Interested candidates, please go to Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh and use requisition #26003380 to apply for this position. The University of Pittsburgh is an Affirmative Action/ Equal Opportunity Employer and values equality of opportunity, human dignity, and diversity, EOE, including disability/vets. Physical Effort Lab - Requires some bending, stooping, and stretching. Walking around laboratory benches and various common laboratory rooms within the Division. The candidate will use stairs often and may have to make multiple trips between common equipment rooms between floors. Requires normal range of hearing and eyesight to record, prepare, and communicate laboratory methods and results. Requires lifting up to 20lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Compliance Specialist I Job Family Compliance & Audit Job Sub-Family Research Compliance Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F 8:30am-5pm Occasional Mornings, Evening and Weekends as needed Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005484": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005484) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005484) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician UPCI Basic Research Administration - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005484 ) The Leukemia and Drug Development Lab (LDDL-P) at UPMC Hillman Cancer Center is seeking a highly skilled and motivated Research Assistant to join a dynamic laboratory focused on developing next‑generation cellular therapies for hematologic malignancies. The successful candidate will support preclinical studies involving engineered immune cells, including NK‑ and T‑cell platforms, and will perform a broad range of advanced technical duties such as cell culture, multi‑parameter flow cytometry, molecular assays, and maintenance of primary cell‑based models. The Research Assistant will work closely with investigators, trainees, and clinical research partners to ensure smooth laboratory operations, generate high‑quality experimental data, and support ongoing therapeutic development programs within the Hillman cellular therapy research ecosystem. The LDDL-P is in the Assembly building. We are a diverse team focused on studying the etiology, pathogenesis, treatment, and cure of hematological malignancies. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions •    Contribute to collective team effort. •    Document and organize research results and data according to NIH’s preferred good laboratory management practices (LabArchives). •    Make independent contributions to projects and studies based on evidence-based literature. •    Independently work on projects and troubleshoot problems. •    Perform statistical and graphical analysis of data, interpretation of data and validity of testing. •    Maintain timely project goals, deadlines, and studies for contributions to publications and grant funding applications. •    Analyze and communicate results and data analysis from high throughput sequencing platforms. •    Molecular biology techniques desired: o    Sterile cell culture techniques o    Tissue culture and related wet lab techniques (i.e. western blotting, functional assays). o    Isolation of NK and T-cells from blood o    Optimize and perform in vitro immune assays o    Flow cytometry o    DNA isolation and cloning technique including PCR o    Gene editing of cell lines and primary cells with CRISPR-Cas9 electroporation or viral transduction o    Some animal handling Physical Effort Moderate physical effort required. May be required to stand/move for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am-5 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered Yes Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003124": {
      "title": "Senior Program Manager, CGM",
      "description": "Job Description - Senior Program Manager, CGM (26003124) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Senior Program Manager, CGM (26003124) Job Description Senior Program Manager, CGM SPIA-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003124 ) The Senior Program Manager oversees the planning, coordination, and implementation of CGM’s research initiatives, with a primary focus on the Pluralism360@Pitt program, which advances civil discourse, civic leadership, and value pluralism across campus and the broader community. The role is embedded in the academic life of the Center, working alongside faculty, graduate students, and undergraduate researchers. The Senior Program Manager serves as the central programmatic liaison connecting faculty leadership, university units, and a wide network of external partners, and is responsible for ensuring the successful delivery of all program commitments. This position is 100% funded by non-operating funds. The Center for Governance and Markets (CGM) at the University of Pittsburgh is a multidisciplinary research center that explores the innovative ways people come together to solve problems. It serves as a global hub for scholars and practitioners studying how institutions — formal and informal — shape governance, civic life, and human flourishing. The Pluralism360@Pitt program is a flagship initiative designed to foster civil discourse, civic leadership, and value pluralism across campus and throughout the Pittsburgh region and beyond. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in political science, philosophy, economics, social sciences, or a related field. Demonstrated experience managing complex grants or project management experience, including direct responsibility for coordinating across multiple external partners, subcontractors, or institutional stakeholders. Familiarity with philosophy, politics, and economics frameworks, whether through academic training, professional experience, or sustained independent study. Strong relationship-building skills across diverse communities, institutions, and ideological perspectives. Excellent organizational, written, and verbal communication skills. Experience with project management tools and digital documentation systems. Comfort working in a viewpoint-diverse, university-based research environment. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a relevant field. Experience integrating AI-enabled tools into project management, communications, or reporting workflows. Substantive familiarity with civil discourse, viewpoint diversity, pluralism, or bridge-building work. Experience working with university, nonprofit, or government partners on civic engagement, pluralism, or civil discourse initiatives. Familiarity with program evaluation frameworks. Job Summary Manages and ensures effective research project completion. Oversees complex and concurring projects and supervises team. Coordinates research operations, answers inquiries, and prepares research reports and materials. Designs and implements an organizational system, quality control procedures, and systems for maximum utilization of project resources. Implements communications plans, obtain applicable regulatory approvals, and ensure adherence to regulations, policies, and procedures. Essential Functions Program Leadership & Implementation Lead the day-to-day coordination and implementation of the Pluralism360@Pitt program and other CGM research initiatives. Maintain continuity and alignment across all project components, proactively monitoring progress against milestones and addressing implementation challenges as they arise. Ensure timely delivery of all required outputs and activities in accordance with grant commitments. Partnership & Community Engagement Serve as the primary programmatic liaison among faculty leadership, university units, and external partners — including civic, religious, nonprofit, and community organizations across Pittsburgh and the greater tri-state region, as well as national and global partner organizations. Lead community-engaged programming and applied civic leadership initiatives rooted in value pluralism. Build and sustain trust-based relationships across ideological, cultural, religious, and institutional divides, ensuring programming authentically reflects the project’s commitment to value pluralism and civil discourse. Represent CGM’s mission and approach in conversations with scholars, civic leaders, and community partners across diverse traditions. Grant Compliance & Reporting Coordinate closely with CGM leadership, SPIA Dean's Office, and Pitt’s Office of Sponsored Programs to ensure all grant compliance, reporting, and evaluation requirements are met. Track program outputs, participation data, and deliverables. Maintain clear and organized documentation to support evaluation, reporting, and replication of program activities. Project & Information Management Manage internal project management systems, digital repositories, and communications workflows. Ensure accurate and up-to-date records across all program components. Physical Effort Primarily sedentary. May occasionally be required to lift or transport materials or supplies and to move between locations on campus for meetings or events. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Supervisor - Research Program Coordinator Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Program Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Resume, Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005375": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Job Description - Financial Aid Counselor (26005375) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Financial Aid Counselor (26005375) Job Description Financial Aid Counselor Admissions & Financial Aid - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005375 ) Job Summary Analyzes applicant financial aid information, selects candidates, and determines awarded financial aid. Assists in financial aid policy preparation and in applications for government loan program federal funds. Conducts applicant interviews and administers assigned financial aid programs. Essential Functions Analyzes financial information submitted by applicants using established federal and University standards and guidelines to determine financial needs; selects candidates and determines the type and amount of financial aid to be awarded. Assists in the preparation of student financial assistance policies for the University. Corresponds and conducts interviews with applicants and their parents, counsels students and answers inquiries from various sources on financial aid policies and procedures. Assists in making application for federal funds for government loan programs; administers rules and regulations set forth by the federal government concerning government funds. Coordinates and administers assigned financial aid programs such as the state grant programs; maintains contact with external individuals to carry out program activities; develops and implements new initiatives within assigned program areas. Prepares detailed reports and compiles information concerning undergraduate financial aid and assigned programs as requested by the federal government and University officials Physical Effort Most work is sedentary, completed within an office setting. Some counseling/presenting is performed at other campuses and off-campus sites. Employee must be able to move about the campus to meetings and travel to locations outside of the University of Pittsburgh. Employee may be required to carry a box of material up to 50 lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Financial Aid Counselor Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Financial Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., some mornings, evenings and weekends may be req Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005382": {
      "title": "Staff Clinician, Licensure Track",
      "description": "Job Description - Staff Clinician, Licensure Track (26005382) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Staff Clinician, Licensure Track (26005382) Job Description Staff Clinician, Licensure Track Counseling Center - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005382 ) The University Counseling Center (UCC) is a department within the Division of Student Affairs and aligned under the Wellness Team consisting of Campus Recreation, Student Health Services, Care and Resource Support, and Financial Wellness. Accredited by the International Accreditation of Counseling Services (IACS) and American Psychological Association (APA), the UCC exists to ensure healthy and thriving lives for the University of Pittsburgh's diverse student population by providing crisis intervention, outreach, workshops, group, individual, and relationship therapy. Consistent with the University and Division of Student Affairs' mission and values, members of the UCC team are committed to cultural humility, justice, and inclusion. As a staff with our own diverse identities - both visible and invisible - we seek to provide support that honor students' unique needs, concerns, and personhoods. The University of Pittsburgh is seeking a recent Master's graduate to join the UCC as Pre-Licensed Clinician with generalist experience (additional training or experience with eating disorders, trauma, and/or substance use is welcomed). This clinician will provide direct and indirect services in the UCC including but not limited to individual, relationship, and group therapy; clinical consultation; outreach programming; and clinical supervision and training as assigned. This clinician will have the opportunity to serve on committees within and outside of the UCC. Job Summary Provides targeted, advanced-level, clinical psychotherapy services addressing a range of mental health concerns for a broad population of students/clients utilizing specialized techniques to foster student development, remediate mental health problems, and promote positive mental health. Facilitates comprehensive assessments and treatments, referrals for hospitalizations, and case reviews. Essential Functions - Participates in twice weekly individual supervision as well as one hour of group supervision per week. - Provides clinical psychotherapy services for a range of mental health concerns, including prevention and crisis services, individual and group therapy, intake services, and outreach. - Utilizes specialized techniques to foster student development, remediate mental health problems, promote positive mental health, develop individual treatment plans, and support academic success. - Works with students, veterans, Office of Disability Services, and other specialized populations, faculty, and other University staff as needed. - Facilitates coordination of services. - Collaborates with the medical psychiatrist when required; provides back-up for other therapists. Physical Effort This position is a sedentary role with occasional light physical effort. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Licensed Professional Counselor Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Behavioral & Mental Health Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Required Licensure/Certification LPC or LMFT or CAADC or LCSW Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification This position is intended for recent graduates working toward licensure; independent licensure not required; LSW or LAPC preferred. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30-5p, with occasional evenings and weekends Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005430": {
      "title": "Staff Clinician-HEART",
      "description": "Job Description - Staff Clinician-HEART (26005430) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Staff Clinician-HEART (26005430) Job Description Staff Clinician-HEART Counseling Center - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005430 ) The University Counseling Center (UCC) is a department within the Division of Student Affairs and aligned under the Wellness Team consisting of Campus Recreation, Student Health Services, Care and Resource Support, and Financial Wellness. Accredited by the International Accreditation of Counseling Services (IACS) and American Psychological Association (APA), the UCC exists to ensure healthy and thriving lives for the University of Pittsburgh's diverse student population by providing crisis intervention, outreach, workshops, group, individual, and relationship therapy. Consistent with the University and Division of Student Affairs' mission and values, members of the UCC team are committed to cultural humility, justice, and inclusion. As a staff with our own diverse identities - both visible and invisible - we seek to provide support that honor students' unique needs, concerns, and personhoods. The University of Pittsburgh is seeking a clinician to join the UCC as a member of the Higher Education and Response Team (HEART) team with interest and/or experience in crisis intervention. This clinician will work closely with the The University of Pittsburgh Police/Public Safety to provide support and crisis intervention to students with emergent behavioral/mental health concerns. This clinician will also provide individual and group therapy; clinical consultation; outreach programming; and clinical supervision and training as assigned. This clinician will have the opportunity to serve on committees within and outside of the UCC. Job Summary Provides individual and group counseling, crisis intervention, and drug and alcohol assessments; creates assessments and therapeutic courses of action. Creates and facilitates student psycho-educational, prevention, and support groups as well as student success programming. Instructs undergraduate classes; administers campus-wide initiatives. Assists to train interns and staff. Essential Functions - Respond to students experiencing urgent or crisis concerns in collaboration with University of Pittsburgh Police/first responders - Co-respond to welfare checks and other crisis calls for student with emergent mental/behavioral concerns - Engage in risk assessment and safety planning - Transport and support students for further assessment at local facilities - Provide individual counseling, group counseling, clinical consultation, outreach programming, crisis intervention, and case management - Provide supervision and training to Master's level trainees/interns Physical Effort This position requires a mixture of sedentary responsibilities and movement around campus when responding to welfare checks and crisis calls. The employee must be comfortable driving a vehicle in and around the Oakland campus when traveling to and from calls and when transporting students to emergency facilities. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Social Worker Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Behavioral & Mental Health Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Required Licensure/Certification MSW + LCSW Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification LPC, LCSW, or LMFT preferred Work Schedule Hours vary - generally 12:30p to 9p, Monday through Friday Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005102": {
      "title": "Accountant",
      "description": "Job Description - Accountant (26005102) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Accountant (26005102) Job Description Accountant Student Financial Services - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005102 ) Student Financial Services (SFS) is a unit within the Controller's Office, which is part of Finance & Operations at the University of Pittsburgh. Student Financial Services (SFS) is responsible for student billing, payment processing, and related technology operations serving students across all campuses. This position supports the accounting and reporting functions of SFS under the direction of the Associate Director for Accounting & Reporting. It performs complex fiscal and accounting tasks related to student accounts receivable, general ledger reconciliation, loan fund administration, and financial reporting, and contributes to the accuracy, integrity, and compliance of student financial records. For more information regarding Pitt Finance & Operations, please visit our website at: https://www.financeoperations.pitt.edu/ Job Summary Facilitates complex fiscal, accounting, accounting analysis, and general ledger functions. Prepares budgets, financial forecasts, and research. Serves to resolve high-level issues. Essential Functions Prepares and maintains general ledger journal entries for student accounts receivable, loan funds, and clearing accounts, ensuring accuracy and timeliness of the university's financial records. Reconciles student information system data to the general ledger on a recurring basis, investigating and resolving discrepancies before they affect student accounts and institutional financial reporting. Supports preparation of the Annual Operating Reports and FISAP financial sections of federally mandated reporting requiring specialized knowledge of Title IV loan fund compliance. Supports bad debt reserve calculations and prepares supporting documentation for write-off recommendations, requiring judgment specific to student receivable accounting. Serves as an accounting resource within SFS, interpreting fiscal regulations and policy to ensure compliance in day-to-day transaction processing. Physical Effort Must be able to sit for prolonged periods of time. Must be able to use a computer, keyboard, and mouse for extended periods. Must be able to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Occasional lifting of materials or equipment up to 10 pounds may be required. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Accountant III Job Family Finance & Procurement Job Sub-Family Accounting & Financial Reporting Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005408": {
      "title": "HR Data Analyst",
      "description": "Job Description - HR Data Analyst (26005408) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - HR Data Analyst (26005408) Job Description HR Data Analyst Pitt IT Analytics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005408 ) We are seeking an HR Data Analyst to join our team and play a critical role in transforming complex employee data into actionable insights for HR leadership and partners across the University. This position will leverage analytics tools and platforms to analyze large HR datasets, develop comprehensive reporting solutions, and drive data-informed decision-making across the University. In this role, you will partner closely with HR leadership and stakeholders to understand their analytical needs — often starting from ambiguous or loosely defined requirements — and translate those needs into concrete technical solutions, while distilling the resulting complexity into clear, actionable insights for non-technical audiences. You will use SQL to merge, transform, and analyze data across multiple systems, including Oracle HCM, Taleo, Salesforce, and third-party benefits vendor platforms. You will also build automated data workflows that streamline business processes and improve data quality across the team's reporting pipeline. And you will build, update, and maintain dashboards in Tableau to visualize this data. You will also collaborate closely with Pitt Digital's broader technical team, who manage enterprise data and reporting platforms across the University, to ensure your analyses and dashboards are built on reliable, well-governed data infrastructure. Required Qualifications 5+ years of professional experience in data analysis or a related role Experience with HR/organizational people data (e.g., headcount, turnover, recruiting metrics) and the judgment to interpret it correctly, avoid common pitfalls (e.g., data lag, org restructuring effects, voluntary vs. involuntary turnover), and communicate findings clearly to non-technical audiences Proficient in SQL, including ability to write joins, understand and write complex queries Understands the concept of data grain (e.g., one row per employee vs. one row per employee per pay period) and applies it to write SQL queries that avoid duplication, incorrect joins, or misleading aggregations Strong experience with visualization tool (Tableau preferred) for dashboard & report development, including calculated fields, parameters & advanced visualizations Working knowledge of Python, R, or similar programming languages for data manipulation & analysis Strong knowledge of data manipulation, cleaning & wrangling techniques Experience with Alteryx for data automation or transformation preferred Applicants should include salary requirements in cover letter.  -------------- The University offers a robust retirement savings plan with 100% employer match, 150% after vesting. 11 Paid Holidays. Paid Vac, Sick, Personal. Add'l Winter Recess Paid Time Off. Paid Parental Leave. Above-average Employer Contribution toward Medical, Prescription Drug, Dental, Vision, Life, and more. Education benefits for staff, spouses/ partners, dependents. Student loan assistance. Free transit pass. --------------- On 8-13-26, Forbes listed Pitt among the 100 best employers in the commonwealth, ranking third among higher education institutions.  This is the 6th year Pitt has been on Forbes' America's Best-in-State Employers list for PA. Join the team responsible for strategy, implementation, and maintenance of technology at the University of Pittsburgh—ranked by Forbes among Amazon, CDW, Cisco Systems, Google, LinkedIn, and Microsoft as one of “America’s Best Large Employers.” Job Summary Evaluates business requirements and performs advanced data integration and analysis. Develops advanced analytical and reporting tools utilizing multiple sources of integrated data. Provides technical support. Essential Functions Must have the ability to work with PC equipment and related hardware/software and telephony video-conferencing systems. Must have good written and verbal communication skills, as well as, analytical, organizational, and planning skills.  Must have proficient knowledge of IT and HR information systems. Physical Effort Generally sedentary desk work with computer-keyboard video phone other than traveling to other buildings on campus for meetings/events on occasion. Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Data Analyst III Job Family Information Technology Job Sub-Family Analytics Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F bus hrs EST.  On occasion, some evening and weekend work may be necessary depending on business load, project timeline requirements, urgent support, or scheduled downtime changes. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001284": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Technician (26001284) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Technician (26001284) Job Description Laboratory Technician Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26001284 ) The Renal-Electrolyte Division is seeking a Laboratory Technician I to work within one of our NIH (National Institutes of Health)- and DOD (Department of Defense)- and Department of Veterans Affairs (VA)- funded laboratories. Our laboratory employs exciting cutting-edge methods from a variety of disciplines, including molecular biology, cellular biology, and animal physiology and pathology to investigate molecular pathways leading to progressive kidney injury. Job Summary Performs laboratory testing and some analysis on multiple types of specimen samples. Operates and properly sterilizes equipment and maintains inventory and assists with ordering. Essential Functions Performs laboratory testing and assays. Prepare and test multiple types of specimens. Operates and maintains laboratory equipment and laboratory cleanliness. Keeps detailed and accurate data and logbooks. Organizes/documents results. Maintains inventory, orders supplies/chemicals/reagents. Organizes rodent colony and performs animal manipulations, surgeries, etc. Physical Effort Moderate physical effort required. May be required to stand/move for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8.00a - 4.30p (designated timeframe flexible) Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range 18.50-20/hr dependent upon chosen candidate Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005348": {
      "title": "Immigration Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Immigration Specialist - Student Team (26005348) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Immigration Specialist - Student Team (26005348) Job Description Immigration Specialist - Student Team University Center for International Studies - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005348 ) The Office of International Services is seeking an Immigration Specialist for the student team. This position services as immigration advisor for students in F and J status, providing accurate information and guidance, and processing applicable casework. Serves as liaison between the University and government agencies and as a resource for the University. Works closely with administrative contacts in departments across campus to ensure compliance for both the students and the University. Job Summary Facilitates legal immigration applications and processes and serves as liaison between the University and  government agencies and as a resource for the University. Ensures accurate document processing and the University's compliance. Performs international credential evaluations for the admissions process. Essential Functions Communicates with international students in F and J status via email, in-person meetings, online meetings, and presentations to provide information and resources so that students can maintain legal status in the US. Coordinates with faculty, staff, employees, and students throughout the University in facilitating and maintaining lawful immigration status. Ensures compliance with immigration/visa rules and regulations by educating faculty and department administrators on the unique limitations of international students. Serves as resource for all University members and affiliates regarding visa matters. Answers non-routine and complex immigration/visa related questions and assists in resolving issues. Maintains relationships with government agencies, sponsoring organizations, and foreign embassies to facilitate visa documentation and employment authorization for foreign students. Maintains accurate records in University systems (e.g. Peoplesoft, Sunapsis) as well as SEVIS. Compiles information and prepares various reports and analyses establishing progress, describing adverse trends, and stating recommendations and/or conclusions. Prepares required reports on foreign students and employees for various government agencies. Remains competent and current through self-directed professional reading, developing professional contacts with colleagues, attending professional development courses, and attending training and/or courses as directed. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Immigration Coordinator II Job Family Legal Job Sub-Family International Legal Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $55,000 - $60,000 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004554": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coord II",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coord II (26004554) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coord II (26004554) Job Description Clinical Research Coord II Med-Cardiothoracic Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004554 ) The Lung Transplant Research Division at UPMC is a dynamic and highly specialized research department dedicated to advancing clinical knowledge and improving outcomes for lung transplant patients. The division supports a diverse and growing research portfolio, currently managing clinical research studies in various phases of enrollment, start-up, and follow-up, with additional studies anticipated in the near future. The research team consists of one dedicated Research Coordinator and two Primary Investigators who work collaboratively with a multidisciplinary group of ancillary support staff, including Physician Assistants (PAs), Certified Registered Nurse Practitioners (CRNPs), operating room personnel, physicians, and other clinical and administrative staff. Together, these individuals contribute to the successful execution of research activities, regulatory compliance, patient recruitment, data collection, and study oversight. Research activities are conducted across multiple UPMC facilities, including the UPMC Shadyside Medical Building, Falk Medical Building, and the UPMC Presbyterian operating rooms, requiring close coordination among clinical and research personnel. This position plays a critical role in supporting the division's research mission by ensuring high-quality study conduct, fostering collaboration among multidisciplinary teams, and contributing to the ongoing expansion of innovative research opportunities within the Lung Transplant Program. Qualifications Required: Bachelor's degree in a health science, biological science, nursing, public health, or related field. Experience coordinating clinical research studies or equivalent research experience; knowledge of clinical research methodology and regulatory requirements; strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills; proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel. Qualifications Preferred: Clinical research coordination experience in transplant, thoracic surgery, pulmonary medicine, or related specialties.  Experience with patient screening, recruitment, and informed consent processes: experience with protocol management and regulatory submissions to the IRB and other oversight committees; experience with research databases and electronic data capture systems; familiarity with GCP, human subject protections, and research compliance requirements. Job Summary Conducts research assessments on study participants. Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Assists with training staff. Ensures adherence to protocols and corrects issues with data collection. Essential Functions The position will coordinate and manage day-to-day operations of clinical research studies within the Lung Transplant Program; screen, recruit, consent, and enroll research participants in accordance with approved protocols and regulatory requirements; maintain compliance with Good Clinical Practice (GCP), institutional policies, sponsor guidelines, and applicable federal regulations. GCP compliance is a foundational component of research study conduct.  In addition, the position will be responsible for: Prepare and submit regulatory documents, including but not limited to Institutional Review Board (IRB) submissions, continuing reviews, amendments, and study closures. Coordinate study visits, specimen collection, and research-related procedures. Perform accurate and timely data collection, entry, verification, and database management. Maintain study files and regulatory binders and ensure completion of required study documentation. Assist investigators with protocol implementation and ongoing study management. Collaborate with multidisciplinary clinical and research teams across multiple locations. Participate in study monitoring visits, audits, and sponsor communications as needed. Physical Effort Ability to sit, stand, and walk for extended periods of time. Ability to travel between UPMC Presbyterian and UPMC Shadyside campuses. Ability to transport study materials and equipment as needed. Must have reliable transportation for travel between clinical and research sites. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005330": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Clinical Services",
      "description": "Job Description - Associate Director, Clinical Services (26005330) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Associate Director, Clinical Services (26005330) Job Description Associate Director, Clinical Services Counseling Center - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005330 ) The University Counseling Center (UCC) is a department within the Division of Student Affairs and aligned under the Wellness Team consisting of Campus Recreation, Student Health Services, Care and Resource Support, and Financial Wellness. Accredited by the International Accreditation of Counseling Services (IACS) and American Psychological Association (APA), the UCC exists to ensure healthy and thriving lives for the University of Pittsburgh's diverse student population by providing crisis intervention, outreach, workshops, group, individual, and relationship therapy. Consistent with the University and Division of Student Affairs' mission and values, members of the UCC team are committed to cultural humility, justice, and inclusion. As a staff with our own diverse identities - both visible and invisible - we seek to provide support that honor students' unique needs, concerns, and personhoods. The University of Pittsburgh is seeking a qualified clinician to join the UCC as a Staff Clinician with generalist experience (additional training or experience with eating disorders, trauma, and/or substance use is welcomed). The Staff Clinician will provide direct and indirect services in the UCC including but not limited to individual, relationship, and group therapy; clinical consultation; outreach programming; and clinical supervision and training as assigned. The Staff Clinician will have the opportunity to serve on committees within and outside of the UCC. Job Summary Leads team and develops and implements counseling center crisis outreach programs and associated trainings. Facilitates needs assessment, strategic planning, and outcome assessment of programs and develops related program materials. Provides therapeutic services and monitors clinical records for compliance with regulations. Compiles outreach program data, develops programs, and collaborates to provide services. Essential Functions Oversight and management of all clinical programs, services, and operations Management of the electronic medical record Consultation resource for staff, faculty, parents, and families with concerns about a student Management of high-level crises impacting the larger campus community Clinical oversight and supervision of complex and high-acuity clinical cases Primary responsibility for developing and implementing center policy and procedures Supervision of both clinical and administrative staff Provision of clinical psychotherapy services for a range of mental health concerns Provides clinical back-up and coverage for other clinicians as needed Keeps accurate and timely clinical documentation abiding by all compliance regulations Physical Effort This role is primarily a sedentary position with occasionally light physical effort. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Assistant Director - Counseling Center Outreach & Training Programs Job Family Community & Government Job Sub-Family Community Outreach Program Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Independent licensure (LPC, LCSW, LMFT, or Licensed Psychologist) required. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30a - 5:00p, with occasional evenings/weekends Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005353": {
      "title": "Emerging Technology and Simulation AV Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Emerging Technology and Simulation AV Specialist (26005353) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Emerging Technology and Simulation AV Specialist (26005353) Job Description Emerging Technology and Simulation AV Specialist SVC HS Information Technology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005353 ) The Emerging Technology and Simulation AV Specialist works under the Health Sciences Information Technology - Educational Technology Team supporting the University’s six Health Science Schools. This position supports the operation, maintenance, and advancement of audiovisual systems and immersive technologies used in simulation and instructional environments. This role partners with faculty, simulation staff, and IT to ensure reliable, high-quality learning experiences supported by integrated AV and extended reality (XR) technologies The Emerging Technology and Simulation AV Specialist operates out of Scaife Hall and is primarily responsible for supporting our two Emerging Technology Labs and one clinical skills lab in Scaife Hall as well as a second clinical skills site at 5 th Avenue and Halkett Street. Preferences: 2 years of AR/VR experience AVIXA certification, CompTIA A+ or Medical Education background is a plus, but not required Job Summary Manages and performs work across multiple areas of the University’s Information Technology (IT) platform and infrastructure. Conducts analyses for proposed IT projects. Assists with team members' goal determinations. Provides IT support and coordinates network activities. Essential Functions • Install, configure, maintain, and troubleshoot AV systems in simulation labs, clinical skills spaces, and technology enhanced classrooms • Support integrated recording and debrief systems for simulation activities • Provide live technical support during high-stakes simulation events and assessments • Support immersive technologies used in health sciences education, including platforms such as the Anatomage Table, GigXR, and 3DOrganon applications • Support AR/VR hardware and software platforms; maintain device inventory and lab equipment • Assist faculty and staff in deploying immersive learning technologies • Assist with support of AV-supported events as needed • Participate in system upgrades, room builds, and AV integration projects as needed • Maintain system documentation and configuration standards • Provide training and user support for simulation, AV and emerging technology tools Physical Effort Moderate physical effort required. May be required to stand/move for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Information Technology Program Supervisor Job Family Information Technology Job Sub-Family IT Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F, 8:30-5; with some off hours as needed Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005184": {
      "title": "Director of Student Involvement",
      "description": "Job Description - Director of Student Involvement (26005184) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director of Student Involvement (26005184) Job Description Director of Student Involvement Involvement & Student Unions - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005184 ) This is an exciting opportunity to lead one of the University's most visible and impactful student-facing departments. Reporting to the Associate Dean of Student Engagement, the Director of Student Involvement provides strategic leadership for a department that shapes the co-curricular experience for thousands of students each year. The Director will oversee a talented leadership team responsible for Campus Programs, the Student Organization Resource Center (SORC), Leadership Development, and Experience Pitt—the University's student engagement platform. Together, these areas support more than 800 registered student organizations, signature campus traditions, leadership programs, student media, and countless opportunities for students to build community and develop lifelong leadership skills. Leading a team of 25 professional staff, 5 direct reports, and approximately 85 student employees, the Director will play a pivotal role in advancing student engagement while partnering across the University to foster an inclusive, vibrant campus community. The Director will also serve as the primary advisor to the University’s undergraduate Student Government Board, providing leadership, guidance, and coaching, and assistance navigating University partners and resources. Job Summary Executes strategic alignment, long-term planning, operational planning, and management oversight of major college, campus, or University-wide student affairs functions. Establishes the direction, goals, implementation strategy, evaluation means, student initiatives, and policies of the department. Maintains responsibility for budgetary matters. Directs effective communications, promotions, and public relations for the department. Essential Functions Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Education, Organizational Leadership, Counseling, Public Administration, or a related field. Six (6) or more years of progressively responsible leadership experience in student affairs, campus activities, student engagement, leadership development, student organizations, residence life, orientation, student success, or related areas. Experience supervising and developing professional staff. Demonstrated experience managing departmental operations, budgets, and strategic initiatives. Strong communication, collaboration, and relationship-building skills. Commitment to fostering inclusive environments where all students can thrive. Ability to utilize assessment, data, and outcomes to support continuous improvement. Additional Preferred Qualifications Experience advising student government or comparable student leadership organizations. Experience leading complex student engagement programs at a large college or university. Experience navigating complex student issues, campus partnerships, and organizational change. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Director - Student Affairs Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. The Division of Student Affairs supports flexible work arrangements with a combination of in-person and remote work days each week.  This role will require in-person presence on campus for some weekend and nighttime events, including weekly student government board meetings. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered Yes Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005315": {
      "title": "AI Data Scientist",
      "description": "Job Description - AI Data Scientist (26005315) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - AI Data Scientist (26005315) Job Description AI Data Scientist SHRS-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005315 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences (SHRS) is a nationally renowned leader in the field of health care education, research, and clinical practice preparation. With 14 different disciplines related to health and rehabilitative care, SHRS shapes future generations of health care professionals—therapists, counselors, advocates, scientists, providers, and practitioners—trained to serve the needs of all people regardless of background, levels of health, or mobility. We are built on a legacy of academic excellence and innovation and fueled by passionate educators and researchers, allowing us to meet the health care and rehabilitation needs of today and drive meaningful change in the future. Learn how bold moves SHRS. https://www.shrs.pitt.edu/about/how-bold-moves-shrs The University of Pittsburgh School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences (SHRS), in partnership with Pitt’s Department of Biomedical Informatics (DBMI), is seeking a data scientist to oversee a large, complex data set, the Rehabilitation Datamart With Informatics Infrastructure for Research (ReDWINE).  ReDWINE draws electronic medical records data from UPMC’s extensive clinical and payor systems and organizes it for analysis by rehabilitation scientists.  The data scientist will work under the direction of Dr. Yanshan Wang, Associate Professor, to utilize advanced programming methods for raw data extraction and aggregation, statistical analysis, and document programming to create analytic data files.  He/she will be part of a larger team of SHRS research leaders and Pitt informaticists and information technologies specialists who collaborate on ReDWINE’s development and management.  The preferred candidate must have a master’s degree, a strong interest in academic research, and experience in managing large data sets, performing statistical analysis, documentation, and reporting. Experience and knowledge of skillsets weighted more heavily Experience with database design, database programming skills, SQL skills Experience designing ETL solutions Expert in one or more programing languages (Java and Python preferred) Experience with data model design, data standards, ontology design is a plus Experience with data warehousing, Hadoop/data lake platform implementation is a plus Experience with IT platform implementation in a technical and analytical role is a plus Experience of writing, submitting, and publishing scientific articles Job Summary Oversees large, complex data sets and utilizes advanced programming methods and statistical software for raw data extraction and aggregation, statistical analysis, and document programming to create analytic data files. Creates statistical reports; assists with manuscripts, grants, and regulatory submissions. Maintains data infrastructure and tracks data assets. Adheres to all protocols. Essential Functions The candidate will design, implement, and maintain the IT infrastructure using enterprise-level Java programming language. Requires experience in Java, SQL, and infrastructure system design. Ability to track and finish project milestones, research data warehouse development, and report to the stakeholders. Responsible for leading the clinical data retrieval, data analysis activities will be conducted using customized Python programming language. In addition, the candidate will also summarize the results in scientific articles and submit to academia conferences and journals. The candidate will communicate with several stakeholders, including rehabilitation researchers to understand the demands, the Pitt internal R3 office to understand the Neptune data warehouse operation, and health informatics faculties for the overall strategy. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Data Scientist III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Data Science Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 6 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Master's degree, or equivalent experience, in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, or related field. \nThe successful candidate will design, implement, and maintain the IT infrastructure, primarily Java, Python, and/or C/C++.\nRequires experience in Java, SQL, Python, and the design of database systems. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005361": {
      "title": "Patient Account & Billing Manager",
      "description": "Job Description - Patient Account & Billing Manager (26005361) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Patient Account & Billing Manager (26005361) Job Description Patient Account & Billing Manager Dent Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005361 ) Since 1896 the School of Dental Medicine has been educating students to take their places among the best dental practitioners in our region and across the country. Each day the School’s faculty and staff contribute to its mission to advance the future of dental medicine through teaching, research, and service. In addition to being a great place to work the University offers robust benefits including : *11 Paid Holidays in addition to paid Vacation, Sick and Personal Days * Additional Paid Time Off (Winter Recess) during the period between Christmas and the New Year * Paid Parental Leave * Education benefits for eligible employees, their dependents and spouse/domestic partner * Above-average Employer Contribution towards Medical, Prescription Drug, Vision, Life, STD, and LTD Insurance plans * A robust retirement savings plan option, including 100% match on employee contributions of 3-8% (150% after vesting) and enhanced match for those nearing retirement * Free PAT bus pass. Job Summary Reviews medical insurance claims and medical charges and ensures appropriately assigned diagnosis code and procedure code. Investigates insurance company denials, processes difficult claims, and resolves moderately complex issues. Audits patient accounts, answers inquiries for assigned accounts, and updates related billing and financial documents and software. Essential Functions The candidate must have excellent communication and customer service abilities.  Working knowledge of medical/dental diagnosis and procedure coding (e.g. ICD-10, CPT) and familiarity with dental EHR software is preferred.  This position will be responsible for, but not limited to, the following functions: liaison between the faculty practice and 3rd-party billing agency, ensure accurate claims processing, assist in claim denials and follow ups, timely payment posting, effective resolution of billing and patient account issues, manage provider procedure entries, assist in researching/locating insurance EOBs and initiate and manage outbound calls to patients regarding outstanding balances. Physical Effort Work is performed in an office environment and requires the ability to operate standard office equipment and keyboards. Position requires moderate physical effort. May be required to sit or stand for an extended time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Medical Billing Lead Job Family Finance & Procurement Job Sub-Family Medical Billing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
