    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005155": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services (26005155) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services (26005155) Job Description Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services SHRS-Counseling and Behavioral Health - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005155 ) University of Pittsburgh School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences Department of Counseling and Behavioral Health - Pittsburgh, PA The Department of Counseling and Behavioral Health at the University of Pittsburgh invites applications for a full-time staff member to serve as a mental health clinician and to direct counseling services provided at School of Health and Rehabilitation Science’s (SHRS) Wellness Pavilion. We are seeking an Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services to offer clinical mental health counseling services to residents of the Homewood and other areas served by the University of Pittsburgh.  This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Counseling and Behavioral Health or designee. The Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services will be embedded at the SHRS Wellness Pavilion, located in Homewood.  The SHRS Wellness Pavilion offers the residents of the community a variety of student-led healthcare and educational services to foster health and well-being.  The successful candidate will deliver counseling services, oversee clinical operations, supervise graduate students, participate in community engagement activities, and drive quality-improvement initiatives that advance patient outcomes and community health.  This clinician will guide our graduate students in the principles and practice of high-value, patient-centered care. The Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services will also provide services through our partner organization, Primary Care Health Services (PCHS).  This staff member will regularly interact with faculty and staff from the University of Pittsburgh's clinical mental health counseling program regarding student training. Estimated start date: October 1, 2026 This position is housed within the University of Pittsburgh, School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences (SHRS), Department of Counseling and Behavioral Health. Pitt SHRS faculty, students, and alumni are leaders in transforming the education and delivery of health care. The Department of Counseling and Behavioral Health offers personalized, experiential training for future professional counselors and prepares graduates to address complex challenges faced by individuals across cultures, across the lifespan, and living with disabilities and behavioral health conditions. The department emphasizes evidence-based practice, clinical research, community engagement, advocacy, and a strong commitment to diversity, inclusion, and cultural humility. The Assistant Director of Community Counseling Services provides leadership and operational oversight at the SHRS Wellness Pavilion, delivering mental health counseling and operational oversight at the SHRS Wellness Pavilion, delivering mental health counseling and behavioral health services, supervising University of Pittsburgh clinical mental health counseling students, community engagement activities, and providing services through our partner PCHS.  The role involves conducting clinical assessments, developing and implementing individualized therapy programs, coordinating services across multiple stakeholders, and ensuring compliance with clinical, regulatory, and documentation standards.  The incumbent will also serve as a key liaison with external partners including community organizations, referral sources, and other service organizations.  There may be opportunities to become engaged in community engaged clinical research. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS -Master's degree in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Clinical or Counseling Psychology, Clinical Social Work, or a related field. -Licensure or licensure-eligibility in Pennsylvania: Licensed Professional Counselor, Licensed Clinical Social Worker, or licensed psychologist. -Minimum of three (3) years of relevant clinical experience. -Strong background in evidence-based clinical intervention, assessment, and service provision for individuals with mental/behavioral health challenges. -Experience providing individual, family, couples, and/or group counseling/psychotherapy. -Demonstrated ability to conduct clinical assessment, case conceptualization, and functional intervention. -Strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills. -Ability to manage multiple priorities and supervise graduate students. -Ability to maintain confidential records and comply with ethical and legal standards. -Strong cultural awareness/humility/competence and awareness of the influence of social determinants of health. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS -Clinical supervisory experience. Job Summary Contributes to the development of strategic goals and plans for clinical services. Assists with human resource actions. Identifies funding opportunities and prepares grant proposals. Conducts clinical therapy services as directed. Essential Functions ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS -Provide leadership and supervision to graduate students delivering counseling services. -Manage daily operations of the SHRS Wellness Pavilion behavioral health programs including service coordination, referral screening, and scheduling. -Conduct clinical assessments and develop individualized intervention and treatment plans. -Ensure quality assurance and adherence to clinical protocols and documentation standards. -Collaborate with multidisciplinary staff, clinical mental health professionals, and external partners. -Maintain clinical documentation, data tracking, and be familiar with utilizing Electronic Medical records (e.g. Medent). -Support program outreach, training, and community engagement related to counseling services. Physical Effort PHYSICAL AND TRAVEL REQUIREMENTS This is an in-person position located at the SHRS Wellness Pavilion in the Homewood community of Pittsburgh, PA.  Daily presence at the Wellness Pavilion or PCHS is required. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Services Assistant Director Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Clinic Operations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Licensure or licensure-eligibility in Pennsylvania: Licensed Professional Counselor, Licensed Clinical Social Worker, or licensed psychologist. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 4:00pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001094": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician III",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician III (26001094) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician III (26001094) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician III Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26001094 ) Job Summary Performs a variety of independent laboratory work and experiments such as determining experimental protocols and preparation of specimens and cultures. Prepares reports of findings subsequent to compilation and analyzation. Oversees specimen inventory. Develops documentation for publication; crafts manuscripts and grant proposals. Essential Functions Incumbent will work under the direct supervision of a junior faculty PI who studies metastatic disease using novel organ-on-a-chip technology. Perform, analyze and interpret mammalian cell culture and molecular biology experiments.   These experiments will include cell passaging and maintenance, western blotting, extracellular vesicle isolation, multiplex assays, immunofluorescence, immunohistochemistry, processing of human tumor specimens and liver cells, and set up and running of single and multi-organ-on-a-chip systems Experiments with mice.   This will involve preparing cancer cells and treatments for injections as well as helping with injections, monitoring mice and end point surgeries The incumbent will also be expected to analyze and interpret the results generated from the experimental work, have basic mathematical skills (such as dilutions, ratios, molarity, etc.) along with strong organization, communication and planning skills. Strong organization, communication and planning skills are required. Physical Effort This position is primarily sedentary.   However, there will be some walking between collaborative laboratories. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003299": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26003299) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26003299) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003299 ) The Pulmonary, Allergy, Critical Care and Sleep Medicine Division of the DOM. The division is made of up approximately 70 clinical staff and over 100 research staff who work in a variety of locations including: Bridgeside Point, Biomedical Science Tower (BST), UPMC Hospitals including Presbyterian, Shadyside, East, Jameson and Mercy. The division provides world class services across 10 inpatient services at five hospitals and over 70,000 outpatient office visits. We have a major research mission that focuses on basic, clinical, and translational research on the lung, microbiome, COVID-19, sleep medicine, and allergy and immunology. The coordinator assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Conducts hands-on subject recruitment. Screens subjects to determine eligibility, including reviewing medical records. Schedules and completes study visits and follow-up appointments according to protocol timelines. Conducts participant interviews and administers questionnaires. Maintains organized, thorough, and accurate source documentation and study records. Ensures timely completion of source documentation and electronic data entry. Works well both independently and as part of a collaborative team. Occasional travel to offsite clinics that are not accessible by public transportation will be required. The ideal candidate should have strong attention to detail, organizational capabilities, and a demonstrated ability to respond to inquiries from participants and clinical staff in a timely and professional manner. Excellent oral and written communication skills, along with strong interpersonal abilities, are essential for building rapport and maintaining trust with participants, their families, multidisciplinary team members, and physicians. Job Summary Conducts research assessments on study participants. Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Assists with training staff. Ensures adherence to protocols and corrects issues with data collection. Essential Functions • Developing and enacting recruitment plans for sleep-related research studies. • Coordinating protocol-related research procedures, study visits, and follow-up appointments. • Completing and overseeing data collection, entry, and management. • Maintaining thorough, accurate, and organized documentation in compliance with regulatory and protocol requirements. • Establishing and maintaining strong rapport with potential and enrolled participants through prompt and regular telephone, text, and email communication. Physical Effort Must be able to: Sit and stand for prolonged periods of time Walk between buildings on campus Use computer, telephone, copier, fax, and other essential office equipment The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. This position may require occasional flexibility in work hours, including availability during evening hours as needed. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005198": {
      "title": "Research Technician II",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Technician II (26005198) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Technician II (26005198) Job Description Research Technician II Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005198 ) This position is for the Division of Genetic and Genomic Medicine within the Department of Pediatrics. The successful Research Technician II will be conducting preclinical trials experiments to validate the efficacy of therapeutic agents in treating metabolic disorders using mouse disease models. The incumbent will be responsible for performing a variety of animal and laboratory experiments and procedures, preparing specimens from animal sources, overseeing supply management, and operating and properly maintaining equipment. Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions The position is primarily for someone to conduct experiments with mice and is expected to manage mouse colonies, assemble cohorts and treat mice with therapeutic agents. • Collect tissue from mice and prepare samples for analysis. • Isolate cells for cell culture, if needed. • Performs a variety of laboratory experiments, molecular techniques, and related technical functions, testing, troubleshooting, and analysis. Identifies and prepares specimens. • Oversees supply management: ordering, procurement, tracking estimates, and receiving items. • Operates and maintains applicable laboratory equipment for job functions. • Keeps detailed, accurate, and timely data and log books. Organizes and documents results. Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Position will require flexibility with shift/hours; evenings and weekends possible, depending on experimental needs. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications. Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005194": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Nurse II",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse II (26005194) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Nurse II (26005194) Job Description Clinical Research Nurse II Med-Neurological Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005194 ) Job Summary Supports clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews lab results, patient data, and lab specimens; administers medications and protocol-specific treatments. Performs general laboratory duties and specialized nursing duties, trains new staff, and ensures regulatory adherence. Essential Functions The Department of Neurological Surgery at the University of Pittsburgh is in search of a Clinical Research Nurse II. This positions duties include but are not limited to the following. The CRN II will support clinical research projects by coordinating projects and drug trials, assessing patients' qualifications, and facilitating protocols. Collects and reviews patient data including medical histories and physical assessments, lab specimens and lab results and monitors results for adverse reactions; assists in study medication accountability and monitoring adverse events and protocol-specific treatments. Assesses patients for inclusion and Assesses patients for inclusion and performs specialized nursing duties such as arterial puncture, venipuncture, and operation of electronic monitoring equipment; assists with lumbar puncture and multi-modality intracranial monitoring procedures. Maintains and enters data into databases/logs in a timely and accurate manner. Participates in the development of internal review board submissions as requested. Collaborates with multiple investigators, sponsors, and research coordinators. Assists with training of new staff and ongoing guidance of newer staff. This position will require on call rotations. Minimum education to be considered for this position is a Bachelor of Nursing. Interested candidates, please go to Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh and use requisition #26005194 to apply for this position. The University of Pittsburgh is an Affirmative Action/ Equal Opportunity Employer and values equality of opportunity, human dignity, and diversity, EOE, including disability/vets. Physical Effort Must be able to walk, stand, or sit for long periods of time. Must be able to use computer, telephone, copier, fax, and other essential office equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Nurse II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research - Nursing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor of Science in Nursing Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Required Licensure/Certification RN Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification RN license in PA is required Work Schedule M-F 8:30am-5pm Occasional Mornings,  Evenings and Weekends as needed and On Call Rotations Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
