    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005249": {
      "title": "Data Coordinator III",
      "description": "Job Description - Data Coordinator III (26005249) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Data Coordinator III (26005249) Job Description Data Coordinator III Med-Cardiothoracic Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005249 ) Experience abstracting data from the electronic medical record preferred. Prior involvement in a research project preferred. Job Summary Collects, inputs, updates, and maintains accurate data on computer systems and in archives. Prepares, compiles, reviews, and verifies data. Designs and prepares advanced reports and data visualizations. Organizes and manipulates data and stores security and backup data files. Essential Functions Active involvement in the systematic migration of data from legacy databases to current databases. Data abstraction from the electronic medical record for assigned projects, presentations, and publications. Physical Effort Must be able to sit for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Data Coordinator III Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Data Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005206": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005206) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician (26005206) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician Med-Cardiovascular Institute - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005206 ) Research under the direction of Dr. Xiangyu Zhang focuses on understanding the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying cardiometabolic diseases, including atherosclerosis. The lab has a particular interest in macrophage and adipocyte metabolism, autophagy/lysosome biology, mTOR signaling, and related inflammatory and metabolic pathways. The research uses a combination of mouse models, primary cells/cell lines, human monocytes/macrophages, standard molecular and cellular biology approaches, and clinical/translational studies. Main Duties: Assist with day-to-day laboratory experiments and general research activities in the lab. Help with mouse colony management, including coordinating with the animal facility, monitoring breeding, weaning, genotyping, and maintaining accurate colony records. Assist with animal-related experimental procedures, sample collection, tissue processing, and preparation of materials, in accordance with approved protocols and institutional guidelines. Perform basic molecular and cellular biology techniques, such as PCR/genotyping, tissue processing, immunostaining, RNA/protein extraction, and other standard lab assays as needed. Maintain organized laboratory records, assist with ordering and inventory, prepare reagents, and help with general lab organization and compliance. Job Summary Performs a variety of laboratory experiments and procedures. Prepares specimens. Oversees supply management. Operates and properly maintains equipment. Essential Functions Experience in basic biomedical laboratory work, including molecular and cellular biology techniques such as PCR/genotyping, DNA/RNA/protein extraction, tissue processing, and other standard lab assays as needed. A very important component of the position will also be working with mice and helping maintain the mouse colony, including breeding, weaning, genotyping, accurate record keeping, coordination with the animal facility, animal handling, sample collection, and tissue harvesting in accordance with approved protocols and institutional guidelines. Physical Effort Must be able to move between university labs and offices.  May require long periods of standing, bending, walking, kneeling.  Movement of lab animals and equipment as needed. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule mon-friday standard Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided Yes Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005176": {
      "title": "Veterinary Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Veterinary Technician (26005176) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Veterinary Technician (26005176) Job Description Veterinary Technician DLAR-Surgical Research Facility - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005176 ) The individual will serve as a Veterinary Technician within the Division of Laboratory and Animal Resources (DLAR). The individual will: • assist DLAR veterinarians with the provision of veterinary medical care and maintenance of animal colony health, • provide animal study support and perform animal technical procedures under the direction of a veterinarian, and • periodically provide animal husbandry and care or cage wash support to meet the operational needs of the facility. The preferred candidate will have a college degree in animal science or a similar biological science, certification by the American Association for Laboratory Animal Science (AALAS), completion of an AVMA CVTEA accredited veterinary technician program and have a licensed, certified, or registered veterinary technician status. The successful candidate must demonstrate strong attention to detail, interpersonal communication, customer service, and organizational skills. The position requires ability to: work some weekends, evenings, and holidays, travel to multiple buildings in a timely manner, pass criminal, Drug Enforcement Act (DEA[AC2.1]) and social background checks, and possibly obtain Child Protection Clearances and/or Select Agent Clearances, and successfully enrollment in the University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program, and other medical surveillance/immunization programs, as dictated by the current research activities. Vaccination and/or TB testing may be required. Job Summary Provides support to veterinarians, fellow technicians, and researchers to provide laboratory animal care and research support, daily monitoring of animal well-being, and cleaning and maintenance of clinical areas. Assists with procedures, provides surgical and anesthesia support, triages cases, performs medical imaging, administers medications, and other various related duties. Maintains documentation and ensures compliance with all applicable regulations. Orders and maintains supply inventory. Essential Functions The employee must be able to: • Perform veterinary technician skills and procedures, • Have sufficient visual acuity and manual dexterity to recognize and identify normal and abnormal species-specific clinical appearances and behavior patterns, perform veterinary technical procedures (including euthanasia), safely handle and restrain animals, and operate and maintain facility equipment and supplies, • Negotiate around equipment within close quarters, and move between rooms, workspaces, and facilities, • Work with a variety of animal species, biohazards, chemical and radiation hazards, and wear personal protective equipment (PPE), • Work directly with live or dead animals and clean or soiled bedding and caging, • Successfully enroll in the University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program (AESP) and other medical surveillance/immunization programs as dictated by current research activities, • Receive vaccinations and health assessments, including TB testing, required to work in some animal holding or procedure areas, in accordance with DLAR and/or EH&S policies and practices, • Perform computer skills including the ability to utilize common applications (e.g., email, Word, Excel) and DLAR systems (ex: CAMs), • Read, understand, and follow DLAR and other institutional guidance documents (SOPs, policies), including IACUC approved animal protocols, • Follow written and verbal instructions, • Accurately and effectively communicate in English, verbally and in writing, • Work variable scheduled during on-call coverage, and some weekends and evenings and holidays, as required to support research operations, and • Travel between DLAR facilities in a timely manner. Physical Effort The employee must be able to: • Stand for extended periods of time throughout most of the workday, • Lift and move objects weighing up to 50 pounds including but not limited to caging and equipment, bags or boxes of animal diet and animal bedding, and operate equipment to move heavier objects or weights exceeding 50 pounds, • Perform repetitive motion tasks that involve pushing, pulling, reaching, and/or bending, and • Physically handle and restrain a variety of small and large laboratory animals. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Veterinary Technician Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Animal Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification ALAT Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Required Licenses/Certifications (short open text field. ) AALAS Certification at the Laboratory Associate Animal Technician (ALAT) level required. External candidates will need to attain within 12 months. Work Schedule M-F, 7AM-4PM, some evenings, weekends and holidays as determined by business need Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Commensurate with experience. Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005172": {
      "title": "Visibility Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Visibility Director (26005172) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Visibility Director (26005172) Job Description Visibility Director GSPH-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005172 ) The Visibility Director serves as a strategic advisor to the Dean of the University of Pittsburgh School of Public Health, leading initiatives that enhance the School’s visibility, reputation, and impact. This role develops and executes creative communications campaigns aligned with the Dean’s priorities, leveraging expertise in visual storytelling, photography, videography, graphic design, and multimedia production. As a member of the School’s Communications team, the Visibility Director collaborates with senior leadership, faculty, staff, and departments to promote the School’s mission, achievements, and contributions to public health. A Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Marketing, Journalism, Public Relations, or a related field and at least five (5) years of relevant professional experience are required. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered in lieu of the degree requirement. Job Summary Oversees strategy and implementation of priority communications projects requiring cross-disciplinary and integrated approaches and serves as central campaign coordinator. Leads team and collaborates with senior leadership and internal clients on high-level communications campaigns. Establishes performance goals and measures and ensures adherence to style, branding, and regulations. Develops core messaging and creates campaign content. Essential Functions Candidate must be able to communicate clearly and effectively both in writing and verbally; must possess high-end reasoning and problem-solving abilities; must be able to manage multiple priorities and tasks, often under deadlines. The successful candidate will possess experience using multiple communications platforms and digital marketing tools. Physical Effort The position is largely sedentary, but the employee must be able to travel within the SPH building and across the University campus and surrounding area to attend meetings and events at various locations. Must be able to lift and transport equipment such as a laptop computer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Assistant Director - Communications Job Family Communications & Marketing Job Sub-Family Communications Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $75,000 - $90,000 annual Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter, Writing Sample, Media Sample Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000686": {
      "title": "Special Projects Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Special Projects Coordinator (26000686) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Special Projects Coordinator (26000686) Job Description Special Projects Coordinator Educ-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26000686 ) The School of Education Dean's Office is hiring a Part Time Special Projects Coordinator to handle administrative tasks, manage special projects, support school-wide events, and enhance outreach efforts. Reporting to the Executive Assistant to the Dean, this coordinator will provide support for initiatives such as the Transfer Pathways Summit, Community Transfer Scholars’ Program, Summer College Access Programs, the Dean’s Ignite Speaker Series (e.g., arrange housing, travel, and other logistical arrangements) etc. The role involves working closely with the SOE communications and marketing unit for event promotion, conducting program evaluations, and serving as a liaison with internal and external stakeholders. In addition to providing programmatic and project support, the coordinator will assist in: Planning networking events, partner engagement and community building activities. Monitoring program development, timelines, and communication. Maintaining calendars and scheduling of activities and events for various programs; as well as participation in SOE and campus committees, community events, meetings, and affiliated activities. Candidates should be: Proficient in Microsoft Office and Google G-Suite, Possess strong interpersonal, organizational, analytical, problem-solving, verbal and written communication skills; and demonstrate an understanding of organizational operations and problem-solving abilities. Align with the school’s values of integrity, equity, and excellence, and be able to work effectively with diverse faculty, staff, students, and community partners. Proficient in ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, to meet deadlines, understand and follow directions, pay attention to detail; keep and maintain accurate and detailed reports and records; work with sensitive information, maintain confidentiality and use discretion. Department Details (Continued) High School Diploma/GED and a minimum of 2 years of experience required Preferred Qualifications: * Bachelor's degree in Education, Psychology, Sociology or a related field * 3-5 years of project-based work is preferred. Job Summary Serves in an administrative capacity and provides administrative support to the project manager and other team members. Assists with fiscal management and compliance with federal regulations and the contracts. Manages day-to-day office operations and interacts with key stakeholders. Essential Functions • Serves in an administrative capacity and provides administrative support to the Dean's projects and other members of the Dean's office Senior staff. • Assists with managing the budget of events and projects. • Interacts with key stakeholders. • Manages daily office operations (responding to and sending correspondence, note taking, maintaining office calendars, scheduling meetings, processing orders), making reservations and travel arrangements, and handling other tasks. Physical Effort Position requires meeting with faculty, staff, and students in other parts of the building and throughout the campus as well as off campus. Mostly a sedentary position. Computer work is required. Light lifting, pushing, and pulling could be needed (less than 25lbs) for events or other activities. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Part-time regular Job Classification Staff.Project Coordinator Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Program & Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Varies during M-F 8:30am - 5:00pm, occasional work outside of normal business hours Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $18/hr - $24/hr Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005154": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Assistant II",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Assistant II (26005154) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Assistant II (26005154) Job Description Clinical Research Assistant II Med-OB-Gyn & Reproductive Science - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005154 ) Magee Womens Research Institute (MWRI) is the largest research institute in the US dedicated to women's health and reproductive biology.  Prior experience working in a clinical research environment is preferred. Job Summary Conducts research assessments and procedures independently. Oversees operations when leadership is unavailable. Recruits and screens participants, reviews records and surveys, and maintains databases. Performs routine data analysis and prepares reports, data visualizations, and models. Essential Functions Conducts research assessments/procedures independently, including obtaining vital signs and brief medical histories, processing specimens using centrifuge, performing phlebotomy, preparing samples for shipment, and assisting with other clinical procedures as directed. Oversees operations when leadership is unavailable; assigns work tasks and provides support. Recruits, screens, and enrolls research participants. Follows up with study participants to schedule appointments and maintain study retention. Reviews participants' medical records, collects and codes surveys, and verifies active status for participants. Attends relevant meetings and prepares reports, data visualizations, and basic models identifying progress and trends. Maintains and updates databases for registry assessments and clinical trial forms. Orders supplies, maintains inventory, and organizes laboratory. Performs data analysis involving routine procedures. Assists in preparing standard operating procedures and manuals. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Assistant II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004622": {
      "title": "Cagewash Technician I",
      "description": "Job Description - Cagewash Technician I (26004622) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Cagewash Technician I (26004622) Job Description Cagewash Technician I DLAR-Animal Husbandry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004622 ) The Division of Laboratory Animal Resources (DLAR) Cagewash Technician I will perform cagewash, equipment maintenance and sanitation activities. The candidate will: •    process soiled animal caging, sterilize and prepare clean caging and equipment for distribution within the animal facility •    operate and validate various types of cagewash equipment •    perform preventative maintenance and minor mechanical repairs to animal caging systems, sanitation and other equipment used to provide laboratory animal husbandry and care •    perform custodial duties including sweeping, mopping and scrubbing floors, removing trash, and cleaning equipment •    receive deliveries, reconcile orders and packing slips, organize, rotate and re-stock supply stations •    maintain logs of sanitation activities and verification of equipment function The successful candidate must consistently demonstrate positive interpersonal and customer service skills, be proficient with technology in order to use common applications (e.g. email, Microsoft Office, Pittworx), be available to work weekends and holidays, stand for extended periods of time, lift 50 pounds, push/pull heavy equipment and pass the mandatory criminal and social background checks.  Candidates working in the Rangos Research Building at Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh will need to obtain Child Protection Clearances.  Vaccinations and TB testing may be required. Pay rate is $18.63/hour. Job Summary Performs cagewash, sanitization, and equipment maintenance. Processes soiled animal bedding and waste, sterilizes and prepares clean caging, and maintains accurate logs. Performs routine preventative maintenance and minor mechanical repairs to equipment used in animal husbandry. Provides janitorial care for area. Processes deliveries; organizes stock and supply stations. Essential Functions The employee must be able to: •    read, understand, and follow DLAR and other institutional guidance documents (SOPs, policies), including IACUC approved animal protocols when applicable •    follow written and verbal instructions •    demonstrate sufficient fine motor skill to manipulate animals and equipment; negotiate around equipment within close quarters; move between rooms and workspaces •    have sufficient visual acuity to recognize animals inadvertently left in cages as well as automated equipment notifications and printouts •    have sufficient audible acuity to hear equipment alarms and other warnings •    wear facility specific Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) for extended periods of time required by the job duties based on risk assessment from EH&S •    work directly with live or dead animals and clean or soiled bedding and caging with reasonable accommodations if necessary •    accurately and legibly document written information in English in a timely manner, including electronic formats and applications (e.g., PRISM, CAMS) •    effective written and verbal communication in English, including the use of email •    receive vaccinations and health assessments, including TB testing, required to work in some animal holding or procedure areas in accordance with DLAR and/or EH&S policies and practices •    successfully enroll in the University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program (AESP) and other medical surveillance/immunization programs as dictated by current research activities Physical Effort The employee must be able to: •    stand for extended periods of time for the majority of the workday •    lift and move objects weighing up to 50 pounds including, but not limited to, caging and equipment, bags or boxes of animal diet and animal bedding •    operate flatbed hand trucks or pallet jacks to push/pull heavier objects or weights exceeding 50 pounds •    perform repetitive motion tasks that involve pushing, pulling, twisting, reaching, and/or bending •    physically handle and restrain a variety of small and large laboratory animals •    negotiate and navigate around animal facility caging, equipment, and the physical plant. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Cagewash Technician I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Animal Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification None required. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.; some weekends and holidays Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $18.63/hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005145": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Administrative Coordinator (26005145) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administrative Coordinator (26005145) Job Description Administrative Coordinator Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005145 ) The Department of Mechanical Engineering & Materials Science at Pitt has state-of-the-art research and educational facilities and strong connections to local industry. Today, Pitt-MEMS features innovative undergraduate and graduate programs and world-class research in advanced manufacturing and design, materials for extreme conditions, soft matter biomechanics, computational and data-enabled engineering, cyber-physical systems and security, and nuclear and other sustainable energies. Our undergraduate and master’s students have an outstanding placement record at leading companies, and our doctoral students have successfully found faculty positions at major universities in the U.S. and abroad, as well as cutting-edge research positions in industry and national laboratories. Job Summary Supports senior level roles in a wide variety of complex administrative and office functions as well as specialized technical support for academic or administrative departments. Essential Functions The Administrative Coordinator will provide advanced professional administrative support to the Chairperson, faculty and the Department Administrator in the Department of Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science of the Swanson School of Engineering. The incumbent will be responsible for performing daily administrative support functions in a highly professional and confidential manner. They will be responsible for overseeing maintenance of the Department’s website, drafting formal correspondence, memorandums, and other confidential documents as directed. The incumbent will also be responsible for organizing and maintaining a calendar and agenda for meetings, events, conferences, travel arrangements, and all other logistical needs for the Chairperson. In addition, the incumbent will be responsible for coordinating faculty searches, assisting new faculty with the onboarding process, hiring students, processing visa paperwork for international visitors, and coordinating the Department seminar series. The incumbent must demonstrate the ability to manage the challenges of supporting senior level personnel, always exercising flexibility and efficiency. As Administrative Coordinator, the incumbent must be congenial, have excellent interpersonal skills, and be able to function in a team environment. The incumbent must demonstrate exceptional communication and organizational skills as well as the ability to be flexible when working under deadlines and operate with a high degree of autonomy and discretion. The incumbent must also demonstrate the ability to function efficiently with a high degree of accuracy and confidentiality. Physical Effort Mostly sedentary.  Must be able to get around a university setting. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Administrative Assistant III Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule In agreement with manager Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $42,500 - $46,000 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005120": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician IV",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV (26005120) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV (26005120) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician IV Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005120 ) Job Summary Performs a variety of independent and complex laboratory work and experiments. Analyzes and interprets data, compiles results, and prepares reports. Maintains inventory, ordering, and logs. Writes manuscripts and grant proposals and prepares data visualizations. Essential Functions Performs a variety of laboratory experiments such as histology, flow cytometry, functional studies, molecular tecjniques, gene sequencing, and related technical functions, testing, troubleshooting, and analysis. Ensures conformity to specifications. Identifies and prepares specimens for cell separation and histology. Oversees supply management: ordering, procurement, tracking estimates, and receiving items. Operates and maintains applicable laboratory equipment for job functions. Keeps detailed, accurate, and timely data and log books. Organizes, documents, and analyzes results. Maintains, calibrates, cleans, and tests sterility of laboratory equipment. Trains students and laboratory personnel. Physical Effort The position is primarily sedentary but may require walking to other collaboration areas. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician IV Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided Yes Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004870": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Administrative Assistant (26004870) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Administrative Assistant (26004870) Job Description Administrative Assistant Nurs-Recruitment and External Relations - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004870 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing is seeking a qualified front desk administrative assistant. This role supports the operations of the School at the department level and supports the needs of its students, faculty and staff by assisting department leadership, welcoming visitors, and providing general clerical support. Scheduling & Meeting Support Schedules and coordinates meetings, appointments, and calendars for staff and/or supervisor(s), resolving scheduling conflicts as they arise. Sets up meeting rooms and equipment and provides logistical support during meetings and office events. Front-Desk & Customer Service Responds to routine questions from the public, staff, and clients via phone, email, or in person, and directs more complex inquiries to the appropriate person. General Administrative Support Provides day-to-day administrative support to assigned staff or department, including maintaining files and records, entering and updating data, tracking basic project tasks, and following up on deadlines. Assists in coordinating communication between departments, staff, and outside contacts, such as clients or service providers. Process Improvement Notices opportunities to make everyday tasks more efficient or accurate and suggests improvements to supervisors. Assists with rolling out new procedures, tools, or forms when asked. Document Preparation Types, formats, and proofreads letters, memos, reports, and other documents according to established templates and style guidelines. Handles confidential information (such as personnel or financial records) with appropriate discretion. Purchasing & Basic Vendor Contact Places routine orders for office supplies and materials, tracks receipts and expenses, and helps verify invoices for accuracy. Contacts vendors for basic order status, pricing, or delivery questions under supervisor guidance. General Clerical Duties Performs standard office tasks such as filing, photocopying, scanning, mail handling, and maintaining supply inventory. Completes other clerical or project-related tasks as assigned. The ideal candidate will demonstrate: Excellent time management and organizational skills Strong verbal and written communication skills Strong customer service skills Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite Attention to detail, flexibility, and problem-solving skills Positive and professional demeanor Ability to work both independently and as part of a team Job Summary Performs administrative assistant support work of moderate complexity. Essential Functions Schedule meetings and manage calendars. Provide logistical support during meetings and events. Answers phone, takes messages, and transfers calls. Provides general information and appropriately answers customer/faculty/staff/student inquiries. Administrative support activities and department specific technical or operations duties. Serve as liaison between internal and external stakeholders Prepares and edits various technical documents. Makes purchases, collects payments, verifies billing information. Performs variety of clerical duties, and project specific tasks Physical Effort Must be able to sit for prolonged periods of time.                                                                                                                       Must be able to climb a step ladder and lift up to 30lbs occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Administrative Assistant II Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $17.74---$22.17 hourly Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005113": {
      "title": "Laboratory Manager II",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Manager II (26005113) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Manager II (26005113) Job Description Laboratory Manager II Bioengineering - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005113 ) The Department of Bioengineering is seeking a Laboratory Manager II for the Batista Lab. The incumbent will maintain a colony of laboratory animals (non-human primates) for a neuroscience research lab. This position has a strong emphasis on hands-on animal work, including daily care, monitoring, and behavioral training of non-human primates. Beyond this, the position involves managing the day-to-day operations of the lab, ensuring compliance with regulations and best practices. Primary duties include: • Provide daily care and monitoring of non-human primates, including feeding, health checks, and maintaining animal welfare standards. • Perform animal handling, including pole/chair training and behavioral conditioning to prepare animals for experimental procedures. • Train animals to perform behavioral tasks required for neuroscience research protocols. • Prepare for and assist in surgical procedures; perform routine surgical tasks and instruct students on proper surgical techniques. • Maintain animal medical files, daily logs, and detailed records of animal health and behavior. • Order supplies and maintain inventory for animal care and laboratory operations. • Maintain, calibrate, and clean laboratory equipment as needed. • Assist with general laboratory tasks and collaborate with other lab members on research activities. • Coordinate onboarding and training of new lab members Ideal candidates will possess a Bachelor’s degree in a STEM field and have minimum of 3 years of experience working with animals, preferably non-human primates, in a research setting. Job Summary Manages day-to-day laboratory operations while ensuring compliance with safety regulations and best practices. Works with, adapts, and installs scientific equipment in research laboratories. Develops and collaborates on routine projects and procedures. Manages inventory and equipment and performs budget functions. Essential Functions Ability to speak clearly for telephone contact, have manual dexterity to use equipment, and also ability to visit various locations throughout the campus. Physical Effort This position requires daily animal interactions, which involves walking around the animal colony floor and standing for long periods of time. May occasionally lift up to 50 lbs. Incumbent may occasionally visit industry or other locations throughout the campus. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Manager II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided Yes Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004816": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Recruitment Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Undergraduate Recruitment Specialist (26004816) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Undergraduate Recruitment Specialist (26004816) Job Description Undergraduate Recruitment Specialist Admissions & Financial Aid - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004816 ) Job Summary Represents the University in new student recruitment and participates in the evaluation of applicants. Participates in recruitment activities and projects, both in and out of state. Essential Functions Helps coordinate both OAFA's and the School of Computing and Information's presence at admissions programs and recruitment events. Represents both offices by delivering presentations and facilitating Q&A sessions with prospective and admitted students and their families. Assists with developing and implementing recruitment strategies to attract a diverse and academically talented pool of first-year applicants. Acts as an academic expert, providing guidance on SCI majors, career pathways, and opportunities while collaborating with both OAFA and SCI staff throughout the recruitment process. Corresponds and interacts with prospective students, applicants, advisors, and others seeking information on admissions standards, academic programs, student experiences, and career outcomes. Conducts informational meetings with prospective students and their families. Physical Effort Mobility with regard to possible travel within the United States. Valid driver’s license is required. May be required to carry a box of material (up to 50 lbs.) from car and/or from building to building or between floors. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Admissions Counselor III Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Admissions, Enrollment, & Recruitment Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., some mornings, evenings and weekends will be required Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005059": {
      "title": "Police Officer (UPJ)",
      "description": "Job Description - Police Officer (UPJ) (26005059) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Police Officer (UPJ) (26005059) Job Description Police Officer (UPJ) Johnstown Campus Police - Pennsylvania-Johnstown - ( 26005059 ) Job Summary Ensures public safety in a multi-cultural environment. Police Officer duties include: vehicular and foot patrol of University property; enforcement of criminal and traffic laws; protection of persons and property; investigation of crimes; completion of police reports; testimony in court; and assistance to other law enforcement agencies. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in criminal justice or other related field from an accredited college or University and must have obtained Pennsylvania Act 120 certification prior to appointment; possess a valid PA driver's license as well as a safe driving record. Essential Functions Responsibilities include ensuring public safety in a multi-cultural environment. Police Officer duties include vehicular and foot patrol of University property; enforcement of criminal and traffic laws; protection of persons and property; investigation of crimes; completion of police reports; testimony in court; and assistance to other law enforcement agencies Physical Effort A physical fitness examination requiring running, jumping, sit-ups, and pushups is required. Ability to operate a motor vehicle and firearms. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in criminal justice or other related field from an accredited college or University and must have obtained Pennsylvania Act 120 certification prior to appointment; possess a valid PA driver’s license; as well as a safe driving record The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Union Eligible.Johnstown Police.Officer Campus Johnstown Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Required Licensure/Certification Pennsylvania Act 120 and a PA driver?s license with a safe driving record required. Work Schedule Schedule varies by need Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Per Collective Bargaining Agreement Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
