    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26000069": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26000069) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26000069) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26000069 ) Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Conducts research assessments on study participants. Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Assists with training staff. Ensures adherence to protocols and corrects issues with data collection. Essential Functions • Conducts research assessments on study participants. • Assists with and adheres to study protocols, and Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. • Assists with training staff on proper and best study research techniques as directed. • Mentors and educates staff and student workers as directed. • Ensures proper protocols are followed and quality assurance of research and related work. • Corrects data collection issues. • Phlebotomy experience desired. Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Shift determined by manager. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004992": {
      "title": "LEGAL CLINIC CONSULTANT",
      "description": "Job Description - LEGAL CLINIC CONSULTANT - School of Law Environmental Law & Policy Clinic (26004992) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - LEGAL CLINIC CONSULTANT - School of Law Environmental Law & Policy Clinic (26004992) Job Description LEGAL CLINIC CONSULTANT - School of Law Environmental Law & Policy Clinic Law-Instruction - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004992 ) This is a FULL-TIME, TEMPORARY 17-MONTH, GRANT-FUNDED, IN-PERSON POSITION. The individual in this role will not represent the University of Pittsburgh in a legal capacity or serve as an attorney for the institution nor will they perform any litigation duties in this position or for the University of Pittsburgh. This position offers an exceptional opportunity for an attorney experienced in public utility law to collaborate on a research project focused on electricity governance. The Legal Clinic Consultant (LCC) will work directly with the principal investigators at the University of Pittsburgh’s School of Law and the School of Public and International Affairs (SPIA). The LCC will apply legal and social science research methods and analysis to specific questions on electricity governance (1) decision-making at the Public Utility Commission of Pennsylvania (PA PUC) and the Public Utility Commission of Ohio (PUCO) pertaining to clean energy issues and (2) public participation at PA PUC and PUCO. The LCC will be credited as a co-author on the research papers and articles submitted for publication. Research support will be provided by law students currently at the School of Law. The Environmental Law & Policy Clinic (ELPC) is a cordial and supportive work environment and home to clinic students who are passionate about clean energy and environmental issues. ELPC works closely with faculty, staff and students at other units at the University of Pittsburgh that are focused on sustainability, including SPIA, the Center for Energy, and the Mascaro Center for Sustainable Innovation; with other law clinics, including the CELC; and with the American Bar Association Section on Energy, Environment and Natural Resources (ABA SEER). The ELPC director will provide career mentoring to the Staff Attorney, including introductions to the network of researchers and lawyers at the University of Pittsburgh, the energy and environmental community in PA and OH, and lawyers at the ABA SEER. Prof. Miranda Leppla, Director of CELC, who has decades-long experience representing clean energy clients at PUCO proceedings, and who has mentored other staff attorneys, will provide additional mentorship. Prof. Shanti Gamper-Rabindra, of the School of Public & International Affairs, will share her preliminary research design and preliminary list of prospective interviewees to jumpstart the collaborative research. The ELPC director, in collaboration with the CELC director, will support the overall project goal on building expertise in energy governance by developing curriculum and teaching law students about electricity markets and governance and building collaborations with other law clinics. Required Qualifications: J .D. from an accredited law school and admission to a state bar; Authorized to work in the United States (this position will not provide any sponsorship for work authorization); Demonstrated knowledge or interest in public utility regulation; Strong legal research and writing skills; Ability to manage complex research projects with attention to detail and timelines; Ability to work collaboratively with senior and student researchers; Experience conducting legal and social science research; Commitment to working the entire scheduled 17 months on the project to complete the deliverables. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in public utility law, energy regulatory practice, or PUC proceedings; Familiarity with PUC dockets, ratemaking or rulemaking practice, or energy agency proceedings in Pennsylvania, Ohio, or comparable jurisdictions; Demonstrated interest in legal scholarship and policy research (e.g., contributions to law review publications or policy reports); Knowledge of Pennsylvania or Ohio energy regulatory frameworks or comparable restructured markets; Experience in a law clinic, legal aid office, government agency, or other public interest legal setting; Experience interviewing or interacting with stakeholders or focus groups. Job Summary Assists in litigating cases before local and federal courts and administrative agencies. Advises upper-level law students and assists in planning and teaching clinic seminars. Engages in research projects utilizing legal education and expertise. May participate in community outreach events. The individual in this role will not represent the University of Pittsburgh in a legal capacity or serve as an attorney for the institution. Essential Functions The Environmental Law & Policy Legal Clinic Consultant will undertake collaborative research applying legal and social science research methods and analysis to specific questions on electricity governance and will be credited as co-author on the research papers and articles submitted for publication. Research support will be provided by law students currently enrolled at the School of Law. Research • Review and analyze PUC dockets, orders, and proceedings in Pennsylvania and Ohio, focusing on decisions involving renewable energy, energy efficiency, distributed energy resources, large load entities, and related issues; Conduct statutory and regulatory analysis of state public utility law frameworks in both states; Research and synthesize administrative law, case law, and agency guidance relevant to PUC decision-making and public participation. • Assess the technical, economic, and legal arguments presented by various intervenors and other stakeholders and PUC staff, judges, and commissioners in PUC proceedings; Contribute to the design of questionnaires to solicit the views of PUC staff and various stakeholders (e.g., energy and consumer groups and the public) to learn about public participation at PUCs; Secure interviews and conduct in-person and virtual interviews of PUC staff and other stakeholders in electricity governance issues. • Contribute to the drafting and submission of two or three high-quality research papers to social science or law journals. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Legal Clinic Consultant Job Family Legal Job Sub-Family Legal Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Juris Doctorate Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification Licensed Attorney Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8:30 a.m.-5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $80,000-$90,000 annually Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter, Writing Sample, Other (review job description for more details) Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004761": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Job Description - Financial Aid Counselor (26004761) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Financial Aid Counselor (26004761) Job Description Financial Aid Counselor Admissions & Financial Aid - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004761 ) Job Summary Analyzes applicant financial aid information, selects candidates, and determines awarded financial aid. Assists in financial aid policy preparation and in applications for government loan program federal funds. Conducts applicant interviews and administers assigned financial aid programs. Essential Functions Analyzes financial information submitted by applicants using established federal and University standards and guidelines to determine financial needs; selects candidates and determines the type and amount of financial aid to be awarded. Assists in the preparation of student financial assistance policies for the University. Corresponds and conducts interviews with applicants and their parents, counsels students and answers inquiries from various sources on financial aid policies and procedures. Assists in making application for federal funds for government loan programs; administers rules and regulations set forth by the federal government concerning government funds. Coordinates and administers assigned financial aid programs such as the federal work study program and federal and institutional loan programs; maintains contact with university payroll clerks, undergraduate, graduate, and professional school student aid coordinators and other University and external individuals to carry out program activities; develops and implements new initiatives within assigned program areas. Prepares detailed reports and compiles information concerning undergraduate financial aid and assigned programs as requested by the federal government and University officials. Edits publication brochures, questionnaires, applications, and other material distributed by the Financial Aid office. Physical Effort Most work is sedentary, completed within an office setting. Some counseling/presenting is performed at other campuses and off-campus sites. Employee must be able to move about the campus to meetings and travel to locations outside of the University of Pittsburgh. Employee may be required to carry a box of material up to 50 lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Financial Aid Counselor Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Financial Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., some mornings, evenings and weekends may be required Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004806": {
      "title": "Doctoral Program Administrator",
      "description": "Job Description - Doctoral Program Administrator (26004806) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Doctoral Program Administrator (26004806) Job Description Doctoral Program Administrator Nurs-Student Affairs and Alumni Relations - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004806 ) Job Summary Oversees administrative operations, facilitates and schedules projects, serves as liaison between internal and external stakeholders, recommends organizational changes to increase effectiveness, and resolves issues. Assists with strategic plans and budgetary functions. Essential Functions •    Oversees administrative operations, including major calendars, purchasing supplies, and handling routine correspondence. •    Plans, coordinates, and schedules projects; serves as liaison between internal and external stakeholders; resolves issues and provides feedback, guidance, and support. •    Assists in the implementation and evaluation of strategic plans; measures and reports on results and actions. •    Assesses and recommends organizational changes to increase effectiveness. •    Assists with developing and monitoring the budget by reviewing reports and projections, providing guidance on permissible expenditures, and ensuring compliance with policies and procedures. •    Prepares routine budget analyses, reports, and projections. •    Maintains physical and digital documentation. •    Communicates effectively with students and program leadership, providing updates, documentation, and support as needed. •    Contributes to continuous improvement efforts related to facilitating, tracking, and reporting doctoral student milestones. •    Manages scheduling logistics for doctoral project presentations and dissertation defenses. •    Other duties as assigned by supervisors. The job duties outlined in this job description include common job responsibilities for this title and level of jobs and are not intended to cover every duty. The University reserves the right to assign other duties to employees that are not listed in this job description. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for long periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Office Supervisor Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification N/A Work Schedule Monday-Friday 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $20.50--$25.62 hourly Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004942": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Project Coordinator (26004942) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Coordinator (26004942) Job Description Project Coordinator Med-Emergency Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004942 ) The position is for a part-time Project Coordinator (18.75 hours/week) with benefits for the Department of Emergency Medicine funded by a foundation grant. The incumbent will support operations of the Center for Cardiac Arrest Survival. Key job functions include: Completion of forms and data entry for registration of project participants Contacting and coordinating activities with project stakeholders Providing event scheduling support Production of flyers/handouts/posters and other project documentation (including social media) Updating the project website Production of simple reports summarizing key project performance indicators Data entry for an AED registry and Supporting orders/acquisitions. This is a hybrid position with a minimum requirement of 4 hours per week in person at the Oakland campus of the University of Pittsburgh and attendance (hybrid) at the weekly CCAS meeting (Wednesdays 12p-1p) and Pulse Point report review and coalition. Job Summary Serves in an administrative capacity and provides administrative support to the project manager and other team members. Assists with fiscal management and compliance with federal regulations and the contracts. Manages day-to-day office operations and interacts with key stakeholders. Essential Functions The incumbent should have excellent organizational and communication skills, be self-motivated and capable of working independently, have strong time management practices, have strong interpersonal skills, and work well when given a task list. Fluency with the Microsoft Office Suite is required. Physical Effort Must be able to sit and stand for prolonged periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Part-time regular Job Classification Staff.Project Coordinator Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Program & Project Management Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule flexible Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $20.00 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004833": {
      "title": "Pre-Award Administrator",
      "description": "Job Description - Pre-Award Administrator (26004833) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Pre-Award Administrator (26004833) Job Description Pre-Award Administrator Med-Pediatrics Research Administration - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004833 ) Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position will be 100% remote.  PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment.  EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Prepares and submits moderately complex grant, contract, and budget proposals. Drafts and negotiates contractual arrangements, procurement proposals, subcontracts, and budgets. Conducts complex cost analyses and oversees invoice processing; analyzes financial documentation and reviews routine reports. Monitors grants, budgets, and contractual arrangements and prepares moderately complex pre-award applications and reports. Provides policy and procedural interpretation and resolves complex issues. Essential Functions • Develops, prepares, and submits moderately complex grant, contract, and budget proposals; drafts and negotiates contractual arrangements, procurement proposals, subcontracts, and budgets; ensures the complete and accurate collection and submission of all pre-award phase materials. • Oversees the processing of invoices; conducts complex cost analyses of proposals and analyzes price proposals. • Monitors grants, budgets, and contractual arrangements to ensure accuracy and compliance with budgets, sponsor terms, federal regulations, policies, and procedures; provides policy and procedure interpretation. • Processes amendments, modifications, extensions, and terminations of contracts; arbitrates claims and complaints; resolves complex issues. • Prepares moderately complex pre-award applications and reports to grant agencies; analyzes financial documentation and reviews routine reports. • Develops and implements accounting techniques, policies, and procedures to improve operations and organization. • Tracks multiple grants and contracts to advise University employees on long-term financial viability; educates employees on grant and contract procedures. • Ensures compliance with sponsor terms, University policies and procedures, and federal Physical Effort None. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Pre-Award) Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Grants & Contracts Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Shift determined by manager. Work Arrangement Remote: Teams working from different locations (off-campus). Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
