    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004892": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator III",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator III (26004892) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator III (26004892) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator III Med-Neurology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004892 ) The University of Pittsburgh Department of Neurology seeks to hire a Clinical Research Coordinator. The coordinator will conduct all aspects of clinical research trials from site initiation through activation and completion under the direction of the Principal Investigator. Responsibilities include study start-up and documentation; budget development and fiscal tracking; IRB submissions and consent forms; protocol implementation across UPMC departments; participant recruitment, screening, enrollment, and follow-up; conducting study visits and neuropsychological assessments; obtaining medical histories, blood pressure screenings, and blood collection via phlebotomy as applicable; processing and shipping biological specimens; dispensing medications under physician or nurse practitioner orders; managing research supplies and equipment; and ensuring timely, accurate documentation and data entry. The coordinator will collaborate with investigators, research staff, IRB personnel, UPMC departments, sponsors, and monitors. Additional duties may include assisting with IRB protocols, the Research Registry, brain bank pager coverage, and community outreach activities. This position has a significant impact on program operations and may affect the health and well-being of research participants. The successful candidate must understand applicable policies and procedures, exercise independent judgment, and resolve unique problems through the collection and interpretation of information. A Master's degree is preferred. Job Summary Prepares grant applications, manuscripts, Institutional Review Board (IRB) applications, research papers, and assists with complex research papers. Audits research studies, monitors study budgets, resolves complex data collection issues, and implements protocol-specific study recruitment plans. Trains staff and oversees student workers; leads team meetings. Monitors study budgets and orders supplies. Essential Functions Oversees and prepares IRB applications. Reviews/audits research studies; assists with next step determination. Monitors study budgets and expenditures. Maintains and orders supplies as needed. Assesses protocol feasibility; establishes protocol-specific recruitment plans. Trains staff and oversees the work of student workers as directed. Communicates effectively with study participants and potential community recruits. Identifies community education opportunities. Facilitates research/project team meetings. Resolves complex data collection issues. Physical Effort Must be able to get around a university setting. Can be sedentary for long period of times. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F, 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004842": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician III- Dr. Omar El Gharbawie's Lab",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician III- Dr. Omar El Gharbawie's Lab (26004842) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician III- Dr. Omar El Gharbawie's Lab (26004842) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician III- Dr. Omar El Gharbawie's Lab Med-Neurobiology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004842 ) Job Summary Performs a variety of independent laboratory work and experiments such as determining experimental protocols and preparation of specimens and cultures. Prepares reports of findings subsequent to compilation and analyzation. Oversees specimen inventory. Develops documentation for publication; crafts manuscripts and grant proposals. Essential Functions We are seeking an energetic, hardworking, individual, to fill a Research Technician position in the laboratory of Omar Gharbawie (Department of Neurobiology at University of Pittsburgh). The lab conducts research on non-human primates to understand how the brain controls movement. The successful candidate will have broad responsibilities including: · Behavioral training and testing in monkeys. Maintain animal well-being. Work closely with attending veterinarian to formulate and execute treatment plans. Assist with experiments in awake and anesthetized animals. Prepare and assist with sterile surgery. Intubate, place IV catheters, and maintain subjects under anesthesia. Maintain animal records. Order supplies and manage lab inventory. Manage IACUC protocol and take steps to ensure that lab remains in compliance. Train new lab members on best practices. Assist with lab maintenance and cleaning. Physical Effort Experience in handling non-human primates are necessary. Must be able to lift 50 lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. The successful applicant is expected to work one late evening every month. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004862": {
      "title": "Part Time Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center)",
      "description": "Job Description - Part Time Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center) (26004862) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part Time Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center) (26004862) Job Description Part Time Assistant Teacher (University Child Development Center) University Child Development Center - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004862 ) The Assistant Teacher will work in an early childhood classroom at the University Child Development Center with children ranging in age from six weeks through five years of age. The position involves a collaborative effort in supporting the functions of the classroom under the supervision of a Head Teacher and an Associate Teacher. The Assistant Teacher is responsible for supporting daily activities and programming in the classroom, interaction with and supervising a group of children and maintaining daily communication with families. Some supervision of University students is required. Assistant Teachers are required to maintain 12 hours of professional development annually during their employment and maintain all DHS, NAEYC, Keystone STARS requirements. They are also required to attend all five professional development days at UCDC annually. Candidates must meet one of the following: High school diploma or GED and 30 credit hours from an accredited college or university in early childhood education, child development, special education, elementary education, or the human services field , High school diploma or GED, including 600 or more hours of secondary training as described in §3270.31(c) High school diploma or GED, 15 credit hours from an accredited college or university in one of the above fields, and 1 year of experience with children High school diploma or GED and completion of a post-secondary training curriculum described in §3270.31(c) High school diploma or GED and 2 years of experience with children Job Summary Supports head and associate teachers in a child development center. Prepares fine and gross motor activities for effective child development. Maintains a safe classroom conducive to learning and engagement. Guides student and temporary workers. Essential Functions The Assistant Teacher supports the Head Teacher in the planning and implementation of a child development program for a class of children. Incumbent may act as supervisor when the Head Teacher and Associate Teacher are not in the classroom. Physical Effort The work involves occasional, and at times sustained performance of heavier physical tasks such as traversing over rough or uneven surfaces, bending, stooping, traversing space quickly, and lifting and/or carrying 40-pound children. Work exposes the employee to potentially non disabling injuries or illnesses. Duties require regular exposure to the outside. Bloodborne and airborne pathogens present a potential hazard. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Part-time regular Job Classification Staff.Assistant Teacher Job Family Child Development Job Sub-Family University Child Development Center Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Candidate must have a high school diploma/GED and two years of verified experience with young children OR a high school diploma/GED, 15 credits in a human service field and one year of verified experience with young children. Work Schedule M-F, 12:30-5:30 pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003529": {
      "title": "Custodial Manager",
      "description": "Job Description - Custodial Manager (26003529) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Custodial Manager (26003529) Job Description Custodial Manager Facilities Management AVC - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003529 ) Responsible for supervising and managing comprehensive custodial operations for residential and administrative buildings at the University of Pittsburgh. Responsible and accountable for the day-to-day operational and administrative activities of custodial services under scope of responsibility. Provides guidance and training to, and evaluates the work performance of, supervisors and custodians in support of service delivery to the campus. Takes an active part in the service implementation of student arrivals/departures, conferences, and events when deemed appropriate. Collaborates and coordinates essential support for special events, other functions, and emergencies, and provides ground coordination for emergency and weather-related incidents. Accountable for evaluating the technical expertise of supervisors, and for training, coaching, and mentoring them. Ensures productivity of custodians, with broad discretion in evaluating work areas for effectiveness and efficiency. Engages in frequent communication, coaching, counseling, redirection, and correction to ensure expected performance levels. Establishes, monitors, and maintains viable inspection, corrective action, and follow-up programs. Proactively works with Employee and Labor Relations, including progressive discipline as needed and directed by the CBA. Refers further disciplinary action to the Senior Manager of Custodial Services. Works with Employee and Labor Relations to uphold procedure and FM policies and collaborates on the grievance process. Performs and oversees administrative tasks such as labor entry, timekeeping, work schedules, etc. Prepares and proofreads correspondence. Ensures accuracy of all materials and documents and completes administrative duties in a timely manner to ensure service and compliance (timecards, performance reviews, etc.). Documents, reviews, assigns, and manages work within the TMA system in accordance with department policy. Regularly inspects all assigned facilities and completes reports in support of quality custodial services. Provides ongoing training and development for supervisors and custodial staff. Assists supervisors in scheduling training for new staff. Works closely with facility managers regarding maintenance issues and reports on repairs, with emphasis on lighting, dispensers, and other related items associated with custodial services. Proactively interacts with University of Pittsburgh staff at all levels who work in buildings to solicit feedback regarding the quality of custodial services, including other members of the Facilities Management team. Job Summary Manages the day-to-day operations and administrative activities of the custodial program. Monitors all custodial service and vendor contracts and verifies invoices. Evaluates, purchases, and repairs equipment to ensure safety. Essential Functions Supervise, train, evaluate, and develop assistant managers who oversee supervisors who oversee 20+ union custodians; coach and conduct annual performance reviews. Administer progressive discipline under the collective bargaining agreement, manage the grievance procedure, and enforce FM policies. Run inspection/corrective-action programs, perform regular facility inspections and QA reporting, and manage work orders in the TMA and Smart Inspection system. Handle labor entry, timekeeping, scheduling, supply ordering, and recordkeeping; monitor vendor contracts and verify invoices. Ensure compliance with cleaning procedures, PPE, SDS, chemical safety, and equipment-use standards. Coordinate and support work during weekends, holidays, weather events, emergencies, or special events as needed. Maintains a professional, responsive, and service-oriented approach with staff, supervisors, managers, building occupants, vendors, and University partners. Physical Effort Walking 50-60% of the day.  Lifting: 10% of the day not to exceed 50lbs.  Sitting 20-30% of the day.  Climbing and squatting 5% of the day. Must have use of all limbs and must have Driver's License. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Manager - Custodial Services Job Family Campus Operations Job Sub-Family Facilities Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday through Friday 8am to 4:30pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004817": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26004817) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Coordinator (26004817) Job Description Clinical Research Coordinator Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004817 ) Equivalent relevant work experience may be substituted for degree requirement. This position is located at UPMC Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh in Lawrenceville. PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and FBI Criminal Record Check will be required prior to the start of employment. Also, a current TB test will be required as a condition of employment. EEO/AA/M/F/Vets/Disabled. Job Summary Assists with and adheres to Institutional Review Board (IRB) renewal, modification, and approved protocols. Recruits research subjects and conducts interviews and research assessments. Essential Functions • Assists with and adheres to IRB renewal, modification, and approved protocols. • Recruits research subjects. Conducts research interviews in-person or via telephone while adhering to all applicable protocols. Completes research assessments on study participants. • Maintains databases in a timely and accurate manner, adhering to all applicable protocols and regulations. • Assists with training new personnel as directed. • Assists with study assessments administration as directed. Physical Effort Light. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Shift determined by manager. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004835": {
      "title": "Laboratory Manager I",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Manager I (26004835) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Manager I (26004835) Job Description Laboratory Manager I Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004835 ) Job Summary Manages day-to-day laboratory operations while ensuring compliance with safety regulations and best practices. Works with, adapts, and installs scientific equipment in research laboratories. Collaborates on routine projects and procedures. Manages inventory and equipment and performs budget functions. Essential Functions Perform a variety of laboratory experiments such as imaging, histology, molecular and cellular techniques, small animal surgical procedures, and cell culture-related techniques Perform related technical functions, testing, troubleshooting, analysis, and ensure conformity to protocol specifications Oversee management of laboratory supplies including ordering, procurement, tracking estimates, and receiving items Operate, maintain, calibrate, clean and test sterility of applicable laboratory equipment related to job functions Keep detailed, accurate, and timely data and log books to organize and document results Contribute to laboratory publications, research presentations, and funding applications Physical Effort Incumbent must be able to stand to perform duties.  Some walking is necessary between laboratories of collaborators. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Manager I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004838": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Manager",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Research Manager (26004838) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Research Manager (26004838) Job Description Clinical Research Manager Psychology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004838 ) The Center for Parents and Children (CPC) within the Department of Psychology at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking a Clinical Manager. The CPC aims to bridge the gap between science and practice in the service of promoting positive outcomes for children and families, with a special emphasis on early childhood. The center provides family-based interventions to parents of young children from predominantly low-income backgrounds in the Pittsburgh community. Reporting to the Administrative Officer, the Clinical Manager will oversee daily operational functions across the center and work in collaboration with the Principal Investigator. The manager provides supervisory responsibility for a team of staff, including hiring, work assignment and review, performance management, and HR administration. A valid driver's license is required with access to personal vehicle. Child protection clearances are required prior to the start of employment; offers of employment and start dates are contingent upon their receipt. HIPAA training will be provided upon hire. Bachelor’s degree in counseling, social work, clinical psychology, or marriage and family counseling plus 3 years of experience working in a clinical setting. Minimum of 1 year supervising clinicians. Masters degree in Applied Developmental Psychology or Clinical Psychology preferred. Clinical experience in delivering interventions to families preferred. Job Summary Manages day-to-day responsibilities for staff in research study administration, recruitment, and logistics. Develops and implements operational plans and systems for recruitment, data collection, and meeting project goals and deliverables. Ensures study protocols are met and adhered to and facilitates an organizational system for accumulated study data forms and procedures. Essential Functions Strong clinical skills, strong written and verbal communication skills, leadership skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work with a range of families and clinical issues. Must work collaboratively with other staff, as well as community and organizational partners, and treat others with courtesy and respect. Individual in this position must be able to use Microsoft Suite (Word, Outlook, TEAMS, OneDrive, Excel), a telephone, must be able to make visits to families, and must be able to communicate verbally. Individual must have a valid driver's license and reliable access to a personal vehicle for the purpose of conducting visits. Physical Effort Individual must be able to drive a car, travel on and off campus, and be able to lift up to 30 lbs for occasional basic needs good drop-offs.  Assistance (both from other staff or in terms of equipment such as a cart) for the lifting of basic needs goods can be provided. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Manager - Clinical Research Coordinator Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday to Friday 8:30am - 5:00pm with occasional weekends and evenings Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $73,000 to $80,000 annually Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002664": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Dental Assistant (26002664) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Dental Assistant (26002664) Job Description Dental Assistant Dent Med-Endodontics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26002664 ) Job Summary Performs chairside dental assisting and radiography. Guides patients through visits and treatments, ensures charts are complete and necessary information is collected, and coordinates patient flow. Ensures infection control in operatories and with instruments. Maintains supplies. Essential Functions Job Responsibilities: Performs chairside dental assisting and radiography. Guides patients through visits and treatments, ensures charts are complete and necessary information is collected, and coordinates patient flow. Ensures infection control in operatories and with instruments. Maintains supplies. Clinical and Patient Support Provide chairside dental assistance to predoctoral and graduate dental residents, utilizing four-handed dentistry techniques. Perform radiography as needed during chairside assisting. Welcome and guide patients, providing information on the patient’s experience. Complete, scan, and enter medical histories, screening forms, and related dental, medical, and/or insurance paperwork into the database, ensuring patient charts are complete and organized. Organize and coordinate the flow of patients to maximize departmental efficiency. Assist the supervisor in effectively matching incoming patients’ dental needs with students' educational requirements for treatment planning. Infection Control and Sterilization: Ensure strict infection control compliance, including monitoring student adherence to procedures. Prepare and turn over patient operatories in accordance with sterilization guidelines. Implement proper sterilization techniques for all instruments, including those supplied through IMS (monitoring instrumentation during and after patient use) and those requiring manual sterilization (wash, brush, pack, and listing instruments in kits). Maintain clinical and related areas in a healthy environment. Perform ongoing maintenance of clinic equipment (e.g., changing water filters, changing solution and cleaning automatic and hand developers) Supply, Inventory, and Laboratory Management: Manage and maintain appropriate inventory of supplies. Dispense supplies, equipment, and instruments to students. Stock cabinets with necessary supplies. Coordinate and maintain all dental laboratory functions within the department. General Department Support: Perform other duties assigned related to the operations of the department. Always maintaining the clinic in operational readiness. This entails ordering and maintaining supplies and equipment, preparing rooms for procedures, and assisting students and patients as required. Required Licenses/Certifications: Radiograph certificate strongly encouraged not required. Physical Effort Incumbent must sit, stand, walk, bend, throughout the day. Stocking supplies and removal of biohazardous waste materials entails including carrying boxes or bags which can be heavy. Assisting/students and patients may require extensive walking or standing. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Dental Assistant Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Clinical Dental Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Radiograph certificate strongly encouraged not required Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003444": {
      "title": "Operating Engineer",
      "description": "Job Description - Operating Engineer (26003444) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Operating Engineer (26003444) Job Description Operating Engineer Work-in Process Labor - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003444 ) Job Summary The Operating Engineer is responsible for properly operating all mechanical systems; for performing selected preventive and corrective maintenance duties as directed; for monitoring and operating building automation system hardware, software, sensors, and components. The incumbent will be responsible for the operation, preventive and corrective maintenance for all mechanical, electrical, and plumbing systems. This position requires a minimum class 4 City of Pittsburgh Power Engineers License or equivalent NIULPE, Universal CFC Certification, preferred five years’ experience as a licensed stationary or operating engineer: a minimum of three years’ experience monitoring and operating building automation systems controlling a large and complex physical plant. Computer-based energy management systems and DDC control experience preferred. Incumbent must be mobile around campus, be able to lift 50 pounds, crawl into confined spaces including manholes and utility tunnels as well as maneuver around small areas and be able to lift equipment and supplies. Essential Functions Incumbent must be able to be mobile around campus, be able to lift 50 lbs., crawl, and have above average sensory perception; must possess valid Pennsylvania driver’s license. Physical Effort Incumbent will be required to climb ladders, crawl into confined spaces including manholes, and utility tunnels. Also, must be able to maneuver around small areas and be able to lift equipment and supplies. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Union Eligible.95 Pittsburgh.Operating Engineer Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification Class 4 City of Pittsburgh Power Engineer License or Equivalent NIULPE, Universal CFC Work Schedule Sunday & Monday 10pm - 6am; Thursday, Friday, Saturday 6am - 2pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Per Collective Bargaining Agreement Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004543": {
      "title": "Biobank Supervisor",
      "description": "Job Description - Biobank Supervisor (26004543) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Biobank Supervisor (26004543) Job Description Biobank Supervisor Med-Neurology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004543 ) The University of Pittsburgh, Department of Neurology, would like to hire a qualified Biobank Supervisor (Clinical Research Coordinator). Directs the day-to-day operations of the biobank, ensuring adherence to best practices in biospecimen collection, processing, storage, and utilization of inventory management systems. Oversees patient consent processes and documentation, ensuring compliance with IRB protocols, regulatory requirements, and grant-specific guidelines; trains, supervises, and coordinates staff involved in biospecimen collection and handling. Manages data and sample workflows, including organization, protocol development, quality control, and preliminary analysis of biospecimen data and sample integrity. Supervises project budget and supports grant related submissions, while ensuring full compliance with institutional, federal, and sponsor-related requirements. Masters Preferred, Bachelor’s Degree acceptable with 2 years clinical research or laboratory experience. Job Summary Prepares grant applications, manuscripts, Institutional Review Board (IRB) applications, research papers, and assists with complex research papers. Audits research studies, monitors study budgets, resolves complex data collection issues, and implements protocol-specific study recruitment plans. Trains staff and oversees student workers; leads team meetings. Monitors study budgets and orders supplies. Essential Functions Prepares grant applications, performs literature reviews, and prepares manuscripts for publication; writes research papers and assists with writing complex papers. • Oversees and prepares IRB applications. • Reviews/audits research studies; assists with next step determination. • Monitors study budgets and expenditures. Maintains and orders supplies as needed. • Assesses protocol feasibility; establishes protocol-specific recruitment plans.• Trains staff and oversees the work of student workers as directed.• Communicates effectively with study participants and potential community recruits. Identifies community education opportunities. • Facilitates research/project team meetings. • Resolves complex data collection issues. Directs the day-to-day operations of the biobank, ensuring adherence to best practices in biospecimen collection, processing, storage, and utilization of inventory management systems. Oversees patient consent processes and documentation, ensuring compliance with IRB protocols, regulatory requirements, and grant-specific guidelines; trains, supervises, and coordinates staff involved in biospecimen collection and handling.Manages data and sample workflows, including organization, protocol development, quality control, obtain and process lab samples, and preliminary analysis of biospecimen data and sample integrity. Supervises project budget and supports grant related submissions, while ensuring full compliance with institutional, federal, and sponsor-related requirements. Physical Effort Moderate physical effort required. May be required to get around a university setting for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Clinical Research Coordinator III Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Clinical Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule M-F, 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004525": {
      "title": "Biostatistician",
      "description": "Job Description - Biostatistician (26004525) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Biostatistician (26004525) Job Description Biostatistician Med-Urology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004525 ) The Biostatistician will work within the Department of Urology on a variety of projects that examine the delivery, access, and quality of urologic care. This position involves responsibilities for a wide range of data management, programming, and analytic needs related to research based on large observational datasets (e.g., SEER-Medicare, Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, Pennsylvania Health Care Cost Containment Council, Optum datasets) as well as institutional clinical datasets. Responsibilities include directing Urology Fellows and Residents in research trial design, including performing power analyses and/or simulations, and writing statistical sections of research proposals. Incumbent will also be responsible for assisting with medical manuscript preparation, including writing and editing statistical methods and results. Job Summary Applies scientific methodology to conceptualize, propose, and implement appropriate methodologies for statistical analyses. Maintains and updates centralized research awards database. Assists with grant preparations and clinical trial budgets. Develops and validates reporting data, validates data subsets of funding data, and facilitates quality control procedures to ensure data accuracy. Essential Functions The Biostatistician will work within the Department of Urology on a variety of projects that examine the delivery, access, and quality of urologic care. This position involves responsibilities for a wide range of data management, programming, and analytic needs related to research based on large observational datasets (e.g., SEER-Medicare, Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, Pennsylvania Health Care Cost Containment Council, Optum datasets) as well as institutional clinical datasets. Responsibilities include directing Urology Fellows and Residents in research trial design, including performing power analyses and/or simulations, and writing statistical sections of research proposals. Incumbent will also be responsible for assisting with medical manuscript preparation, including writing and editing statistical methods and results. Physical Effort Duties are primarly sedentary. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Medical Data Scientist I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Data Science Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 am - 4:30 pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $44,000 - $59,000 Annual Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002784": {
      "title": "Maintenance Services II",
      "description": "Job Description - Maintenance Services II (26002784) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Maintenance Services II (26002784) Job Description Maintenance Services II Greensburg Facilities Management - Pennsylvania-Greensburg - ( 26002784 ) The University of Pittsburgh at Greensburg Facilities Management & Operations department is responsible for maintaining, preserving and enhancing the University's physical assets. We are committed to operation excellence. Our core services include custodial, building, and ground maintenance, in addition to construction and renovation projects done in partnership with the University of Pittsburgh Oakland Office of Facilities Management. Our goal is to ensure a safe, operational and appealing campus environment. Job Summary Responsible for the general and craft maintenance of the residence halls, operation of University equipment, preventive and scheduled maintenance to support special events, projects, conferences, planned utility outages and activities sponsored by individuals/groups using the campus facilities. Essential Functions The Maintenance Worker II will perform general groundskeeping and craft maintenance on campus grounds and related equipment as follows: - Perform preventive maintenance and repair of equipment; - Operate tractors, mowers, trucks, dump truck with spreader, and backhoes; - Assist in performing electrical, HVAC, carpentry and plumbing repairs, installations and overhauls; - Cut grass, plant shrubbery, weed gardens, mulch, remove snow and spread salt; - Assist in painting outside surfaces, laying concrete, constructing fences and other fixtures, clean basins and yard drains; - Drive campus vehicle to pick up and/or deliver supplies, materials or passengers on campus; - Aid in loading and unloading vehicles and moving heavy boxes and supplies; - Follow prescribed safety regulations and inform management of potential risks or hazards; - Complete work requests and notify management of repair work and required materials; - Support special events, projects, conferences, planned utility outages and activities sponsored by individuals or groups using campus facilities; - Perform other related duties as required or assigned. Work will be completed individually or as part of a team. Physical Effort The Maintenance Worker II must have the ability to travel independently throughout campus and be capable of lifting up to 50 pounds including equipment and supplies. Will operate equipment such as mowers, tractors, trucks and backhoes. Will crawl into and work in confined spaces climb ladders. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Union Eligible.95 Regionals.Maintenance II Campus Greensburg Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Tuesday - Friday 2:00 p.m. - 10:30 p.m.; Saturday 7:00 a.m. - 3:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Per Collective Bargaining Agreement Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004610": {
      "title": "Digital Imaging Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Digital Imaging Specialist (26004610) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Digital Imaging Specialist (26004610) Job Description Digital Imaging Specialist Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004610 ) Job Summary Provide advanced microscopy and specialized histology imaging support, baseline informatics/ Laboratory Information Management System (LIMS) accession duties to support lab operations. The position performs whole slide imaging (WSI) activities, including general and specialized microscopy, scanner operation, post-scanning quality checking, data entry, storage and archival. Responsibilities will also include interaction with scanning vendors and troubleshooting software operation/ hardware issues, as necessary. Essential Functions • Image acquisition: Operate manual and motorized/ automated digital light and fluorescence microscopy systems. Understand and apply/ modify automation routines for focus acquisition, background and signal-to-noise optimization. • Provide microtomy feedback and overall specimen quality reports to histology operations. • Perform quality assurance evaluations on scanned images, ensure diagnostic and analysis quality and data de-identification when appropriate • Upload/archival of the slide images into various LIMS repository as required in the lab workflow protocol and/or project • Collect and organize experimental data associated with scanning projects (Basic grouping, Assist with research activities – manuscript generation, data input, algorithms • Prepare and analyze data metrics related to imaging system reliability, overall data storage usage, and predictive/ anticipation of data archival tasks • Perform routine maintenance, alignments, and calibrations on hardware to ensure system functionality and regulatory compliance • Serve as primary resource for equipment knowledge, troubleshooting and data information regarding the imaging system and pathology workflow software. • Attention to detail, accurate, precise, and dependable performance of techniques and organization is critical to interpretation and experimental conclusions. Physical Effort This position is primarily sedentary.   However, there will be some walking between laboratories. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Digital Imaging Specialist Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Imaging Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:30-5:00 Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004463": {
      "title": "Evaluation Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Evaluation Coordinator (26004463) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Evaluation Coordinator (26004463) Job Description Evaluation Coordinator Educ-Office of Child Development - Pennsylvania-Hershey - ( 26004463 ) The Office of Child Development (OCD) is seeking an experienced, creative, and versatile professional capable of handling a variety of administrative and research tasks for the Evaluation and Research Team (ERT). This employee will provide targeted administrative support and research assistance for a comprehensive evaluation of an innovative Early Childhood Education program in Central Pennsylvania. Responsibilities include: collecting quantitative and qualitative assessment data from young children and adults, entering and analyzing data in a variety of software programs; managing scheduling, communications, and logistics for project activities; creating data visualizations, preparing presentations, and writing executive summaries; and providing project-wide administrative support. The incumbent will maintain positive, professional relationships with a variety of stakeholders from school staff to parents. They must understand detailed research plans and protocols, and have skill, competence, and comfort working with young children in early childhood education settings with the ability to collect data from children as well as their educators and families. The incumbent must be detail oriented in data documentation and storage. Additional responsibilities include collaborating with supervisor and practitioners to organize and support writing of various reports, prepare and administer surveys, maintain databases, and coordinate meetings/events. Experience in interviewing and conducting focus groups preferred. Incumbent must be able to obtain a TB test clearance. This position will be located at the Catherine Hershey Schools - Elizabethtown Center in Elizabethtown, PA. Experience related to early childhood education settings required. Experience with Excel, SPSS, quantitative and qualitative data collection (interviews; focus groups) and analysis, survey design and analysis, and use of Qualtrics preferred. Job Summary Initiates, develops, and manages applied research and program evaluation projects and identifies gaps and opportunities in child welfare processes, products, and practices. Develops research questions, data collection strategies, and testing plans. Provides support to internal and external stakeholders. Collects and analyzes data, crafts reports, and contributes to the child welfare field through publications and conference presentations. Pursues funding opportunities. Essential Functions -Initiates, develops, and manages applied research and program evaluation projects. -Develops research questions and data collection strategies. Devises testing plans and monitors project goals and time lines. -Provides research, evaluation, and data-related support to internal and external stakeholders. -Maintains communication with project leaders, supervisors, and stakeholders for the project's duration. -Collects data through appropriate methods, including surveys, interviews, and focus groups. Analyzes data and records relevant findings. -Crafts reports and presentations to communicate project insights and any accompanying recommendations for improvement. -Contributes to the field of early childhood education through journal publications and presentations at professional conferences. Physical Effort This position is mostly sedentary, but the individual must attend a variety of meetings in different places and use the computer for extended periods of time. This individual must operate appropriate computers and software; be able to communicate with diverse audiences; and work with various professionals. Ability to drive or use public transportation. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research & Evaluation Specialist II Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Child Development Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Mon - Fri 8:00 - 4:00pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $45,000 - $55,000 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004526": {
      "title": "Animal Behavior Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Animal Behavior Technician (26004526) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Animal Behavior Technician (26004526) Job Description Animal Behavior Technician DLAR-Veterinary Services - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004526 ) The individual will serve as an Animal Behavior Technician within the Division of Laboratory and Animal Resources (DLAR). The individual will assume a lead veterinary support role by assisting DLAR veterinarians, managers, and supervisors with enhancing the animal environment for all species and providing for the psychological well-being of nonhuman primates (NHPs) and regulated birds as required by applicable regulations, industry guidelines, and institutional and DLAR policies and practices. The position requires successful enrollment in the University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program and other medical surveillance/immunization programs as dictated by the current research activities. Vaccination and/or TB testing may be required. The successful candidate must be able to comprehend and follow written and verbal instructions, maintain accurate and legible records and other forms of documentation, consistently demonstrate positive interpersonal and customer service skills, be available to work weekends and holidays, travel to multiple buildings in a timely manner, stand for extended periods of time, lift 50 pounds, push/pull heavy equipment, pass the mandatory criminal and social background check, and possibly the PA Child Abuse History Clearance and/or Federal Select Agent Clearance. Job Summary Performs behavioral assessments on new and existing acquisitions of nonhuman primates. Supports the research program by promoting the environmental enhancement and psychological well-being of nonhuman primates and other laboratory animal species, in accordance with regulatory requirements. Essential Functions The employee must be able to: Read, understand, and follow DLAR and other institutional guidance documents (SOPs, policies), including IACUC approved animal protocols when applicable; Follow written and verbal instructions; Have sufficient visual acuity and manual dexterity to recognize and identify normal and abnormal species specific clinical appearances and behavior patterns, safely handle and restrain the animal species involved with his/her duties, and operate and maintain facility equipment and supplies utilized in the provision of veterinary care and animal husbandry and care; Wear facility specific Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) required by the job duties based on risk assessment from EH&S; Work directly with live or dead animals and clean or soiled bedding and caging with reasonable accommodations if necessary; Accurately and legibly document written information in English in a timely manner, including electronic formats and applications (e.g., PRISM, CAMS); Effective written and verbal communication in English, including the use of email; Receive vaccinations and health assessments, including TB testing, required to work in some animal holding or procedure areas in accordance with DLAR and/or EH&S policies and practices. Physical Effort The employee must be able to: Stand for extended periods of time throughout the majority of the work day; Lift and move objects weighing up to 50 pounds including but not limited to caging and equipment, bags or boxes of animal diet and animal bedding, and operate flatbed hand trucks or pallet jacks to move heavier objects or weights exceeding 50 pounds; Perform repetitive motion tasks that involve pushing, pulling, reaching, and/or bending; Physically handle and restrain a variety of small and large laboratory animals; Negotiate and navigate around animal facility caging, equipment, and the physical plant. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Animal Behavior Technician Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Animal Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Required Licensure/Certification LAT Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Internal candidates:   \nCertification by AALAS at the Assistant Laboratory Animal Technician (ALAT) level \n\nExternal candidates:  \nCertification by AALAS at the Assistant Laboratory Animal Technician (ALAT) level within 12 months of start date Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 7am - 4pm. Some weekends and holidays. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004504": {
      "title": "Scientific Writer",
      "description": "Job Description - Scientific Writer (26004504) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Scientific Writer (26004504) Job Description Scientific Writer Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004504 ) The Scientific Writer II supports faculty researchers and multi-disciplinary teams at the Vascular Medicine Institute (VMI) in securing and sustaining grant funding by producing clear, compelling, and compliant scientific documents. The primary responsibilities of this position are grant writing and preparing detailed scientific progress reports and slide decks for funded grants. The writer works closely with principal investigators (PIs) and project managers/administrators and may assist with coordinating document preparation and timelines across multiple PIs to ensure complete, polished submissions. Additional responsibilities may include writing newsletter articles, responding to funder requests for information, and preparing other scientific communications as needed. Position Duties: Grant proposal writing. Draft, revise, and/or refine narrative components of large, multi-investigator grant proposals – including specific aims, research strategy sections, and other supporting administrative materials – working collaboratively with PIs, project managers, and grants administrators to ensure scientific accuracy, clarity, and compliance with funder guidelines. Scientific progress reporting. Write and edit detailed scientific progress reports for funded grants, accurately synthesizing research findings, milestones, and next steps as provided by faculty investigators and translating technical content for funders and other audiences. Scientific presentation development. Prepare scientific slide decks for faculty to present grant progress and research outcomes, organizing complex data and narratives into polished, visually clear, and logically structured presentations. Position-specific duties continued Document coordination across investigators. Support the project management team in collecting, organizing, and integrating written contributions from multiple PIs; track document status and deadlines to keep submissions on schedule. Ad hoc scientific communications. Write short articles and summaries for newsletters, websites, and social media posts; respond to funder requests for information; and prepare other scientific communications as assigned by faculty, project managers, or leadership. Multimedia and digital content development. Collaborate with faculty and staff to translate scientific work into multimedia formats such as infographics, short videos, visual abstracts, web features, or social media content to broaden reach and accessibility. Research dissemination support. Assist in preparing materials that support dissemination of findings to broader audiences, including lay summaries, public-facing content, or translational research highlights. Editorial and content strategy support . Contribute to planning and coordinating scientific content across channels, ensuring consistency in messaging, tone, and alignment with institutional priorities. Job Summary Assists, in conjunction with multi-disciplinary teams, with writing large, multi-investigator grant proposals and other manuscripts, as well as editing scientific reports, assisting with website copy, providing writing/editing support for book chapters, editing reports by internal and external stakeholders, and developing ad hoc requested materials. Implements critical scientific research editing to documents and maintains compliance with all guidelines and regulations. Essential Functions •    Scientific writing and editing. Demonstrated ability to write clearly and accurately about complex scientific topics for varied audiences, including funders, lay readers, and scientific peers. •    Grant writing experience. Familiarity with federal or foundation grant proposal structure and requirements (e.g., NIH, NSF, or comparable agencies), including the ability to translate investigators' research into compelling, compliant narratives. •    Domain knowledge in cardiovascular, pulmonary, or vascular biology. Familiarity with research areas relevant to the VMI's work – including vascular biology, heart and lung disease, pulmonary hypertension, hemostasis, sickle cell disease, atherosclerosis, or related fields in basic, translational, or clinical research – sufficient to accurately represent and communicate faculty science. •    Presentation design in PowerPoint. Proficiency with Microsoft PowerPoint, including the ability to translate scientific data and narratives into well-organized, professional slide decks suitable for funder and research audiences. •    Visual communication and data presentation. Ability to present scientific data clearly through figures, diagrams, and visual storytelling approaches that enhance comprehension and impact. •    Attention to detail and compliance awareness. Ability to carefully follow funder guidelines, formatting requirements, and institutional submission standards across multiple simultaneous projects. •    Collaboration and communication. Comfortable working with faculty, project managers, and other stakeholders to gather information, incorporate feedback, and meet shared deadlines – including across multiple investigators with competing priorities. •    Organization and self-direction. Ability to independently manage multiple writing projects and document workflows with minimal supervision, exercising sound judgment about priorities and timelines. Physical Effort Mostly sedentary, but must be able to move between university labs and offices.  Could require walking and long periods of writing. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Scientific Writer II Job Family Communications & Marketing Job Sub-Family Writing Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule mon-friday standard Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter, Writing Sample Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004366": {
      "title": "Director, Creative Content (VB)",
      "description": "Job Description - Director, Creative Content (VB) (26004366) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director, Creative Content (VB) (26004366) Job Description Director, Creative Content (VB) Athletics Administration - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004366 ) The University of Pittsburgh is seeking a qualified Director of Creative Content for Volleyball. This position is responsible for assisting with the development, management, and promotion of Pitt Volleyball through social media accounts; working closely with Communications on developing and implementing the social media plan for the program; coordinating with Content Strategy; Lead photography and videography efforts for Pitt Volleyball; and developing and coordinating a plan, including presentations, for Volleyball recruiting initiatives; recruit, lead, and develop a student intern program to assist with creative content. The individual also will assist with all campus recruiting activities for Volleyball and perform other duties as assigned. Job Summary Assists with developing, implementing, and management of an overall social media plan for recruitment and promotion of Department of Athletics. Develops, collaborates on, and coordinates video productions, creative content, and social media graphics. Assists with all on-campus recruiting efforts. Essential Functions Work closely with the coaching staff as well as Communications on developing and implementing a social media plan for Volleyball including a plan to utilize various social media outlets advantageously to the recruiting efforts of the program. This includes overall program brand on social media platforms (X, Instagram, and Tiktok). Responsible for designing and developing creative content for the Pitt Volleyball program in conjunction with the external relations and coaching staff.  The content produced will also be used in advertising campaigns (commercials, website, social media, etc.). Must generate new and creative ideas while staying consistent with the Pitt Volleyball brand. Create graphics to enhance the program’s recruiting efforts and overall brand development on all platforms. Develop visual and creative materials and content for recruiting activities. Other duties as assigned. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. May need to lift equipment, mail, or supplies up to 50 pounds. Required to be mobile for long periods of time, especially on gamedays. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Athletics Creative Content Manager Job Family Athletics Job Sub-Family Athletics Administration Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite; Photography; Videography; all social media platforms; and NCAA and ACC rules and regulations. An equivalent combination of work experience and high level playing experience may be substituted at the discretion of the University. Work Schedule Varies Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered Yes Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004591": {
      "title": "Project Administrator",
      "description": "Job Description - Project Administrator (26004591) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Project Administrator (26004591) Job Description Project Administrator UPCI/NSABP - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004591 ) The NRG Oncology Statistics and Data Management Center (NRG SDMC) is a large, national, federally funded multi-center organization that conducts clinical trials research with offices in Pittsburgh, Philadelphia, Buffalo and Chicago. The NRG SDMC office at the University of Pittsburgh is responsible for collection, processing, and management of numerous cancer clinical trials. There are over 1800 clinical sites in our research network which provide over 6,000 participants annually for the NRG Oncology clinical trials. Under supervision of the Director of PI, the Administrative Assistant supports the operation of the SDMC Pittsburgh Office . Administrative duties Act as a liaison between the Office and the Hillman Cancer Center Act as liaison between the Office and sponsors, including University of Chicago, the NRG Foundation and the NSABP Foundation. Make announcements within the Data Center Prepare travel reimbursements and assist with travel arrangements. Collect needed information from staff and faculty members of the Office. Track training certificates. Format and edit budget justifications and other application forms, such as Other Support and NIH Biosketch. Financial duties Maintain grant and project documents Work with Director on grant/project-related documents Track timelines/milestones Interpret University accounting levels Purchasing responsibilities-collect quotes, agreements, and other required docs for submission through Pitt purchasing system. Job Summary Supports senior level roles in a wide variety of complex administrative and office functions as well as specialized technical support for academic or administrative departments. Essential Functions The candidate must have excellent communication and interpersonal skills and should have the ability to work across multiple tasks at one time. Physical Effort Light - Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Administrative Assistant III Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $37,182.00 - $46,478.00 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004592": {
      "title": "Assistant Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Director - Research Operations (26004592) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Director - Research Operations (26004592) Job Description Assistant Director - Research Operations UPCI/NSABP - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004592 ) Job Summary The NRG Oncology Statistics and Data Management Center (NRG SDMC) is a large, national, federally funded multi-center organization that conducts clinical trials research with offices in Pittsburgh, Philadelphia, Buffalo and Chicago. The NRG SDMC office at the University of Pittsburgh is responsible for collection, processing, and management of numerous cancer clinical trials. There are over 1800 clinical sites in our research network which provide over 6,000 participants annually for the NRG Oncology clinical trials. The Assistant Director – Research Operations directs the local quality assurance program of the SDMC, including the day-to-day audit operations. The Assistant Director supports audit program development and implementation, staff supervision and ensures compliance with Federal regulations, and the development and maintenance of written standard operating procedures. The Assistant Director supports the Center Director and is a member of the local NRG SDMC leadership team. Job Duties Directs the daily work of the Quality Assurance Specialists and Quality Assurance Program Manager. Oversees operations of the Pittsburgh SDMC Quality Assurance Team; collaborating and supporting the audit activities of the broader quality assurance program. Participates in monthly and semi-annual cross-office quality assurance team meetings. Ensures all required audit reviews and reports are prepared and submitted timely and accurately in support of the overall goals of the audit program. Participates in external audits as required. Supports education and training of member institutions at semi-annual meetings as required. Job Summary Leads team and manages the administrative responsibilities of the Research Operations Department. Oversees logistical efforts and writes research grant proposals. Creates and ensures compliance with policies, procedures, and regulations. Formulates and monitors budgets, disperses expenses, and performs associated financial duties. Essential Functions Position requires coding, entering, verifying, and maintaining data as it relates to the external site visit audit program of the NRG Oncology. Incumbent will work with external sites to ensure adherence to data collection procedures. This requires maintaining files and communicating effectively. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. duties are primarily sedentary The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Assistant Director - Research Operations Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Operations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Monday - Friday Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $58,979.00 - $78,638.00 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003319": {
      "title": "Patient Experience Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Patient Experience Specialist (26003319) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Patient Experience Specialist (26003319) Job Description Patient Experience Specialist Dent Med-Clinical Affairs - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003319 ) Job Summary Provides administrative support services for patient care to include scheduling and confirming a large volume of appointments and surgeries via telephone, web, email, and in-person utilizing exceptional patient and customer service skills. Acts as liaison for patient records, maintains accurate databases and records, and ensures all forms and paperwork are completed and correct. Performs basic financial functions and guides students in administrative tasks. Essential Functions Responsible for optimizing student clinic schedules, confirming patient appointments, and supporting student compliance with care policies. Oversees patient assignments and recalls, approves clinical documentation, and supports students in administrative tasks to ensure productivity and efficiency.  Provides support to Team Leaders and Faculty, while performing additional duties as needed. Physical Effort This position is primarily sedentary but does require the ability to move around the School and Clinic areas. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Patient Office Assistant Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Clinic Operations Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $19.23 - $19.80 per hour Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
