    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004393": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Technician (26004393) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Technician (26004393) Job Description Research Technician Med-Structural Biology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004393 ) The Department of Structural Biology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine is located in Biomedical Science Tower 3. We currently have twelve faculty members working in the fields of cryo-electron microscopy, NMR spectroscopy, X-ray crystallography, and biochemistry. This laboratory technician position requires a B.S. degree in a relevant field of study. Job Summary Performs laboratory testing and some analysis on multiple types of specimen samples. Operates and properly sterilizes equipment and maintains inventory and assists with ordering. Essential Functions Conducting and managing laboratory experiments. Manage multiple research projects concurrently using techniques such as PCR, DNA cloning, sample preparation for electron microscopy, and cryo-EM data collection/analysis. Work together with PI or independently to perform complex laboratory work and technical analysis. Troubleshoot technical problems and find suitable experimental solutions or design new procedures to circumvent problems. Research concentrates on trafficking essential for cilia or flagella biogenesis using cryogenic electron tomography. By combining cell biology and structural biology, experiments aim to understand molecular and structural function cilia or flagella using Trypanosoma brucei, a single celled parasite cell, as a model organism and pave the way to treat various important ciliopathy diseases.  The successful candidate will work with other lab members to conduct cell culture, molecular and cellular biology (cloning, genetic manipulation of singe-cell system), immunofluorescence-labelling, and cryo-electron tomography. Organization of lab space, coordination with other lab members for ordering and stocks, and presentation of data at lab meetings are essential. The candidate will assist the PI with experimental design, implementation of novel strategies/procedures, and manuscript preparation for publication, including figures and writing. The applicant should be highly motivated, well-organized, detail-oriented, be able to prioritize multiple tasks, and will be encouraged to work independently. Strong interpersonal skills and judgment is essential. The successful applicant should have some experience in molecular biology including PCR, cloning, or SDS-PAGE, or fluorescent imaging, and cell culture. Experience in cryo-EM (electron microscopy, FIB milling) and proficient computer skills (Linux, python, scripting) are highly desired but not essential. Most of all we are looking for applicants that are motivated to learn novel technologies, take on new challenges, and to develop innovative techniques and methods. Physical Effort Ability to manipulate laboratory instruments and reagents to conduct experiments; ability to move about the lab environment. Will require standing or sitting at lab benches for long periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician I Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=25005964": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Dental Assistant (25005964) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Dental Assistant (25005964) Job Description Dental Assistant Dent Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 25005964 ) S ince 1896 the University of Pittsburgh School of Dental Medicine has been educating students to take their places among the best dental practitioners in our region and across the country. Each day the School’s faculty and staff contribute to its mission to advance the future of dental medicine through teaching, research and service. In addition to being a great place to work the University offers robust benefits including : *11 Paid Holidays, Paid Vacation, Sick and Personal Days * Additional Paid Time Off (Winter Recess) during the period between Christmas and the New Year * Paid Parental Leave * Education benefits for eligible employees, their dependents and spouse/domestic partner * Above-average Employer Contribution towards Medical, Prescription Drug, Vision, Life, STD, and LTD Insurance plans * A robust retirement savings plan option. Including 100% match on employee contributions of 3-8% (150% after vesting) and enhanced match for those nearing retirement * Free PAT bus pass. School of Dental Medicine Orthodontics Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery laboratory is seeking a dental assistant. Job Summary Performs chairside dental assisting and radiography in a dental clinic with patients who have received sedation and outpatient general anesthesia. Assists with oral surgery procedures; maintains oral surgery instruments, trays, and sterilization practices; sets up dental operatories. Instructs on and ensures students use proper infection controls and protocols. Schedules cases and procedures, maintains department records and charts, handles post-op emergencies, assists with student clinical evaluations and attendance records, and monitors and distributes narcotic and non-narcotic prescriptions. Maintains clinic and sterilization room; orders supplies. Essential Functions Must be able to provide assistance to faculty members, residents, and predoc students in the Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery/ University Dental Health Services (UDHS).  While providing support for surgical procedures and patient sedation, the assistant will be responsible for maintaining an aseptic environment, following OSHA and infection control guidelines, and following HIPPA guidelines as well as maintain and dispense inventory and instruments. Must be able to assess usage volume and of supplies in relation to inventory levels and notify when ordering is needed.  Must restock operatories daily.  Preparation of operatory and dental rooms for treatment is required throughout the day and at the end of the day for following morning procedures.  Cleaning clinic treatment rooms and operatories after each procedure. Escorting patients from waiting area to operatory and ensure patient chart is available for treatment is required. Escorting patient back to check out are once treatment is finished. Must demonstrate knowledge and skill in the support of surgical procedures for sedated patients.  Must be organized, responsive to the needs of faculty and residents, and highly attentive to patient needs. Physical Effort This is not a sedentary job position. This is a very mobile position. There is much movement throughout the day. Depending on the procedure, there may be long periods of sitting or standing. Required to carry biohazard trash to the proper waste disposal area in the school. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Dental Surgical Assistant Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Clinical Dental Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Graduate of Dental Technology Program Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Required Licensure/Certification Current PA dental radiology certificate. EFDA preferred. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Any of the following are also recommended:  NELDA, CDA, DAANCE.  CPR/BLS is required and will be provided as needed to be recertified. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004032": {
      "title": "Director of Strategic Initiatives",
      "description": "Job Description - Director of Strategic Initiatives (26004032) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Director of Strategic Initiatives (26004032) Job Description Director of Strategic Initiatives Student Affairs - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004032 ) The Director of Strategic Initiatives provides leadership for division-wide strategic planning, organizational effectiveness, and cross-functional project management within the Division of Student Affairs. Reporting to the Vice Provost of Student Affairs, this position partners closely with divisional leadership to advance strategic priorities, improve organizational performance, and strengthen operational alignment across more than twenty departments. The Director serves as the Division's central resource for coordinating strategic initiatives, facilitating planning processes, and supporting implementation of institutional priorities. Through collaboration with senior leadership, assessment professionals, communications staff, and campus partners, the position ensures strategic projects are effectively planned, executed, assessed, and communicated. Strategic Planning & Organizational Effectiveness •    Coordinate development, implementation, and ongoing assessment of the Division's Strategic Plan. •    Facilitate strategic planning meetings, retreats, and leadership work sessions. •    Develop implementation plans, timelines, performance measures, and accountability frameworks. •    Identify opportunities to improve organizational effectiveness, operational efficiency, and cross-departmental collaboration. Project & Initiative Management •    Lead complex, division-wide strategic initiatives involving multiple Student Affairs departments. •    Coordinate implementation of executive priorities and monitor project progress. •    Support organizational change initiatives through planning, communication, and stakeholder engagement. •    Develop project management tools, dashboards, and status reports. Assessment, Reporting & Executive Support •    Integrate assessment findings, institutional research, and operational data into strategic decision-making. •    Prepare executive reports, Board of Trustees materials, annual reports, presentations, and strategic communications. •    Monitor progress toward strategic goals using performance metrics and assessment data. •    Provide research, analysis, and strategic planning support to divisional leadership. Collaboration & Partnership Development •    Foster collaborative relationships across Student Affairs and University partners. •    Coordinate strategic initiatives requiring collaboration among multiple campus stakeholders. •    Represent the Division on assigned committees and strategic initiatives. •    Promote a culture of continuous improvement, innovation, and organizational learning. Job Summary Executes strategic alignment, long-term planning, operational planning, and management oversight of major college, campus, or University-wide student affairs functions. Establishes the direction, goals, implementation strategy, evaluation means, student initiatives, and policies of the department. Maintains responsibility for budgetary matters. Directs effective communications, promotions, and public relations for the department. Essential Functions Coordinates division-wide strategic planning initiatives and organizational effectiveness efforts. Manages implementation of strategic projects and monitors progress toward divisional priorities. Develops planning documents, executive reports, annual reports, presentations, and strategic communications. Facilitates strategic planning meetings, retreats, and cross-functional workgroups. Integrates assessment findings and institutional data into planning and decision-making processes. Identifies opportunities to improve organizational effectiveness and operational efficiency. Collaborates with campus partners to advance strategic priorities across the Division. Supports executive leadership through research, analysis, planning, and project coordination. Represents the Division on assigned committees and strategic initiatives. Performs additional duties as assigned. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Director - Student Affairs Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 7 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Master's degree in Higher Education, Public Administration, Business Administration, Organizational Leadership, Project Management, or a related field preferred. Minimum seven years of progressively responsible experience in strategic planning, project management, organizational effectiveness, assessment, or higher education administration. Combination of education and relevant experience may be considered in lieu of minimum requirements. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. occasional nights and weekends required. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered Yes Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003688": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Scientist (26003688) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Scientist (26003688) Job Description Research Scientist Med-Ophthalmology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003688 ) The Betegon Lab (https://betegonlab.org) at the University of Pittsburgh Ophthalmology Department is looking for a motivated Research Scientist to work on the development of novel AAV technologies that will enable safe and efficient gene therapies. The candidate must have a PhD in biophysics, biochemistry, biology, structural biology, or related field. Demonstrated and extensive experience with protein expression in bacterial or mammalian cells and FPLC protein purification is required for this position, as is experience with protein assays and basic molecular biology techniques including molecular cloning. Previous experience working with AAV is not required. Job Summary Conducts independent scientific research projects from inception to presentation. Prepares and crafts various documentations of research results into manuscripts, proposals, grant applications, and presentations. Trains undergraduates and research technicians. Manages laboratory policies and coordinates project development in collaboration with other specialists. Essential Functions Under the supervision of the PI, the researcher will lead the design, development and evaluation of  novel AAV technologies. Other tasks are to: present research findings at meetings,  contribute to the preparation of manuscripts and train students in the lab. Physical Effort The position may require some physical effort, for example, moving and lifting boxes containing laboratory supplies and equipment. The employee may also be required to sit and work at a laboratory bench or desk for extended periods of time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Research Scientist Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Research Science Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Professional Doctorate Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule M- F 8:30am to 5:00pm Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided Yes Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003697": {
      "title": "Customer Care Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Customer Care Specialist (26003697) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Customer Care Specialist (26003697) Job Description Customer Care Specialist Panther Central - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003697 ) The Office of Business, Hospitality and Auxiliary Services (BHAS) leads the University's foundational business services and is one of the many units under Finance and Operations . BHAS performs critical services to ensure our students, staff, faculty, and visitors have an exceptional experience on campus, including: All residence halls and University-owned leased apartments 36 dining locations across campus Hospitality services, including camps and conferences, the University Club, and Heinz Memorial Chapel University Logistics, including student and campus mail, surplus property, campus printing, and moving services Campus Mobility, including parking lots and garages, campus shuttles, and commuting opportunities Panther Central – the University’s one-stop shop for all campus needs including Pitt IDs Campus retail operations, including three on-campus stores - The University Store on Fifth, Maggie & Stella's Cards & Gifts, and The Pitt Shop We welcome you to BHAS, and invite you to explore our services, get to know our leadership team, and learn about our mission, vision, and values. For more information about BHAS, please visit our website at BHAS.pitt.edu or follow us on LinkedIn . Job Summary Serves as contact for internal and external customers and responds to routine inquiries and needs. Resolves moderately complex issues and refers customers to appropriate personnel. Maintains records, details comments and complaints, and performs administrative duties. Essential Functions * Serves as first point of contact for internal and external customers including guests, clients, faculty, staff, students, and vendors * Responds appropriately to and ensures resolution of routine customer questions, needs, and issues; assesses needs and suggests alternative products or services * Troubleshoots and handles moderately complex inquiries and issues * Refers customers to supervisors and/or other departments as needed * Maintains accurate record of customer interactions and transactions; details all comments and complaints; tracks and gathers information as needed * Files documents, provides data entry, and completes forms requiring standard information * Explains policies and procedures of housing, dining, parking, transportation, commuting, and Pitt IDs to students, parents, faculty, staff, and visitors * Other duties and special projects as assigned Panther Central is dedicated to being an available resource to the University community. Our Customer Care Specialists are required to work mandatory overtime during our busier seasons (i.e. Student Move-in) and provide holiday coverage as needed. Physical Effort Sitting, standing, walking, lifting (up to 35 pounds), carrying, reaching, pushing, and pulling. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Customer Service Representative II Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Customer Service Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Associate's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Wednesday - Sunday 12-8PM or Thursday – Monday 3-11PM Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $17.74/hour with overtime opportunities Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003585": {
      "title": "Psychiatrist",
      "description": "Job Description - Psychiatrist (26003585) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Psychiatrist (26003585) Job Description Psychiatrist Student Health Service - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003585 ) The University of Pittsburgh Student Health Services provides high quality primary health care, prevention, health education and pharmacy services to enhance student living and learning. Primary care services include management of both acute and chronic conditions as well as travel health and provision of gender affirming care. The Gynecological services include screening for STIs, provision of age specific screening as well as full contraceptive management.  Psychiatric services include management of mood disorders as well as ADHD. Student Health Services is accredited by the Accreditation Association for Ambulatory Health Care (AAAHC), these services uphold rigorous standards of quality and safety, promoting a healthy environment conducive to academic success. Job Summary Provides individual psychiatric assessments and evaluations of students/patients and diagnoses and prescribes appropriate treatments, psychotropic medications, and medication management. Prepares comprehensive records of evaluations and treatments and documents in an electronic database. Orders referral consultations and provides consultations with applicable University medical and therapeutic staff. Serves as consultant and mental health subject expert; publishes mental health findings and maintains educational standards of mental health educational programming for the University. Essential Functions • Provides individual psychiatric assessments and evaluations of students/patients, including evaluations, diagnosis, psychiatric treatments, prescribing psychotropic medications, and medication management. • Prepares comprehensive records, including patient evaluations and treatments. Documents and maintains patient care into electronic database in a timely, accurate manner. • Orders and/or refers medical consultations when appropriate. • Provides consultations with applicable University medical staff, clinicians, and therapists. • Acts as consultant and mental health subject matter expert to any agency or department within the University. • Researches mental health problems, publishes findings, and maintains educational standards of ongoing mental health educational programs for the University. • Attends University and staff-related meetings as directed. The job duties outlined in this job description include common job responsibilities for this title and level of jobs and are not intended to cover every duty. The University reserves the right to assign other duties to employees that are not listed in this job description. Physical Effort Moderate phys·cal effort required. May be required to stand/move for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Psychiatrist Job Family Health Professionals Job Sub-Family Behavioral & Mental Health Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Professional Doctorate Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Required Licensure/Certification Active Medical License Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30am - 5:00pm; may need to work occasional evening and weekend Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003393": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician IV-DeMazumder Lab",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV-DeMazumder Lab (26003393) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV-DeMazumder Lab (26003393) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician IV-DeMazumder Lab Med-MIRM-Dr Chandan Sen Group - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003393 ) Job Summary Performs a variety of independent and complex laboratory work and experiments. Analyzes and interprets data, compiles results, and prepares reports. Maintains inventory, ordering, and logs. Writes manuscripts and grant proposals and prepares data visualizations. Essential Functions Performs a variety of independent and complex laboratory work and experiments. Analyzes and interprets data, compiles results, and prepares reports. Maintains inventory, ordering, and logs. Writes manuscripts and grant proposals and prepares data visualizations. Physical Effort Mostly sedentary. May be required to lift up to 25 lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Laboratory Research Technician IV Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Laboratory Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range $43,894.50-$59,319 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003389": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician IV",
      "description": "Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV       (26003389) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Laboratory Research Technician IV       (26003389) Job Description Laboratory Research Technician IV Talent Acquisition - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003389 ) Job Summary Laboratory research technician iv The University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine seeks a Laboratory Research Technician IV to work in Pittsburgh, PA. Duties include designing/performing: (i) isolation, activation, and expansion of T cells (ii) cryopreservation, sub-culturing, and revival of various cell lines and primary cells; (iii) cell-based assays including cytotoxicity, cell viability, and  cell proliferation assays; (iv) immunofluorescence imaging using confocal microscopy and single-cell time-lapse imaging; (v) isolation and handling of PBMCs from human whole blood; (vi) multicolor flow cytometry, SDS-PAGE, western blot, multi-mode reader-based assays and various biochemical assays; and (vii) data analysis using Graphpad Prism, FlowJo, Excel and Image-J. Must have a master’s degree (or foreign equivalent degree) in Biology, Biotechnology, or a related field plus one (1) year of experience in a related position. Must have any experience working with: (i) Cryopreservation, sub-culturing and revival of various cell lines, mammalian cell lines and primary cells; (ii) In-vitro assays such as cytotoxicity, cell viability, cell proliferation; (iii) Live cell time-lapse imaging for cell viability assays, spheroids, immune cell killing, co-culture assays and image analysis; (iv) Isolation of and assays using Peripheral Blood Mononuclear Cells (PBMCs) from human blood; (v) isolation and expansion of naïve T cells, CD4 T cells, CD8 T cells, and regulatory T cells; (vi) Activation and expansion of T cells using Dynabeads and plate coated antigen; (vii) Screening of peptide pools, cytokine/chemokine profiling using LUMINEX, and direct, indirect, Quantikine, and sandwich ELISA assays; (viii) Seed, treat, fix, permeabilize, block and antibody staining/addition of cell lines and primary immune cells for multicolor flow cytometry of surface and intracellular markers using appropriate compensation and FMO controls for different multi-point in-vitro assays; (ix) Analysis of the flow cytometry data for receptor quantification and drug screening using Flow-Jo Software; (x) Preparing cells for molecular biology techniques such as SDS-PAGE, western Blot, protein/antibody quantification using Bradford/BCA assay and other multi-mode reader-based assays, bacterial transformation and cloning; and (xi) data analysis using Graphpad Prism and Excel. Image analysis using Image-J. Must be able to work weekends and holidays. Experience can be concurrent. Apply at https://www.join.pitt.edu , # 26003389 The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Must have a master’s degree (or foreign equivalent degree) in Biology, Biotechnology, or a related field plus one (1) year of experience in a related position. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 1 Hiring Range TBD Based on Qualifications Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26003022": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Assistant Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Financial Aid Assistant Director (26003022) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Financial Aid Assistant Director (26003022) Job Description Financial Aid Assistant Director Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26003022 ) The Admissions and Financial Aid Office is responsible for administering all financial aid and admission for the Doctor of Medicine degree. Information on how to apply to medical school, required courses, as well as admission and financial aid deadlines can be found on this site. Job Summary Directs the University's financial aid program to meet enrollment goals and establish best practices. Oversees the implementation and operational functionality of financial aid systems as well as data integrity, warehousing, and user training. Coordinates the budgeting and fiscal management of a variety of programs and all financial aid reporting, awarding, and disbursing activities. Develops financial aid policies and procedures. Essential Functions The Financial Aid Assistant Director oversees and provides financial aid services in the School of Medicine. Duties include development, implementation, and maintenance of departmental policies and procedures so the department is able to provide as many opportunities and resources as possible for medical student financial support; coordinate financial aid counseling services, and coordinate liaison relationship of department with related University personnel, and external agencies. Financial aid administration is under the direction of the Assistant Dean. Oversee the financial aid operations for the School of Medicine, Office of Admissions and Financial Aid; interpret federal, state, and private aid regulations and implement and maintain policies and procedures in compliance with these regulations; stay abreast of all funding opportunities for medical students; Primary processor of federal, state, University grant and institutional and federal loans; Coordinate the creation and implementation of the strategic plan for the need-based funding for the SOM; manage the coordination of the financial aid student complaint/appeal procedure for the School of Medicine in collaboration with the Executive Director; oversee the development and implementation School of Medicine interface with University financial aid data systems; supervise the system for collection and maintenance of all financial aid application materials and information; develop and implement tracking procedures needed for various aid programs; prepare projections of student needs, funding available, and student eligibility; administer institutional aid programs as directed; oversee all federal, state, and private loan and scholarship application processing; ensure that financial aid services attain greatest effectiveness, efficiency, and maintain hospitable student services environment; train financial aid staff; assist assistant and associate deans as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned Physical Effort The essential functions of the position are communications, and the incumbent must be able to use the telephone and computer. Normal business office, generally sedentary activities. Must also have the ability to stand for long periods of time and have the ability to travel. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Financial Aid Assistant Director Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Student Financial Services Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 5 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. *a hybrid work arrangement is available after successful completion of provisional period: 3 days onsite and 2 days remote **Must be within commuting distance of the university to be considered Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26001086": {
      "title": "Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Pre & Post Award)",
      "description": "Job Description - Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Pre & Post Award) (26001086) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Pre & Post Award) (26001086) Job Description Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Pre & Post Award) Med-Emergency Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26001086 ) The University of Pittsburgh Department of Emergency Medicine is seeking a Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Pre & Post Award) employee who will: Perform pre and post award accounting duties for complex grants and contracts not limited to overseeing the processing of invoices, conducting complex cost analyses, re-budgeting projects, setting up sub-awards, and coordinating supply and equipment purchases. Prepares, negotiates, and monitors grants, contracts, and budgets, processes amendments, modifications, extensions, and terminations of contracts. Maintains award-related schedules; ensures complete and accurate collection and distribution of all materials. Monitors account activity including expenditures, cost transfers, adjustments, reconciliations, and other related transactions. Ensures accuracy and adherence to budgets, sponsor terms, federal regulations, policies, and procedures; provides policy and procedure interpretation. Prepares account reports; analyzes financial documentation and reviews routine reports. Tracks multiple grants and contracts to advise University employees on long-term financial viability. Assists with preparing project budgets. Job Summary Performs pre- and post-award accounting duties for complex grants and contracts. Prepares, negotiates, and monitors grants, contracts, and budgets. Maintains award-related schedules, prepares complex government applications and reports, and interprets policy and procedure. Monitors account activity, performs internal audits, resolves complex issues, and reviews routine financial documents. Develops and implements accounting techniques and procedures for operational improvements and assists with managing special projects and preparing operating budgets. Essential Functions Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.), Grants Forecasting, Fiscal Panther, Peris, and pertinent grant programs.  Excellent communications skills via phone, email and virtual platforms (Teams, Zoom, etc.) is imperative.  Ability to sit for long periods of time and attend meetings in various campus buildings when required. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time and lift small packages under 10 lbs. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Grants & Contracts Specialist III (Pre & Post-Award) Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Grants & Contracts Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006152": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Description - Office Coordinator (26006152) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Office Coordinator (26006152) Job Description Office Coordinator Student Affairs - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006152 ) The Division of Student Affairs is seeking an Office Manager. This position assists in the coordination of activities and provides customer service for the Office of the Vice Provost and Dean of Students office. The incumbent will be responsible for: Greeting and directing visitors. Providing excellent customer service both in person and over the telephone. Assisting the Office of the Dean with correspondence and communications. Assisting in maintaining the appointment calendars for office staff. Distributing voicemail messages received on the main telephone number. Assisting in answering/distributing email messages to the departmental email account. General office, administrative, and clerical responsibilities. Coordinating data management. Assisting with student staff supervision. Providing support to Senior Executive Assistant to the Vice Provost and the Executive Assistant to the Dean of Students, as well as administrative support for Associate Deans and broader Division of Student Affairs activities. Other duties as assigned. High school diploma or GED and one to two years of relevant experience required. Equivalent combination of education and experience may be substituted for the education/experience requirement per university guidelines. Customer service experience required. Some experience in an office setting preferred; proficiency in basic word processing and ability to quickly learn general computer software applications. Ability to remain helpful and friendly in a fast-paced environment. Job Summary Greets visitors and directs them to appropriate offices and meeting rooms. Answers telephone and inquiries, takes messages, and transfers and refers callers. Manages calendars, operates standard office equipment, and performs a variety of clerical work. Essential Functions Greets and checks in customers, clients, and other visitors; directs visitors to appropriate destination and/or employee. Answers telephone, takes messages, and transfers callers; provides general information and appropriately answers customer inquiries from walk-ins, incoming calls, and emails. Schedules appointments and manages calendars. Operates standard office equipment including a telephone, copy machine, fax machine, and computer on a regular basis. Performs a variety of clerical duties, including filing paperwork, distributing mail, preparing routine reports, and data entry. Physical Effort Little physical effort required. Duties are primarily sedentary. May be required to move objects up to 25 pounds occasionally. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Receptionist Job Family Administrative Support Job Sub-Family Clerical Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required No experience required Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006071": {
      "title": "Media Producer",
      "description": "Job Description - Media Producer (26006071) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Media Producer (26006071) Job Description Media Producer University Center for Teaching and Learning - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006071 ) The University of Pittsburgh Center for Teaching and Learning is seeking a qualified media producer to support the Academic Media team creation of video and multimedia content for a variety of uses. This on-campus position is ideal for a professional with extensive videography experience including field and studio production as well as footage/media management. Bachelor’s degree in film, media production, communications or related field and/or relevant professional experience. Experience and proficiency with Sony cameras (FX6 or similar), lighting and audio techniques, and inventory management is required. Producing or post-production skills and knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite is highly desirable. Work outside of regular business hours will be required occasionally. Please note: candidates will be required to provide a videography portfolio. Candidates may include a link to an online portfolio in their resume or they may include this as a \"media sample\" attachment along with their application. Job Summary Records and edits studio sessions and webinars, shoots and edits photographs, and creates media announcements on information monitors and University bulletin boards. Maintains and troubleshoots audiovisual (AV) equipment, instructs on proper usage, and facilitates AV skill development workshops. Coordinates acquisition requests and updates AV supply inventory. Essential Functions Essential Functions Capture video in studio and on-location settings, and work with a team to complete video and media production projects. •     Operate camera, audio, and lighting equipment, proficiency with Sony cameras (FX6 or similar) •    Manage two studio spaces and video production equipment. •     Organize, log, and archive media files following team file-management standards. •     Coordinate with faculty, staff, and student collaborators on routine production logistics. •     Use team-approved AI tools to support production workflow tasks. Other production duties, including producing and editing, as needed. Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for prolonged periods of time. May need to lift equipment, mail, or supplies up to 50 pounds. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Multimedia Coordinator Job Family Communications & Marketing Job Sub-Family Multimedia Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required High School Diploma/GED Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? No Work Schedule Varied, may require some evenings and weekends Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range To be determined based on qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Media Sample Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006168": {
      "title": "Learning and Development Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Learning and Development Specialist (26006168) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Learning and Development Specialist (26006168) Job Description Learning and Development Specialist Organization Development - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006168 ) Organization Development (OD) is a department within the Office of Human Resources that serves as a strategic partner with University community clients to help them create and realize their strategic plans, and achieve greater levels of effectiveness and productivity in their organization. The OD consulting team provides comprehensive consultation along with customized products, services, and results-based solutions to assist University colleges, schools and departments to achieve success. This position combines instructional design and learning facilitation. The successful candidate is equally excited by designing engaging learning experiences as they are confidently delivering them. Core Competencies Exceptional facilitation skills with the ability to create engaging, learner-centered experiences that encourage participation, discussion, and knowledge application across in-person, virtual, and hybrid environments Ability to translate complex or technical information into accessible, engaging content Strong project management and organizational skills; ability to manage multiple concurrent training initiatives Collaborative self-starter—ability to work well in a small team environment while also managing workload autonomously Adaptability—able to pivot between topics, audiences, delivery modes (virtual vs. in-person) Strong customer service orientation and a collaborative, consultative approach with departments and leadership Cultural competence and ability to design inclusive training for a diverse university community Job Summary Designs and delivers organizational development programs and initiatives, including learning and professional development programming and technology-enabled platforms, for assigned schools or departments. Analyzes workforce and organizational needs, recommends strategies to improve efficiency and productivity, supports change management processes, and delivers training and development opportunities for faculty and staff. Essential Functions Deliver Organization Development (OD) workshops as appropriate in topics such as Customer Service, Performance Management, and Supervisor Skills. Deliver weekly Faculty Staff and Development (FSDP) workshops related to professional and personal skill development. Recognize and accommodate various learning styles while creating energizing learning experiences that meet the needs of the targeted audience. This will include consideration of a wide range of age groups, work experience levels, and learners at different career stages. Work with subject matter experts and other stakeholders to proactively identify and analyze workforce learning and development needs. Determine and state learning objectives and create content that matches the objectives for both online and classroom environments, depending on need. Update existing programming content to meet specific client needs and reflect current trends. Create or assist in the creation of supporting material/media (audio, video, simulations, role plays, games, etc.) Ability to develop and measure learning outcomes. Also, decide on the criteria used to judge learners’ performance and develop assessment instruments. Maintain project documentation. Cultivate and maintain relationships with stakeholders (subject matter experts, technical professionals, communication professionals, faculty, etc.) Preferred Experience Experience in a higher education, nonprofit, or large complex organizational setting Experience training on a variety of workplace topics, such as professional communication, time management, difficult conversations, supervisor skills, performance management, etc. Experience designing learning experiences grounded in adult learning theory and instructional design best practices that align with organizational goals Experience partnering with subject matter experts (SMEs) to build content Experience working with a diverse population of staff and faculty stakeholders Preferred Technical Skills Proficiency with Learning Management Systems (LMS) Proficiency with virtual facilitation platforms (e.g,  Zoom, Microsoft Teams) Experience with e-learning design tools (e.g., Articulate 360 (Storyline/Rise) Familiarity with learning design models (e.g., ADDIE, Bloom's Taxonomy) Facility with Microsoft Office/PowerPoint for content creation Basic data/reporting skills to track training metrics, completion rates, and evaluation feedback Physical Effort Ability to travel between campus locations or other locations in the Pittsburgh area, when applicable, for in-person sessions. Moderate physical effort required. May be required to stand/move for several hours at a time. May be required to move objects up to 50 pounds with or without assistance of equipment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Organizational Development Specialist II Job Family Human Resources Job Sub-Family Organization Development Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Bachelor’s degree in Education, Human Resources, Business, or related field ; Master's degree preferred. Relevant certifications (e.g., instructional design, teaching, facilitation, DDI, ATD, CPTD, or related professional credentials) preferred. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Hybrid: Combination of On-Campus and Remote work as determined by the department. Hiring Range $55,000-$60,000 Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26002263": {
      "title": "Online Instructional Designer, Law",
      "description": "Job Description - Online Instructional Designer, Law (26002263) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Online Instructional Designer, Law (26002263) Job Description Online Instructional Designer, Law Office of the SVC and Provost - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26002263 ) Pitt EDGE is the University of Pittsburgh’s central hub for digital education, housed within the Office of the Provost. This inaugural Center advances the University’s strategic vision for online, hybrid, and continuing education by partnering with Pitt’s 16 schools to expand access and improve quality for diverse learners. Pitt EDGE supports the full lifecycle of digital learning through services such as instructional design, technology integration, market analysis, academic planning, recruitment, and quality assurance. This position's primary client will be the University of Pittsburgh's School of Law Master's degree in instructional design or related field, and 3-5 years of relevant professional experience. Experience and proficiency designing courses in Canvas and Articulate 360 is required. Previous experience designing legal or paralegal courses is highly desirable. Please note: candidates will be required to provide a portfolio. Candidates may include a link to an online portfolio in their resume, or they may include this as a \"media sample\" attachment along with their application Job Summary Consult with educators on the design, development, and delivery of moderately complex instructional materials and the integration of instructional technologies. Essential Functions • Consults individually with faculty and subject matter experts on the design and development of instructional content and the integration of instructional technologies for new online and hybrid courses/programs. • Conducts needs assessments for online and hybrid course design. • Develops or transitions curricula for new online or hybrid programs utilizing appropriate instructional technologies, authoring tools, and features of the learning management system (LMS). • Builds and reviews online and hybrid courses within the LMS. • Designs, develops, and edits text-based and multimedia content for online and hybrid courses. • Recommends teaching methods for online and hybrid learning modalities and implements pedagogical improvements for online and hybrid courses. • Conducts training programs related to online and hybrid pedagogy or technology. Conducts quality assurance and digital accessibility reviews on instructional content for online and hybrid courses. OTHER SKILLS Experience with graphic design and Artificial Intelligence is a plus. Physical Effort Must be able to sit for prolonged periods of time and work with computing technology. This position involves extensive screen time. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Online Instructional Designer II Job Family Academic & Student Services Job Sub-Family Instructional and Classroom Support Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Master's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 3 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Work Schedule Monday- Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Work Arrangement Remote: Teams working from different locations (off-campus). Hiring Range TBD Based Upon Qualifications Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances Not Applicable Required Documents Resume, Cover Letter, Media Sample Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_staff_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005930": {
      "title": "Animal Care and Operations Supervisor",
      "description": "Job Description - Animal Care and Operations Supervisor (26005930) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Animal Care and Operations Supervisor (26005930) Job Description Animal Care and Operations Supervisor DLAR-Animal Husbandry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005930 ) The Division of Laboratory Animal Resources (DLAR) Animal Care and Operations Supervisor will be responsible for managing daily operations and staff involved with the provision of animal husbandry and care. The candidate will: • Supervise personnel including assessing and recruiting for labor needs, creating work assignments, managing employee performance and training serving as a mentor, and facilitating professional development; • Manage facility and equipment operations including assessing supply and capital needs, preventive maintenance schedules, facility projects, space demands and vendor coordination; • Provide support and services to researchers and their teams to ensure study perimeters are met; • Establish and maintain collaborative, productive working relationships with immediate staff, as well as, various DLAR (vet services, administration) and University (IACUC, EHS) departments • Promote animal welfare and well-being; • Ensure that the daily operations and activities of the assigned animal facility are accomplished in accordance with DLAR guidelines and Standard Operating Procedures, University policies, federal regulations, and industry standards and guidelines. A successful candidate must have two years of lab animal experience with one year in a supervisory capacity; consistently demonstrate professional verbal, written, and interpersonal skills; execute effective time and process management; possess positive customer service and team-building skills; be proficient with technology in order to use common applications (e.g. email, Microsoft Office, Zoom) and to learn CAMS (DLAR business application software); be available to work occasional weekends and holidays; stand for extended periods of time; lift 50 pounds; push/pull heavy equipment and pass the mandatory criminal and social background checks. Preferred candidate will have completed criteria in the DLAR Career Development Program. Candidates working in the Rangos Research Building at Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh will need to obtain Child Protection Clearances. Vaccinations and/or TB testing may be required. Job Summary Supervises team and manages day-to-day animal care operations. Ensures proper functioning and maintenance of equipment. Directs the enrichment and social animal housing programs at assigned facility. Maintains records, oversees billing, and ensures compliance with processes, practices, and regulations. Essential Functions The employee must be able to: • read, understand, and follow DLAR and other institutional guidance documents (SOPs, policies), including IACUC approved animal protocols when applicable • follow written and verbal instructions • demonstrate sufficient fine motor skill to manipulate animals and equipment; negotiate around equipment within close quarters; move between rooms and workspaces • have sufficient visual acuity to recognize and identify normal and abnormal species-specific clinical appearances and behavior patterns, safely handle and restrain the animal species, and operate and maintain facility equipment and supplies utilized in the provision of animal husbandry and care and in the cash wash areas • have sufficient audible acuity to hear equipment alarms and other warnings • wear facility specific Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) required by the job duties based on risk assessment from EH&S • work directly with live or dead animals and clean or soiled bedding and caging with reasonable accommodations if necessary • accurately and legibly document written information in English in a timely manner, including electronic formats and applications (e.g., PRISM, CAMS); • effective written and verbal communication in English, including the use of email • receive vaccinations and health assessments, including TB testing, required to work in some animal holding or procedure areas in accordance with DLAR and/or EH&S policies and practices • successfully enroll in University of Pittsburgh Animal Exposure Surveillance Program (AESP) and other medical surveillance/immunization programs as dictated by current research activities Physical Effort The employee must be able to: • stand for extended periods of time throughout the majority of the workday. • lift and move objects weighing up to 50 pounds including but not limited to caging and equipment, bags or boxes of animal diet and animal bedding, and operate flatbed hand trucks or pallet jacks to move heavier objects or weights exceeding 50 pounds. • perform repetitive motion tasks that involve pushing, pulling, reaching, and/or bending. • physically handle and restrain a variety of small and large laboratory animals. • negotiate and navigate around animal facility caging, equipment, and the physical plant. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category Full-time regular Job Classification Staff.Supervisor - Animal Care Job Family Research Job Sub-Family Animal Research Campus Pittsburgh Minimum Education Level Required Bachelor's Degree Minimum Years of Experience Required 2 Will this position accept substitution in lieu of education or experience? Combination of education and relevant experience will be considered in lieu of education and/ or experience requirement. Additional details about Required Licensure/Certification Certification by the American Association for Laboratory Animal Science (AALAS) at the Laboratory Animal Technician (LAT) level.  External candidate must achieve within 12 months of start date. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.; some weekends and holidays Work Arrangement On-Campus: Teams that work on campus, in an office, or in a lab. Hiring Range Commensurate with experience. Relocation Offered No Visa Sponsorship Provided No Background Check For position finalists, employment with the University will require successful completion of a background check Child Protection Clearances The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Not Applicable Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    }
  },
